R-24 None \n Personal timetable page /timetable for TEACHER (own courses incl. co-teaching), STUDENT (ACTIVE enrollments) and PARENT. It uses the same grid read-only and highlights the current period when today is a teaching day. \n AC: null\n### FR-25 None \n A PARENT with more than one linked child sees a child selector on /timetable, and switching it changes the grid. \n AC: null\n### FR-26 None \n A 'Week' / 'Today' toggle. The Today view is a vertical list of today's periods with course, teacher and room, plus 'Now' (in progress) and 'Next' badges. \n AC: null\n### FR-27 None \n Register a 'Timetable' student tab in src/config/student-tabs.ts that reuses the read-only grid for that student. \n AC: null\n### FR-28 None \n Add a course 'Schedule' tab (registered in the existing src/config/course-tabs.ts) that lists the course's weekly meeting times (day, period, times, room). \n AC: null\n### FR-29 None \n A 'Print' button on any grid view gives a print-friendly layout (@media print, A4 landscape, no sidebar). The printed page contains only the grid, the entity name and the academic year. \n AC: null\n### FR-30 None \n Export getScheduleForDate(userOrSection, date), which returns an ordered list of { period, course, room } for that date and returns empty on non-teaching days. Holidays are deferred to PRD-14. \n AC: null\n### FR-31 None \n Export getCurrentSlot(user, now), which returns the slot in progress (period start ≤ now < end in the school timezone) or null. \n AC: null\n### FR-32 None \n Navigation: add 'Timetable' (/timetable) for TEACHER, STUDENT and PARENT. Add 'Timetable editor' (/admin/timetable) and 'Bell schedule' (/admin/timetable/periods) for ADMIN in the Administration group. \n AC: null\n### FR-33 None \n Periods API: GET /api/periods (any role, ordered). POST /api/periods, PATCH and DELETE /api/periods/:id, and POST /api/periods/reorder { periodIds } are ADMIN only. \n AC: null\n### FR-34 None \n School days API: GET /api/school-days (any role) and PUT /api/school-days (ADMIN). \n AC: null\n### FR-35 None \n GET /api/timetable?view=section|teacher|room&id=&academicYearId= returns slots with course, teacher and room. ADMIN may use any view. TEACHER may use only their own teacher view and sections they are homeroom teacher of; anything else is 403. \n AC: null\n### FR-36 None \n GET /api/timetable/availability?courseId= (ADMIN) returns { '<day>-<periodId>': [clash messages] } for that course's academic year. \n AC: null\n### FR-37 None \n Slots API (ADMIN): POST /api/timetable/slots { courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId, roomId? }, PATCH /api/timetable/slots/:id and DELETE /api/timetable/slots/:id. A clash returns 409 CONFLICT with details.clashes[] and saves nothing. academicYearId is derived from the course server-side. \n AC: null\n### FR-38 None \n GET /api/me/timetable?studentId= (any role) returns the caller's own timetable. studentId is required for a PARENT with multiple children and must be a linked child; otherwise 403. \n AC: null\n### FR-39 None \n Zod schemas for periods, school days, slots and timetable queries live in src/lib/validators/timetable.ts, shared by the forms and the handlers. \n AC: null\n### FR-40 None \n Write AuditLog rows via audit() for slot create/move/delete, period create/update/delete/reorder, and teaching-day changes (including the cascade-deleted slot count). \n AC: null\n### FR-41 None \n Seed the periods: Period 1 08:00–08:45, Period 2 08:50–09:35, Break 09:35–09:55 (BREAK), Period 3 09:55–10:40, Period 4 10:45–11:30, Lunch 11:30–12:15 (LUNCH), Period 5 12:15–13:00, Period 6 13:05–13:50. The seed is idempotent. \n AC: null\n### FR-42 None \n Seed SchoolDay rows 1–7 with Monday–Friday teaching and Saturday–Sunday non-teaching. \n AC: null\n### FR-43 None \n Seed a complete clash-free week for 7A and 7B: MATH 5, ENG 5, SCI 4, HIST 3, PE 2 and ART 2 (21 of 30 class slots each), plus Robotics Club on Wednesday Period 6 with 7A and 7B free then. \n AC: null\n### FR-44 None \n Seed the minimal prerequisite fixtures the timetable seed and acceptance criteria rely on: teacher Tom (teaches MATH-7A and MATH-7B), student Sam (7A, enrolled in Robotics Club and ART-7A), parent Pat linked to two children, sections 7A/7B with homeroom rooms, their courses, and the Robotics Club elective (sectionId null). Reuse the existing ELA/SOC subjects for ENG/HIST. \n AC: null\n### FR-45 None \n All 'now' calculations (current period highlight, Now/Next badges, getCurrentSlot, today's day-of-week) use SchoolSettings.timezone, not the server or browser timezone. \n AC: null\n### NFR-1 None \n Integrity: clash validation and the slot insert/update run in one SERIALIZABLE Prisma transaction (retry on serialization failure), so two concurrent conflicting inserts yield exactly one success. \n AC: null\n### NFR-2 None \n Performance: the editor loads a section week (up to 7 days × 12 periods) in under 400 ms. \n AC: null\n### NFR-3 None \n Performance: the availability map for one course returns in under 300 ms. \n AC: null\n### NFR-4 None \n Accessibility: drag-and-drop has a keyboard alternative (FR-22), and colour is never the only signal (clashing cells also show an icon and a tooltip; 'Now'/'Next' are text badges). \n AC: null\n### NFR-5 None \n UI component rule: every visible element is built from @mui/material, @mui/icons-material or the listed MUI X packages, and every component is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before use. If mui-mcp is unreachable, that is a blocker; never guess props. \n AC: null\n### NFR-6 None \n No banned UI/styling libraries (Tailwind, shadcn, Radix, FullCalendar, react-datepicker, notistack, etc.; enforced by ESLint no-restricted-imports). The only new dependency allowed is the non-visual @dnd-kit/core (pinned), plus @dnd-kit/sortable only if needed. \n AC: null\n### NFR-7 None \n Security: every handler and server page enforces role and per-entity access server-side via requireUser/requireRole and the existing access helpers. Hiding UI is never the only protection. \n AC: null\n### NFR-8 None \n API conventions: thin handlers (Zod → service → JSON), the { data } / { error: { code, message, details } } shape, and the standard error codes (409 CONFLICT for clashes and for period delete-with-slots). \n AC: null\n### NFR-9 None \n Brownfield reuse: never re-scaffold. Reuse the existing helpers (http.ts, audit(), useToast, ConfirmDialog, PageHeader, the access helpers). New service at src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts. Do not rename existing routes or models. \n AC: null\n### NFR-10 None \n Quality gate: npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test all keep passing with TypeScript strict. \n AC: null\n### NFR-11 None \n Unit tests: every clash rule (including co-teacher and student overlap), the non-class period/day rule, period overlap validation, and current/next slot calculation across timezones. \n AC: null\n### NFR-12 None \n Integration test: concurrent conflicting slot inserts, where only one succeeds. \n AC: null\n### NFR-13 None \n Playwright e2e: drag a course into a cell, see a clash error snackbar on a conflicting drop, and the student Today view. \n AC: null\n### NFR-14 None \n No console.log in committed code; use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts. \n AC: null\n### NFR-15 None \n Scope guard: no automatic timetable solver, no A/B multi-week cycles, no substitute-teacher management, and no holiday handling (PRD-14). A single repeating week only. \n AC: null\n### NFR-16 None \n English-only UI, single school, and support for the last 2 versions of Chrome, Edge, Firefox and Safari (including print output). \n AC: null","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XKv4CQHJ4tmyp5x2aPP2a2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
