eing moved is not compared against itself.\n- **Period delete:** deleting a period that still has slots is refused with the slot count.\n- **Teaching days:** switching a day off deletes its slots.\n- **Audit rows:** slot create, move and delete, and teaching-day changes.\n- **Time:** the today's-schedule and current-period functions use the school's timezone.\n- **Access:** who may view which timetable.\n\nIt skips unless `TEST_DATABASE_URL` is set.\n\n**Minor deviations in the built backend:**\n- A parent with several children who leaves out `studentId` gets a 400 error rather than the 403 the spec asks for.\n- A teacher can view the timetable of any section they teach in, not only their homeroom section. This follows the design decision D8.\n\nThere's no coverage tool installed, and I didn't add one, so `coverage-report.md` maps coverage by hand. It estimates about 75% of the service functions are tested. The API route files have no automated tests because next-auth won't load under the test runner.\n\nMy recommendation is to send SH-6 back to Dev for TASK-9–16. They should also write a real SH-6 dev log and completion markers.\n\nFiles are in `artifacts/qa/`:\n- `qa-report.md`\n- `coverage-report.md`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5174,"cache_read_input_tokens":91605,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5174},"output_tokens":713,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b6711741-6c85-44a1-926e-b6198252edd5","uuid":"38213426-b911-4f58-aa0e-dcecc3017763","timestamp":"2026-11-05T05:34:36.884Z","request_id":"req_011CgjEhPtnWGSaK1vw78Ddz"}
