eviations in the built backend:**\n- A parent with several children who leaves out `studentId` gets a 400 error rather than the 403 the spec asks for.\n- A teacher can view the timetable of any section they teach in, not only their homeroom section. This follows the design decision D8.\n\nThere's no coverage tool installed, and I didn't add one, so `coverage-report.md` maps coverage by hand. It estimates about 75% of the service functions are tested. The API route files have no automated tests because next-auth won't load under the test runner.\n\nMy recommendation is to send SH-6 back to Dev for TASK-9–16. They should also write a real SH-6 dev log and completion markers.\n\nFiles are in `artifacts/qa/`:\n- `qa-report.md`\n- `coverage-report.md`","ttft_ms":2397,"type":"result","duration_ms":260992,"uuid":"6c2844d5-ecac-4a39-b3be-9a3cf304ee63","ttft_stream_ms":1816,"time_to_request_ms":100,"first_content_frame_ms":1817,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":36,"outputTokens":25779,"cacheReadInputTokens":1059194,"cacheCreationInputTokens":86824,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.4221548,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":4470,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":86824,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
