{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FbfsyVq154wHXTBeR9nxze","type":"tool_result","content":"total 32\ndrwxr-xr-x   4 ikramaansari  staff    128 Nov  5 10:34 .\ndrwxr-xr-x  11 ikramaansari  staff    352 Nov  5 11:37 ..\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff   3790 Nov  5 10:33 coverage-report.md\n-rw-r--r--   1 ikramaansari  staff  10899 Nov  5 10:34 qa-report.md\n# QA Report — SH-6 (PRD-06 Bell Schedule & Timetable)\n\n## QA Summary\n\n- ticketId: SH-6\n- timestamp: 2026-11-05T10:36:00Z\n- overallStatus: FAIL\n- requirementsChecked: 61\n- requirementsPassed: 34\n- requirementsFailed: 27 (1 FAIL + 26 NOT-IMPLEMENTED)\n\n## Headline findings\n\n1. **Dev stopped after TASK-8. The whole UI and the seed are missing.**\n   - Not built: TASK-9 to TASK-16, which cover the grid, the bell schedule page, the timetable editor, the personal, student and course timetable views, navigation, the seed, and the e2e test.\n   - None of the 25 planned CREATE files for those tasks exist.\n   - The planned edits to `student-tabs.ts`, `course-tabs.ts`, `navigation.ts`, `shell.tsx` and `seed.ts` were not made.\n   - `@dnd-kit/core` was added to `package.json` but is never imported.\n2. **The Dev artifacts are stale and do not describe this ticket.**\n   - `artifacts/dev/dev-log.md` and `task-completion-markers.json` are SH-4 (Notifications) files dated 2026-11-04. Their \"TASK-1..21 complete\" claims refer to PRD-04.\n   - No SH-6 dev log exists, but `dev-rerun-count.json` says `firstPassAccepted: true`. The pipeline accepted a Dev phase that never wrote its own outputs.\n3. **The backend that does exist is solid.**\n   - Covers TASK-1 to TASK-8: schema, migration, validators, clash engine, service, and 10 API routes.\n   - Contains real logic, with no stubs, TODO markers or console.log calls.\n   - Typecheck and lint pass.\n   - Passes 21 Dev unit tests and 16 new QA integration tests against real Postgres, including the NFR-1 concurrency guarantee.\n4. **The build is healthy, with no regressions.**\n   - `npm run typecheck` and `npm run lint` are both clean.\n   - `vitest run` shows 3 failing files. They are the same 3 failures recorded before this ticket (`DataTable` MUI X exports, `lockout` next-auth import, `useToast` timer), and none of them touch SH-6 code.\n\n## Requirement Results\n\n| Requirement | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | PASS | prisma/schema.prisma (`enum PeriodKind`, `model Period`); migration 20261105000000_timetable; used by tests/integration/timetable-concurrency.test.ts |\n| FR-2 | PASS | `model SchoolDay` + migration; integration \"FR-7/FR-40\" test upserts and reads it |\n| FR-3 | PASS | `model TimetableSlot` with `@@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` and `@@index([academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` in migration.sql; course FK `ON DELETE CASCADE` |\n| FR-4 | PASS | One additive migration with no ALTERs to existing tables except new FKs; back-relations on Course, Period and Room (schema lines 219/280/418/459); `prisma migrate status` reports it as up to date |\n| FR-5 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | `src/app/(app)/admin/timetable/periods/page.tsx` and `BellScheduleEditor.tsx` are missing. Only the API exists. |\n| FR-6 | PASS | src/lib/validators/timetable.ts (`hhmm`, `periodSchema`); service `assertNoOverlap`; tests/unit/timetable-time.test.ts (periodsOverlap, periodSchema) |\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-1\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-05T16:26:09Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"intake\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"prd\": \"PRD-01: Authentication, Sessions & Role-Based Access Control (SCH-001)\",\n  \"runMode\": \"--brownfield --tech-stack react\",\n  \"brownfieldFindings\": [\n    \"Ticket id: the task prompt says SH-1 and the PRD header says SCH-001. All artifacts use SH-1.\",\n    \"Re-run of intake on 2026-11-05. The workspace was re-checked, and some gaps reported by the earlier SH-1 intake have since been closed.\",\n    \"ALREADY IMPLEMENTED (do not rebuild): the Role/UserStatus/AuthTokenType enums and the User/AuthToken/AuditLog models; src/server/auth/tokens.ts; credentials.ts (authorize, DUMMY_HASH, lockout); auth.ts/auth.config.ts (JWT 8h, 5-min passwordChangedAt recheck, signOut export); src/middleware.ts + src/config/public-routes.ts; src/server/rate-limit.ts; src/server/audit.ts; src/lib/validators/auth.ts (policy, safeCallbackUrl, signInSchema); common-passwords.txt; services/auth.ts; services/users.ts (createUser, createInviteToken, real sendInvite → sendAuthEmail); every API route in the Pages & Routes table.\",\n    \"requireRole.ts already has no PLACEHOLDER_USER. It exports getCurrentUser (React cache), requireUser, requireRole, requirePageUser and requirePageRole on the real Auth.js session. FR-9 of the PRD is satisfied.\",\n    \"NOW PRESENT (closed since the earlier intake): the /login page (src/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx + LoginForm.tsx, with RHF+zod, an aria-live error Alert, a show-password toggle via passwordInputSlot, the rate-limit message, safeCallbackUrl and a forgot-password link); seed users (six ACTIVE users plus invited@schoolhub.test, whose invite link is logged via logger.info); migration 20261106000000_user_role_status_index (@@index([role, status])).\",\n    \"REUSABLE UI that already exists: TextFormField (src/components/FormField/FormField), PasswordChecklist + passwordInputSlot (src/components/PasswordChecklist), useToast (src/components/Toast/useToast). New auth pages must reuse these and must not duplicate them.\",\n    \"MISSING: the pages /forgot-password, /reset-password/[token] and /invite/[token] under src/app/(auth)/; the /account/security page (only /account/notifications exists).\",\n    \"MISSING: src/app/(app)/shell.tsx still defines PLACEHOLDER_USER (lines 40, 78, 162-167). No UI calls signOut(), and the user menu has no 'Account security' item.\",\n    \"MISSING TESTS: the unit tests exist (tokens, lockout, rate-limit, password-policy, auth-validators, login-error-message). No integration tests exist for the authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password or change-password (tests/integration has only email-dispatch and timetable). No Playwright auth specs exist (tests/e2e has only dashboard, landing and notifications).\",\n    \"SCHEMA DRIFT vs the PRD FR-1 snippet: AuditLog stores the IP in a column named `ip`, not `ipAddress`, and has @@index([actorId]) and @@index([action]) rather than the PRD's [entityType, entityId] and [actorId, createdAt] indexes. Under the no-rename rule, keep `ip`.\",\n    \"PRD-04 is already present: sendAuthEmail() renders the email and enqueues it into EmailOutbox. The PRD's interim 'log via logger.info' behaviour must NOT be reintroduced.\"\n  ],\n  \"functionalRequirements\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-1\",\n      \"description\": \"Prisma enums Role, UserStatus, AuthTokenType and models User, AuthToken, AuditLog exist with the fields in the PRD (status default INVITED, failedLoginCount default 0, nullable passwordHash until invite accepted, AuthToken.tokenHash unique, cascade delete). Status: already present; keep as-is.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Functional Requirements › FR-1 Data model\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-2\",\n      \"description\": \"A public /login page built from MUI sign-in template patterns (Card, TextField, Button, InputAdornment+IconButton show-password toggle, Alert for form errors). It has email and password fields and submits through Auth.js signIn('credentials'). Status: PRESENT (src/app/(auth)/login). Verify only; do not rebuild.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.1; Pages & Routes '/login'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-3\",\n      \"description\": \"The credentials authorize function lower-cases and trims the email. It rejects when the user does not exist, status != ACTIVE, archivedAt is set, or lockedUntil > now, and it verifies the password with bcrypt cost 12. Status: present in src/server/auth/credentials.ts.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-4\",\n      \"description\": \"Every sign-in failure shows 'Email or password is incorrect.', with two exceptions: a locked account shows 'This account is temporarily locked. Try again in N minutes.' and a disabled account shows 'This account is disabled. Contact the school office.' The /login UI must surface the server's message.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.3; Acceptance Criteria 2, 3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-5\",\n      \"description\": \"A failed password increments failedLoginCount. At 5 failures, lockedUntil is set to now+15min and the count resets to 0. A successful sign-in resets failedLoginCount to 0 and sets lastLoginAt. Status: present (computeLockout).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.4; Acceptance Criterion 2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-6\",\n      \"description\": \"Sign-in is rate-limited to 10 attempts per IP per 5 minutes using the in-memory sliding window exported from src/server/rate-limit.ts. Going over returns RATE_LIMITED, and the form shows 'Too many attempts. Wait a few minutes and try again.' Status: limiter present; the UI message is MISSING.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.5\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-7\",\n      \"description\": \"After sign-in, the user is redirected to callbackUrl only when it is a same-origin relative path; otherwise to /dashboard. Reuse safeCallbackUrl() from src/lib/validators/auth.ts.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.6; Acceptance Criterion 1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-8\",\n      \"description\": \"Sign-in writes the audit entries auth.login.success, auth.login.failure (metadata: attempted email and reason) and auth.lockout.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-2.7; Acceptance Criterion 2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-9\",\n      \"description\": \"The JWT session lasts 8 hours and is refreshed on activity. The JWT and session.user carry id, role, firstName, lastName and email. Status: present.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-10\",\n      \"description\": \"A session is invalid when passwordChangedAt is later than the token issue time. The jwt callback checks this at most once every 5 minutes per token, so other devices are signed out within 5 minutes. Status: present (RECHECK_MS).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.2; Acceptance Criterion 7\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-11\",\n      \"description\": \"middleware.ts redirects unauthenticated (app)-group page requests to /login?callbackUrl=<path>. Unauthenticated /api/* requests get 401 JSON with error.code UNAUTHENTICATED, except /api/health, /api/auth/* and the paths in src/config/public-routes.ts. Status: present in src/middleware.ts.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-3.3; Goals 2; Acceptance Criterion 8\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-12\",\n      \"description\": \"All AuthToken creation, lookup and consumption goes through src/server/auth/tokens.ts: createToken(userId, type, ttl) returns the raw token and stores its SHA-256 hash; verifyToken(raw, type) returns user/token or null when missing, used or expired; consumeToken(tokenId) sets usedAt. Status: present; no other module may re-implement hashing.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.0\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-13\",\n      \"description\": \"A public /invite/[token] page verifies the INVITE token (7-day expiry). An invalid, used or expired token shows 'This invitation link is invalid or has expired. Ask the school office to send a new one.' A valid token shows the user's name and email read-only, plus new-password and confirm fields. Status: MISSING (UI page). The API and service exist.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.1, FR-4.2; Acceptance Criteria 4, 5\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-14\",\n      \"description\": \"Accepting an invite validates the password policy, hashes the password, sets status=ACTIVE and passwordChangedAt=now, consumes the token, signs the user in, redirects to /dashboard, and audits auth.invite.accepted. Reusing the link afterwards shows the invalid-link message. Status: the service and API exist; the UI page is MISSING.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-4.3; Acceptance Criterion 4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-15\",\n      \"description\": \"Password policy in src/lib/validators/auth.ts: 10–128 characters, at least one letter and one digit, not equal to the user's email, and not in the bundled 1,000-entry src/server/auth/common-passwords.txt. 'password123' fails the common-password rule. Status: present.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.1; Acceptance Criterion 10\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-16\",\n      \"description\": \"A live strength checklist under every new-password field (invite, reset, change) shows each policy rule as met or unmet, driven by passwordChecks()/PASSWORD_RULES. Status: the PasswordChecklist component exists. It must be wired into the invite, reset and security pages.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-5.2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-17\",\n      \"description\": \"A public /forgot-password page has an email field. It always shows \\\"If an account exists for that email, we've sent a reset link.\\\" (no user enumeration) and is rate-limited to 3 requests per email per hour and 10 per IP per hour. Status: the API exists; the /forgot-password UI page is MISSING.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.1; Acceptance Criterion 6\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-18\",\n      \"description\": \"When the email belongs to an ACTIVE user, the service creates a PASSWORD_RESET token via createToken(userId, 'PASSWORD_RESET', { minutes: 60 }) (32 random bytes, base64url), invalidates older unused reset tokens, and calls sendAuthEmail(user, 'password-reset', link). An unknown email creates no token row.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.2; Acceptance Criterion 6\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-19\",\n      \"description\": \"A public /reset-password/[token] page has new-password and confirm fields. On success the service sets the hash and passwordChangedAt=now, clears the lockout fields, consumes the token, and audits auth.password.reset. The UI then redirects to /login, which shows a useToast success toast. Status: the API exists; the /reset-password/[token] UI page is MISSING.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-6.3; Acceptance Criterion 7\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-20\",\n      \"description\": \"An /account/security page (any signed-in user) has current, new and confirm password fields and calls POST /api/account/password. A wrong current password shows the field error 'Current password is incorrect.' Success shows the toast 'Password updated', invalidates other sessions through passwordChangedAt, and re-issues the current session. Status: the API exists; the /account/security UI page is MISSING.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.1; Pages & Routes '/account/security'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-21\",\n      \"description\": \"Add an 'Account security' item, linking to /account/security, to the top-bar user menu. Status: MISSING.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-7.2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-22\",\n      \"description\": \"src/server/services/users.ts provides createUser (INVITED, throws CONFLICT on duplicate email), createInviteToken (7-day INVITE token via tokens.ts, invalidates older unused invites), sendInvite (createInviteToken + sendAuthEmail 'invite'), setUserStatus and unlockUser. Status: present; verify only.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-8.1–FR-8.4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-23\",\n      \"description\": \"src/server/auth/requireRole.ts exposes getCurrentUser() (session user or null), requireUser() (throws AppError UNAUTHENTICATED; pages redirect to /login) and requireRole(...roles) (throws FORBIDDEN, so a STUDENT calling an ADMIN handler gets 403; pages redirect to /forbidden). There is no separate permissions.ts and no can() helper. Status: present.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-9.1–FR-9.5; Goals 3; Acceptance Criterion 9\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-24\",\n      \"description\": \"src/server/audit.ts audit({ actorId, action, entityType?, entityId?, metadata?, request? }) inserts an AuditLog row, captures the IP from x-forwarded-for when a request is passed, and never throws (errors go to the logger). Status: present.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-10.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-25\",\n      \"description\": \"Delete PLACEHOLDER_USER from src/app/(app)/shell.tsx. The shell gets the real signed-in user from the session, so the codebase has exactly one source of 'current user'. Status: MISSING (PLACEHOLDER_USER is still in shell.tsx).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-11.1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-26\",\n      \"description\": \"The top-bar user menu shows the real user's name, a role badge and avatar initials. 'Sign out' calls signOut() and redirects to /login. Status: MISSING.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-11.2; Acceptance Criterion 1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-27\",\n      \"description\": \"Sidebar navigation filtering (navigationForRole in src/config/navigation.ts) uses the session role instead of the placeholder role. Status: MISSING (navigationForRole(PLACEHOLDER_USER.role)).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-11.3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-28\",\n      \"description\": \"The seed idempotently creates six ACTIVE users with password 'SchoolHub123!': admin@ Alice Admin ADMIN, teacher@ Tom Teacher TEACHER, teacher2@ Tina Tutor TEACHER, student@ Sam Student STUDENT, student2@ Sara Scholar STUDENT, parent@ Pat Parent PARENT (all @schoolhub.test). The existing seed has no users. Status: PRESENT (prisma/seed.ts).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data table\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-29\",\n      \"description\": \"The seed creates one INVITED user, invited@schoolhub.test, and logs its invite link during seeding. Status: PRESENT (prisma/seed.ts).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data, final sentence\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-30\",\n      \"description\": \"The seed logs the invite link through logger (createInviteToken + authLink) rather than through sendAuthEmail, because PRD-04's sendAuthEmail enqueues email and deliberately never logs raw links.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Seed Data + §Out of Scope (sendAuthEmail/PRD-04 note); inferred from workspace state\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-31\",\n      \"description\": \"Keep the existing PRD-04 sendAuthEmail() behaviour (render template and enqueue into EmailOutbox). Do not revert it to the interim logger.info stub described for the pre-PRD-04 state.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Out of Scope (email delivery) + §Platform Context 'reuse existing… never duplicate'; inferred from brownfield state\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-32\",\n      \"description\": \"The AuditLog IP column stays `ip` (existing name) rather than being renamed to the PRD snippet's `ipAddress`, because renaming existing model fields is prohibited. Flagged for human validation.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"LOW\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 (AuditLog.ipAddress) vs §Platform Context 'never rename existing routes or models'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-33\",\n      \"description\": \"An additive migration adds @@index([role, status]) on User, which the PRD FR-1 model declares and the current schema lacks. Status: PRESENT (migration 20261106000000_user_role_status_index).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"MEDIUM\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-1 User model '@@index([role, status])'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"FR-34\",\n      \"description\": \"Tests: unit tests for password policy, token hashing/expiry, lockout counter, rate limiter and callbackUrl check (mostly existing); Vitest integration tests against the test DB for authorize branches, accept-invite, reset-password and change-password (MISSING); Playwright e2e for sign-in/out, the failed-login message and forgot → reset, reading the link from a test-only DB helper or the EmailOutbox (MISSING). Status: the unit tests exist. The integration tests and Playwright auth specs are MISSING.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Test Requirements\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"nonFunctionalRequirements\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-1\",\n      \"description\": \"Raw tokens are never stored, only their SHA-256 hashes, and token hashes are compared in constant time.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-2\",\n      \"description\": \"Session cookies are HttpOnly, Secure in production, and SameSite=Lax. Every auth form carries Auth.js-supplied CSRF protection.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 1\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-3\",\n      \"description\": \"'No such user' and 'wrong password' sign-in responses take similar time: a dummy bcrypt compare runs when the user does not exist.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-4\",\n      \"description\": \"Sign-in completes in under 1 second at p95 on local hardware with bcrypt cost 12.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 3\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-5\",\n      \"description\": \"Accessibility: form errors are announced with aria-live=\\\"polite\\\", and focus moves to the first invalid field on submit, on every auth form.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Non-Functional Requirements 4\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-6\",\n      \"description\": \"UI component rule: every visible element uses @mui/material, @mui/icons-material or the listed MUI X packages, composed with Box/Stack/Grid and the theme. Before any component is used, it is looked up via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs then fetchDocs for @mui/material@9.5.0), and only documented props, slots and imports are used. If the MCP server is unreachable, that is a blocker; do not guess. Toasts use useToast() (Snackbar+Alert).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context › UI component rule 1, 2, 5, 6\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-7\",\n      \"description\": \"No banned UI or styling libraries are used (Tailwind, shadcn/ui, Radix, Headless UI, Chakra, AntD, Bootstrap, lucide-react, next-themes, @tanstack/react-table, Recharts, FullCalendar, react-select, react-datepicker, sonner, notistack). Styling goes only through the theme, sx and styled(). QA checks for banned imports and verifies that every MUI import resolves to a documented component.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Platform Context › UI component rule 3, 6; Fixed technology decisions 'Theming'\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-8\",\n      \"description\": \"Audit metadata never contains password hashes, raw tokens or full passwords.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD FR-10.2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-9\",\n      \"description\": \"Every protected page and API handler enforces access on the server through requireUser/requireRole. Hiding a UI control is never the only protection.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (requireRole.ts bullet); Goals 2\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-10\",\n      \"description\": \"API handlers are thin (parse with Zod, call a service, return JSON). They use the {data} / list / {error:{code,message,details}} envelope and the standard error codes (VALIDATION_ERROR 400, UNAUTHENTICATED 401, FORBIDDEN 403, NOT_FOUND 404, CONFLICT 409, RATE_LIMITED 429, INTERNAL 500).\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (route handlers, response shape)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-11\",\n      \"description\": \"Forms use React Hook Form with zodResolver and the Zod schemas shared from src/lib/validators/auth.ts. Client and server use the same validation.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Fixed technology decisions (Validation, Forms)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-12\",\n      \"description\": \"No console.log in committed code; use the logger from src/lib/logger.ts.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Code layout and conventions (last bullet)\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-13\",\n      \"description\": \"Scope and regression guard: delivered in a single run with no scope expansion. Do not modify src/server/auth/course-access.ts or student-access.ts, do not rebuild existing auth modules, and do not rename existing routes or models. npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test must keep passing.\",\n      \"confidence\": \"HIGH\",\n      \"source\": \"PRD §Assumptions and constraints; §Out of Scope; §Platform Context intro\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NFR-14\",\n      \"description\": \"Only invited users can