s.spec.ts`, `dashboard.spec.ts` (T8) | dashboard.spec ran (2/2 pass with CSP bypass) | notifications.spec is blocked by the pre-existing DataGrid build error on /admin/email-log |\n| `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts` (T9) | — (test file, 5 tests) | 5/5 pass (with CSP bypass) |\n\nUnchanged server modules the SH-1 UI calls (`services/auth.ts`, `credentials.ts`, `tokens.ts`, `rate-limit.ts`, `audit.ts`) are covered by `tests/integration/auth.test.ts` and the existing unit tests.\n\n## Tests added by QA\n\n| File | Tests | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx` | 10 | 9 pass, 1 **fails on purpose**: it shows the NFR-5 focus defect |\n| `tests/unit/public-routes.test.ts` | 14 | 14 pass |\n| `tests/e2e/auth-qa.spec.ts` | 5 | 4 pass, 1 **fails on purpose**: it shows the NFR-5 focus defect in Chromium |\n\nQA also made one change to Dev's `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`. Two `getByRole('alert')` locators were scoped with `.filter({ hasText: /\\S/ })`. Without that, once the page hydrates, they also match Next's empty `#__next-route-announcer__` (role=alert) and fail strict mode.\n\n## Not covered\n\n- **Code paths with no test:**\n  - The signIn-failure fallback in `TokenPasswordForm`, after an invite is accepted.\n  - The network-error branch of `postJson`.\n  - The `limit 3/email/hour` branch of forgot-password (`services/auth.ts:46`). It is code-reviewed only.\n- **Behaviour with no test:**\n  - Sign-out of other devices within 5 minutes (FR-10). Only the same-session re-issue is verified, by reloading after a password change.\n  - `auth.login.failure` audit rows (FR-8). The code is reviewed at `credentials.ts:43`, but no test asserts the row.\n- **Browsers:** Firefox, WebKit and Edge (NFR-15). Only Chromium was executed.\n- **Production:** behaviour under `next build`/`next start`. The build fails for a pre-existing reason (see qa-report.md).\n"}}}
