2 bytes base64url), :56 (timingSafeEqual); tests/unit/tokens.test.ts |\n| NFR-2 | PASS | Observed `Set-Cookie: authjs.session-token=…; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax` (Secure applies under https in Auth.js and could not be checked on localhost); a POST without csrfToken → `/login?error=MissingCSRF`. See blocker 1 for the GET credential leak. |\n| NFR-3 | PASS | credentials.ts:24,56 (DUMMY_HASH compare); integration \"same code for unknown email and wrong password\" |\n| NFR-4 | PASS | 6 sign-ins via /api/auth/callback/credentials on the local dev server took 0.31–0.63s (bcrypt 12) |\n| NFR-5 | **FAIL** | aria-live regions are present, but focus does not move: tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx \"blocks an invalid email client-side, focusing the field\" and tests/e2e/auth-qa.spec.ts \"…focuses the first invalid field\" both fail. Root cause: FormField.tsx:39 (see finding 2). |\n| NFR-6 | PASS | All SH-1 UI imports come from @mui/material and @mui/icons-material (typecheck clean); toasts go through useToast. Whether Dev consulted mui-mcp cannot be verified after the fact. |\n| NFR-7 | PASS | tests/unit/eslint-no-restricted-imports.test.ts (16 pass); grep for banned packages in src → 0 |\n| NFR-8 | PASS | tests/integration/auth.test.ts \"no audit metadata carries password or token keys or values\" |\n| NFR-9 | PASS | (app)/layout.tsx + account/security/page.tsx `requirePageUser`; api/account/password `requireUser`; unauthenticated curl → 307 |\n| NFR-10 | PASS | api/account/password/route.ts (parseBody → service → ok); tests/unit/http.test.ts |\n| NFR-11 | PASS | ForgotPasswordForm, SetPasswordForm and ChangePasswordForm use zodResolver with schemas from src/lib/validators/auth.ts, which the API routes also use |\n| NFR-12 | PASS | `grep -rn console.log src` → only inside src/lib/logger.ts |\n| NFR-13 | **FAIL** | Scope guard OK: only the 14 owned files changed, and course-access.ts and student-access.ts are untouched. Typecheck and lint pass. But `npm run test` cannot start (vitest.config.ts imports `vitest/config.js`), and the suite run with the identical config has 3 failing tests and 2 test files that won't load. The ones caused by SH-1 work are the rate-limit timeout and the NFR-5 defect; the rest existed before (finding 3). |\n| NFR-14 | PASS | tests/e2e/auth-qa.spec.ts (/signup, /sign-up, /register → /login); tests/unit/public-routes.test.ts |\n| NFR-15 | PASS | No browser-specific APIs in the SH-1 code. Only Chromium was executed; Firefox, WebKit and Edge were not run. |\n\n## How QA ran things\n\n- `npm run typecheck` ✔ and `npm run lint` ✔.\n- `npm run test` ✘ (startup error). The suite was run with `TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://schoolhub:schoolhub@localhost:5433/schoolhub?schema=public npx vitest run -c vitest.tmp.config.ts`: **188 passed, 3 failed** (191 tests across 22 files).\n- `npm run build` ✘: MUI X `useFirstRender` export mismatch (existed before SH-1).\n- E2E:\n  - Ran against `next dev -p 3100`. Port 3000 is a stale `next-server` from Oct 27 that returns 500 on every route; QA did not kill it.\n  - Ran with a throwaway Playwright config that set `use.bypassCSP: true`. That config has been deleted.\n  - Playwright chromium build 1134 was installed into the user cache.\n  - Results: `auth.spec.ts` 5/5, `dashboard.spec.ts` 2/2 (render), `auth-qa.spec.ts` 4/5 (NFR-5).\n  - Without the bypass, every interactive e2e test fails because of blocker 1.\n- All QA test users (`@qa-e2e.test`, `@auth-it.test`) were removed. Seed user student2 was restored by `auth.spec.ts` afterAll.\n\n## Recommended fixes (in priority order)\n\n1. Make the CSP compatible with Next hydration (nonce via middleware, or `'unsafe-inline'`), and add `method=\"post\"` to the auth forms.\n2. In `FormField.tsx`, pass `inputRef={field.ref}` (fixes NFR-5 everywhere).\n3. In `vitest.config.ts`, change the import from `'vitest/config.js'` to `'vitest/config'`, then delete `vitest.tmp.config.ts`.\n4. Give the rate-limit integration test a 20s timeout.\n5. Align the `@mui/x-*` versions so that `next build` succeeds.\n6. Have the Dev phase write an SH-1 dev-log and task-completion-markers.\n"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TFC9zBBzkQfn3JxS55bLkY","type":"tool_result","content":"The file /Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/qa/qa-report.md has been updated successfully. (file state is current in your context — no need to Read it back)"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f52d74ab-5795-43ec-9250-cb726f8a81b9","uuid":"da478ea0-5f02-43ec-94b7-120fde51ef34","timestamp":"2026-11-05T17:14:55.650Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"update","filePath":"/Users/ikramaansari/Documents/forge/schoolhub/artifacts/qa/qa-report.md","content":"# QA Report — SH-1 (PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC)\n\n## QA Summary\n\n- ticketId: SH-1\n- timestamp: 2026-11-05T17:16:00Z\n- overallStatus: FAIL\n- requirementsChecked: 49\n- requirementsPassed: 47\n- requirementsFailed: 2\n\n## Headline findings\n\n1. **BLOCKER (existed before SH-1, but every SH-1 page depends on it): the app's CSP stops React from hydrating, so no client UI works in a real browser.**\n   - `next.config.js` (dated Oct 16) sends `Content-Security-Policy: … script-src 'self'`.\n   - That policy blocks Next's inline `self.__next_f` scripts, plus `eval` in dev. In Chromium, `/login` was still not hydrated after 60s.\n   - Consequences:\n     - `/login`, `/forgot-password`, `/invite/[token]`, `/reset-password/[token]` and `/account/security` all render, but none of them work.\n     - Submitting a form falls back to a native **GET**, which puts credentials in the URL. For example: `/login?email=admin%40schoolhub.test&password=SchoolHub123%21` (seed creds).\n   - Every UI verdict below was proven with Playwright `bypassCSP: true`. That proves the SH-1 code is correct; it does **not** prove the shipped app works.\n   - Fix:\n     - Use a nonce-based CSP in middleware, or allow `'unsafe-inline'` for scripts (plus `'unsafe-eval'` in dev only).\n     - Also add `method=\"post\"` to the auth `<form>`s so a hydration failure can never leak passwords into URLs, logs or history.\n2. **FAIL NFR-5: focus does not move to the first invalid field.**\n   - The shared `TextFormField` (`src/components/FormField/FormField.tsx:39`) spreads `{...field}`. That puts RHF's `ref` on the TextField root `<div>` instead of the `<input>`, so neither `shouldFocusError` nor `setError(…, { shouldFocus })` can focus anything.\n   - Reproduced in jsdom (`tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx`) and in real Chromium (`tests/e2e/auth-qa.spec.ts` › NFR-5).\n   - One-line fix: pass `inputRef={field.ref}`, and keep `ref` out of the spread.\n   - This fixes every form in the app, not only the auth forms.\n3. **FAIL NFR-13: `npm run test` cannot start.**\n   - `vitest.config.ts` imports `vitest/config.js`, which doesn't exist in vitest 2.1.1. The file dates from 10:47 today, before SH-1's Dev run.\n   - `vitest.tmp.config.ts` is identical apart from the import, so QA ran the suite with it.\n   - The full suite then has 3 failing tests:\n     - `useToast` auto-hide: existed before SH-1.\n     - The QA NFR-5 test: the real defect in finding 2.\n     - The Dev integration test \"rate limits after 10 attempts per IP\": it times out at the 5s default under parallel load, because 10 × bcrypt-12 dummy compares run too long. It passes on its own (3/3 runs). Give it a `{ timeout: 20_000 }`.\n   - Two test files fail to load for reasons that existed before SH-1: `DataTable` (MUI X `useFirstRender` export) and `lockout` (`next/server` import).\n4. **`next build` fails, for a reason that existed before SH-1.**\n   - Cause: `@mui/x-data-grid` imports `@mui/x-internals/useFirstRender`, which that package doesn't export (a version mismatch).\n   - It also wedges `next dev` once any DataGrid page compiles. That page is `/admin/email-log`, so `notifications.spec.ts` could not run.\n   - SH-1 pages don't import DataGrid.\n5. **The Dev artifacts are stale.**\n   - `artifacts/dev/dev-log.md` and `task-completion-markers.json` are SH-4 files from 2026-11-04.\n   - There is no SH-1 dev log. Even so, `dev-rerun-count.json` says `firstPassAccepted: true`.\n   - QA therefore checked reality directly: all 14 files in `file-ownership-matrix.json` exist, they contain real implementations (no stubs, no TODOs), and no other file was modified.\n6. **The SH-1 code itself is solid.**\n   - Typecheck and lint are clean.\n   - Tests pass:\n     - Dev integration tests: 11/11 against real Postgres.\n     - Dev e2e `auth.spec.ts`: 5/5.\n     - QA tests: 27/29, and the 2 failures are the NFR-5 defect.\n   - Sign-in p95 is under 0.65s.\n\nAlso seen, outside SH-1's scope: the sidebar `<ul>` has `<a>` children (`ListItemButton component={Link}`), which is an axe `list` serious violation on signed-in pages. It only shows once the page hydrates. This is pre-existing shell nav code.\n\n## Requirement Results\n\n| Requirement | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | PASS | prisma/schema.prisma (User/AuthToken/AuditLog, AuthToken.tokenHash @unique, onDelete Cascade); exercised by tests/integration/auth.test.ts |\n| FR-2 | PASS | src/app/(auth)/login/*; tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts \"admin signs in…\" (with CSP bypass; see blocker 1) |\n| FR-3 | PASS | src/server/auth/credentials.ts; tests/integration/auth.test.ts \"rejects DISABLED, archived and locked accounts\", \"rejects unknown email and wrong password with the same code\" |\n| FR-4 | PASS | LoginForm.tsx `loginErrorMessage`; tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts; tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts \"a wrong password shows the generic error\" |\n| FR-5 | PASS | tests/integration/auth.test.ts \"locks on the 5th failure…\" and \"success resets failedLoginCount, sets lastLoginAt…\" |\n| FR-6 | PASS | tests/integration/auth.test.ts \"rate limits after 10 attempts per IP\" (passes in isolation; full-suite timeout under NFR-13); tests/unit/rate-limit.test.ts; 429 copy in tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx |\n| FR-7 | PASS | tests/unit/auth-validators.test.ts `safeCallbackUrl`; tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts callbackUrl redirect |\n| FR-