 `vitest/config.js`), and the suite run with the identical config has 3 failing tests and 2 test files that won't load. The ones caused by SH-1 work are the rate-limit timeout and the NFR-5 defect; the rest existed before (finding 3). |\n| NFR-14 | PASS | tests/e2e/auth-qa.spec.ts (/signup, /sign-up, /register → /login); tests/unit/public-routes.test.ts |\n| NFR-15 | PASS | No browser-specific APIs in the SH-1 code. Only Chromium was executed; Firefox, WebKit and Edge were not run. |\n\n## How QA ran things\n\n- `npm run typecheck` ✔ and `npm run lint` ✔.\n- `npm run test` ✘ (startup error). The suite was run with `TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://schoolhub:schoolhub@localhost:5433/schoolhub?schema=public npx vitest run -c vitest.tmp.config.ts`: **188 passed, 3 failed** (191 tests across 22 files).\n- `npm run build` ✘: MUI X `useFirstRender` export mismatch (existed before SH-1).\n- E2E:\n  - Ran against `next dev -p 3100`. Port 3000 is a stale `next-server` from Oct 27 that returns 500 on every route; QA did not kill it.\n  - Ran with a throwaway Playwright config that set `use.bypassCSP: true`. That config has been deleted.\n  - Playwright chromium build 1134 was installed into the user cache.\n  - Results: `auth.spec.ts` 5/5, `dashboard.spec.ts` 2/2 (render), `auth-qa.spec.ts` 4/5 (NFR-5).\n  - Without the bypass, every interactive e2e test fails because of blocker 1.\n- All QA test users (`@qa-e2e.test`, `@auth-it.test`) were removed. Seed user student2 was restored by `auth.spec.ts` afterAll.\n\n## Recommended fixes (in priority order)\n\n1. Make the CSP compatible with Next hydration (nonce via middleware, or `'unsafe-inline'`), and add `method=\"post\"` to the auth forms.\n2. In `FormField.tsx`, pass `inputRef={field.ref}` (fixes NFR-5 everywhere).\n3. In `vitest.config.ts`, change the import from `'vitest/config.js'` to `'vitest/config'`, then delete `vitest.tmp.config.ts`.\n4. Give the rate-limit integration test a 20s timeout.\n5. Align the `@mui/x-*` versions so that `next build` succeeds.\n6. Have the Dev phase write an SH-1 dev-log and task-completion-markers.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":106,"newStart":1,"newLines":129,"lines":["-# QA Report — SH-6 (PRD-06 Bell Schedule & Timetable)","+# QA Report — SH-1 (PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC)"," "," ## QA Summary"," ","-- ticketId: SH-6","-- timestamp: 2026-11-05T10:36:00Z","+- ticketId: SH-1","+- timestamp: 2026-11-05T17:16:00Z"," - overallStatus: FAIL","-- requirementsChecked: 61","-- requirementsPassed: 34","-- requirementsFailed: 27 (1 FAIL + 26 NOT-IMPLEMENTED)","+- requirementsChecked: 49","+- requirementsPassed: 47","+- requirementsFailed: 2"," "," ## Headline findings"," ","-1. **Dev stopped after TASK-8. The whole UI and the seed are missing.**","-   - Not built: TASK-9 to TASK-16, which cover the grid, the bell schedule page, the timetable editor, the personal, student and course timetable views, navigation, the seed, and the e2e test.","-   - None of the 25 planned CREATE files for those tasks exist.","-   - The planned edits to `student-tabs.ts`, `course-tabs.ts`, `navigation.ts`, `shell.tsx` and `seed.ts` were not made.","-   - `@dnd-kit/core` was added to `package.json` but is never imported.","-2. **The Dev artifacts are stale and do not describe this ticket.**","-   - `artifacts/dev/dev-log.md` and `task-completion-markers.json` are SH-4 (Notifications) files dated 2026-11-04. Their \"TASK-1..21 complete\" claims refer to PRD-04.","-   - No SH-6 dev log exists, but `dev-rerun-count.json` says `firstPassAccepted: true`. The pipeline accepted a Dev phase that never wrote its own outputs.","-3. **The backend that does exist is solid.**","-   - Covers TASK-1 to TASK-8: schema, migration, validators, clash engine, service, and 10 API routes.","-   - Contains real logic, with no stubs, TODO markers or console.log calls.","-   - Typecheck and lint pass.","-   - Passes 21 Dev unit tests and 16 new QA integration tests against real Postgres, including the NFR-1 concurrency guarantee.","-4. **The build is healthy, with no regressions.**","-   - `npm run typecheck` and `npm run lint` are both clean.","-   - `vitest run` shows 3 failing files. They are the same 3 failures recorded before this ticket (`DataTable` MUI X exports, `lockout` next-auth import, `useToast` timer), and none of them touch SH-6 code.","+1. **BLOCKER (existed before SH-1, but every SH-1 page depends on it): the app's CSP stops React from hydrating, so no client UI works in a real browser.**","+   - `next.config.js` (dated Oct 16) sends `Content-Security-Policy: … script-src 'self'`.","+   - That policy blocks Next's inline `self.__next_f` scripts, plus `eval` in dev. In Chromium, `/login` was still not hydrated after 60s.","+   - Consequences:","+     - `/login`, `/forgot-password`, `/invite/[token]`, `/reset-password/[token]` and `/account/security` all render, but none of them work.","+     - Submitting a form falls back to a native **GET**, which puts credentials in the URL. For example: `/login?email=admin%40schoolhub.test&password=SchoolHub123%21` (seed creds).","+   - Every UI verdict below was proven with Playwright `bypassCSP: true`. That proves the SH-1 code is correct; it does **not** prove the shipped app works.","+   - Fix:","+     - Use a nonce-based CSP in middleware, or allow `'unsafe-inline'` for scripts (plus `'unsafe-eval'` in dev only).","+     - Also add `method=\"post\"` to the auth `<form>`s so a hydration failure can never leak passwords into URLs, logs or history.","+2. **FAIL NFR-5: focus does not move to the first invalid field.**","+   - The shared `TextFormField` (`src/components/FormField/FormField.tsx:39`) spreads `{...field}`. That puts RHF's `ref` on the TextField root `<div>` instead of the `<input>`, so neither `shouldFocusError` nor `setError(…, { shouldFocus })` can focus anything.","+   - Reproduced in jsdom (`tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx`) and in real Chromium (`tests/e2e/auth-qa.spec.ts` › NFR-5).","+   - One-line fix: pass `inputRef={field.ref}`, and keep `ref` out of the spread.","+   - This fixes every form in the app, not only the auth forms.","+3. **FAIL NFR-13: `npm run test` cannot start.**","+   - `vitest.config.ts` imports `vitest/config.js`, which doesn't exist in vitest 2.1.1. The file dates from 10:47 today, before SH-1's Dev run.","+   - `vitest.tmp.config.ts` is identical apart from the import, so QA ran the suite with it.","+   - The full suite then has 3 failing tests:","+     - `useToast` auto-hide: existed before SH-1.","+     - The QA NFR-5 test: the real defect in finding 2.","+     - The Dev integration test \"rate limits after 10 attempts per IP\": it times out at the 5s default under parallel load, because 10 × bcrypt-12 dummy compares run too long. It passes on its own (3/3 runs). Give it a `{ timeout: 20_000 }`.","+   - Two test files fail to load for reasons that existed before SH-1: `DataTable` (MUI X `useFirstRender` export) and `lockout` (`next/server` import).","+4. **`next build` fails, for a reason that existed before SH-1.**","+   - Cause: `@mui/x-data-grid` imports `@mui/x-internals/useFirstRender`, which that package doesn't export (a version mismatch).","+   - It also wedges `next dev` once any DataGrid page compiles. That page is `/admin/email-log`, so `notifications.spec.ts` could not run.","+   - SH-1 pages don't import DataGrid.","+5. **The Dev artifacts are stale.**","+   - `artifacts/dev/dev-log.md` and `task-completion-markers.json` are SH-4 files from 2026-11-04.","+   - There is no SH-1 dev log. Even so, `dev-rerun-count.json` says `firstPassAccepted: true`.","+   - QA therefore checked reality directly: all 14 files in `file-ownership-matrix.json` exist, they contain real implementations (no stubs, no TODOs), and no other file was modified.","+6. **The SH-1 code itself is solid.**","+   - Typecheck and lint are clean.","+   - Tests pass:","+     - Dev integration tests: 11/11 against real Postgres.","+     - Dev e2e `auth.spec.ts`: 5/5.","+     - QA tests: 27/29, and the 2 failures are the NFR-5 defect.","+   - Sign-in p95 is under 0.65s."," ","+Also seen, outside SH-1's scope: the sidebar `<ul>` has `<a>` children (`ListItemButton component={Link}`), which is an axe `list` serious violation on signed-in pages. It only shows once the page hydrates. This is pre-existing shell nav code.","+"," ## Requirement Results"," "," | Requirement | Status | Evidence |"," |---|---|---|","-| FR-1 | PASS | prisma/schema.prisma (`enum PeriodKind`, `model Period`); migration 20261105000000_timetable; used by tests/integration/timetable-concurrency.test.ts |","-| FR-2 | PASS | `model SchoolDay` + migration; integration \"FR-7/FR-40\" test upserts and reads it |","-| FR-3 | PASS | `model TimetableSlot` with `@@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` and `@@index([academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` in migration.sql; course FK `ON DELETE CASCADE` |","-| FR-4 | PASS | One additive migration with no ALTERs to existing tables except new FKs; back-relations on Course, Period and Room (schema lines 219/280/418/459); `prisma migrate status` reports it as up to date |","-| FR-5 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | `src/app/(app)/admin/timetable/periods/page.tsx` and `BellScheduleEditor.tsx` are missing. Only the API exists. |","-| FR-6 | PASS | src/lib/validators/timetable.ts (`hhmm`, `periodSchema`); service `assertNoOverlap`; tests/unit/timetable-time.test.ts (periodsOverlap, periodSchema) |","-| FR-7 | FAIL | The backend works: `updateSchoolDays` cascade-deletes slots and returns the count (integration \"FR-7/FR-40\"). The ToggleButton editor and the confirmation dialog are missing. |","-| FR-8 | PASS | `deletePeriod` throws CONFLICT with `details.slotCount`; integration \"FR-8\" |","-| FR-9 | PASS | clash-rules.ts TEACHER rule; unit (main and co-teacher, both directions); integration \"FR-9/FR-10\" (exact message) and \"co-teacher clash\" |","-| FR-10 | PASS | ROOM rule; unit; integration exact message `Clash: QA6-R1 is used by QA6-MATH-7A on Monday, QA6-P1.` |","-| FR-11 | PASS | SECTION rule; unit; integration \"FR-11\" exact message |","-| FR-12 | PASS | `overlapByCourse` (ACTIVE only); integration \"FR-12\" (a DROPPED enrollment is excluded, count = 1) |","-| FR-13 | PASS | PERIOD_KIND / NON_TEACHING_DAY; unit; integration \"FR-13\" |","-| FR-14 | PASS | `validateSlot` returns every clash (integration gets TEACHER and ROOM together); PATCH excludes the moving slot (integration \"FR-14/FR-18\", unit \"excludes the moving slot\") |","-| FR-15 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | `src/app/(app)/admin/timetable/page.tsx` and `TimetableEditor.tsx` are missing |","-| FR-16 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | `src/components/TimetableGrid/` is missing |","-| FR-17 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | Editor is missing (POST /api/timetable/slots exists) |","-| FR-18 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | The UI drag, Delete key and confirmation are missing. The PATCH/DELETE service is tested in integration. |","-| FR-19 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | The red tint, icon and tooltip are missing. The availability API passes (see FR-36). |","-| FR-20 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | The snap-back and toast are missing |","-| FR-21 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | The room Popover is missing. `getFreeRooms` / GET /api/timetable/free-rooms is tested in integration \"FR-21\". |","-| FR-22 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | The keyboard \"Place course\" dialog is missing |","-| FR-23 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | `@dnd-kit/core` 6.3.1 is installed but imported nowhere in src/ |","-| FR-24 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | `src/app/(app)/timetable/page.tsx` and `PersonalTimetable.tsx` are missing. The data API passes (FR-38). |","-| FR-25 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | The child selector UI is missing. The server-side rule is tested (integration \"FR-38/FR-25\"). |","-| FR-26 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | The Week/Today toggle is missing. The `nowAndNext` helper exists and is unit-tested. |","-| FR-27 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | src/config/student-tabs.ts has no Timetable entry; `students/[id]/timetable/page.tsx` is missing |","-| FR-28 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | src/config/course-tabs.ts has no Schedule entry; `courses/[courseId]/schedule/page.tsx` is missing |","-| FR-29 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | `PrintButton.tsx` and `TimetablePrintStyles.tsx` are missing |","-| FR-30 | PASS | `getScheduleForDate`; integration \"FR-30/FR-31/FR-45\" (ordered entries for teacher and student; Saturday returns []) |","-| FR-31 | PASS | `getCurrentSlot`; same test (inside the period → slot; at the exclusive end → null) |","-| FR-32 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | src/config/navigation.ts has no Timetable, Timetable editor or Bell schedule entries |","-| FR-33 | PASS | src/app/api/periods/{route,[id]/route,reorder/route}.ts: GET uses `requireUser`, writes use `requireRole('ADMIN')`. Handler wiring was checked by reading the code; the service is tested in integration. |","-| FR-34 | PASS | src/app/api/school-days/route.ts (GET `requireUser`, PUT `requireRole('ADMIN')`); service tested in integration \"FR-7/FR-40\" |","-| FR-35 | PASS | `assertCanViewTimetable`; integration \"FR-35\" covers ADMIN any view, TEACHER own view and homeroom section, and 403 for another teacher, another section and a STUDENT. Note: TEACHER can also view sections they teach a course in (design decision D8), which is broader than \"homeroom only\". |","-| FR-36 | PASS | `getAvailability`; integration \"FR-36\" (key `4-<periodId>` holds the exact clash message; free cells are absent) |","-| FR-37 | PASS | slots routes are ADMIN-only; integration \"FR-37/FR-40\" (academicYearId comes from the course) and \"FR-9/FR-10\" (CONFLICT with `details.clashes[]` and 0 rows saved) |","-| FR-38 | PASS | `resolvePersonalTarget`; integration \"FR-38/FR-25\". Minor: a multi-child parent with no `studentId` gets 400 VALIDATION_ERROR rather than 403. That is reasonable, but it differs from the spec wording. |","-| FR-39 | PASS | src/lib/validators/timetable.ts holds every schema and is imported by all 10 handlers; unit \"periodSchema\" tests |","-| FR-40 | PASS | `audit()` calls in every write; integration checks the slot create, update and delete rows and `schoolDay.update` with `deletedSlotCount`. Period create, update, delete and reorder audits were checked by reading the code only. |","-| FR-41 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | prisma/seed.ts seeds no periods; `prisma/seed-timetable-week.ts` is missing |","-| FR-42 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | No SchoolDay seed (the dev DB has 0 SchoolDay rows; the service defaults to Mon–Fri) |","-| FR-43 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | No 7A/7B week seed |","-| FR-44 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | No Tom, Sam or Pat fixtures, sections or courses; the dev DB has 0 users |","-| FR-45 | PASS (server) | `schoolNow` + `schoolTimezone()`; unit tests across UTC, Los Angeles and Kolkata, including the date line; integration runs with SchoolSettings.timezone = Asia/Kolkata. The UI consumers do not exist yet (see FR-24 and FR-26). |","-| NFR-1 | PASS | `createSlot`/`moveSlot` use a SERIALIZABLE transaction and retry on P2034; integration \"NFR-1/NFR-12\" (exactly 1 of 2 concurrent inserts succeeds; the retry path ran) |","-| NFR-2 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | The editor does not exist, so the section-week load cannot be measured |","-| NFR-3 | PASS (indicative) | `getAvailability` runs a fixed number of queries. The whole 16-test integration suite, availability included, ran in about 400 ms on a small dataset. It was not measured at seed scale. |","-| NFR-4 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | There is no UI to check |","-| NFR-5 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | No UI was written, so there is no mui-mcp lookup trail |","-| NFR-6 | PASS | The only new dependency is `@dnd-kit/core` pinned at 6.3.1; `next lint` (no-restricted-imports) is clean |","-| NFR-7 | PASS (API) | All 10 handlers call `requireUser` or `requireRole` before the service runs, and per-entity checks run on the server (`assertCanViewTimetable`, `resolvePersonalTarget`). There are no server pages yet. |","-| NFR-8 | PASS | Handlers follow `withHandler` → `parseBody`/`parseQuery` (Zod) → service → `ok()`; CONFLICT is used for clashes and for period delete-with-slots |","-| NFR-9 | PASS | Reuses `http.ts`, `audit()` and `logger`; service at src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts; no renames |","-| NFR-10 | PASS | `tsc --noEmit` and `next lint` are clean. `vitest run`: 133 pass, 1 fail, in the same 3 files that failed before SH-6, so nothing regressed. |","-| NFR-11 | PASS | tests/unit/timetable-clash.test.ts and tests/unit/timetable-time.test.ts (21/21) |","-| NFR-12 | PASS | tests/integration/timetable-concurrency.test.ts (written by QA) |","-| NFR-13 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | `tests/e2e/timetable.spec.ts` is missing, and there is no UI to drive |","-| NFR-14 | PASS | grep finds no `console.log` in any SH-6 file; the service uses `logger.warn` |","-| NFR-15 | PASS | No solver, multi-week cycle, substitute or holiday code; there is only a holiday hook comment in `getScheduleForDate` |","-| NFR-16 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | There is no UI or print output to check |","+| FR-1 | PASS | prisma/schema.prisma (User/AuthToken/AuditLog, AuthToken.tokenHash @unique, onDelete Cascade); exercised by tests/integration/auth.test.ts |","+| FR-2 | PASS | src/app/(auth)/login/*; tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts \"admin signs in…\" (with CSP bypass; see blocker 1) |","+| FR-3 | PASS | src/server/auth/credentials.ts; tests/integration/auth.test.ts \"rejects DISABLED, archived and locked accounts\", \"rejects unknown email and wrong password with the same code\" |","+| FR-4 | PASS | LoginForm.tsx `loginErrorMessage`; tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts; tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts \"a wrong password shows the generic error\" |","+| FR-5 | PASS | tests/integration/auth.test.ts \"locks on the 5th failure…\" and \"success resets failedLoginCount, sets lastLoginAt…\" |","+| FR-6 | PASS | tests/integration/auth.test.ts \"rate limits after 10 attempts per IP\" (passes in isolation; full-suite timeout under NFR-13); tests/unit/rate-limit.test.ts; 429 copy in tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx |","+| FR-7 | PASS | tests/unit/auth-validators.test.ts `safeCallbackUrl`; tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts callbackUrl redirect |","+| FR-8 | PASS | tests/integration/auth.test.ts (auth.lockout and auth.login.success rows asserted); auth.login.failure in credentials.ts:43 (code-reviewed only, no test asserts the row) |","+| FR-9 | PASS | auth.config.ts:12 (maxAge 8h, updateAge 15m); the user menu shows the session name and role in tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts |","+| FR-10 | PASS | auth.ts:36-47 (authTime vs passwordChangedAt; `reauth` update); tests/integration/auth.test.ts \"success bumps passwordChangedAt\"; tests/e2e/auth-qa.spec.ts (current session survives reload after change). Logout of other devices is not e2e-tested. |","+| FR-11 | PASS | src/middleware.ts; tests/unit/public-routes.test.ts (QA); tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts redirect; curl /account/security → 307 /login?callbackUrl=%2Faccount%2Fsecurity |","+| FR-12 | PASS | src/server/auth/tokens.ts; tests/unit/tokens.test.ts; the invite/reset pages call verifyToken, and the APIs consume the token (integration \"token cannot be reused\") |","+| FR-13 | PASS | src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx; tests/e2e/auth-qa.spec.ts \"bogus invite token…\" and the read-only name/email; tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx |","+| FR-14 | PASS | tests/e2e/auth-qa.spec.ts \"invite accept → signed in on /dashboard; the link cannot be reused\" (DB: status ACTIVE, passwordChangedAt set); tests/integration/auth.test.ts acceptInvite |","+| FR-15 | PASS | src/lib/validators/auth.ts; tests/unit/password-policy.test.ts and auth-validators.test.ts; client rejection in tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx |","+| FR-16 | PASS | PasswordChecklist wired into SetPasswordForm (invite and reset) and ChangePasswordForm.tsx:70; asserted in tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx |","+| FR-17 | PASS | forgot-password/page.tsx + ForgotPasswordForm.tsx; tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx (same copy, 429); tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts; limits in services/auth.ts:42,46 (code-reviewed) |","+| FR-18 | PASS | tests/integration/auth.test.ts \"a known email gets a token and an outbox row; an unknown email gets neither\" |","+| FR-19 | PASS | reset-password/[token]/page.tsx; tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts forgot → reset → /login?reset=1 toast → sign in; tests/integration/auth.test.ts \"resetPassword clears lockout fields…\" |","+| FR-20 | PASS | account/security/*; tests/e2e/auth-qa.spec.ts (wrong current → field error; success → \"Password updated\"); tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx; api/account/password/route.ts re-issues the session through unstable_update |","+| FR-21 | PASS | shell.tsx:167-169; tests/e2e/auth-qa.spec.ts clicks the \"Account security\" menu item and lands on /account/security |","+| FR-22 | PASS | src/server/services/users.ts (createUser:118, setUserStatus:345, unlockUser:374, createInviteToken:383, sendInvite:392); verify-only, unchanged |","+| FR-23 | PASS | src/server/auth/requireRole.ts; used by (app)/layout.tsx and account/security/page.tsx; tests/unit/http.test.ts (error envelope) |","+| FR-24 | PASS | src/server/audit.ts; audit rows asserted in tests/integration/auth.test.ts |","+| FR-25 | PASS | `grep -rn PLACEHOLDER_USER src` → 0 matches; layout.tsx passes the requirePageUser() user to AppShell |","+| FR-26 | PASS | shell.tsx:162-176; tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts (name \"Alice Admin\", \"ADMIN\" chip, Sign out → /login) |","+| FR-27 | PASS | shell.tsx:74 `navigationForRole(user.role)` |","+| FR-28 | PASS | DB: 6 ACTIVE @schoolhub.test users; tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts signs in with `SchoolHub123!` |","+| FR-29 | PASS | DB: invited@schoolhub.test is INVITED; prisma/seed.ts:56 |","+| FR-30 | PASS | prisma/seed.ts:29,56 (createInviteToken + authLink via logger.info) |","+| FR-31 | PASS | tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts reads the reset link from EmailOutbox; tests/integration/auth.test.ts outbox row |","+| FR-32 | PASS | prisma/schema.prisma:176 `ip String?` (not renamed) |","+| FR-33 | PASS | prisma/migrations/20261106000000_user_role_status_index |","+| FR-34 | PASS | tests/integration/auth.test.ts (11 tests); tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts (5 tests); tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts |","+| NFR-1 | PASS | tokens.ts:17 (sha256), :27 (32 bytes base64url), :56 (timingSafeEqual); tests/unit/tokens.test.ts |","+| NFR-2 | PASS | Observed `Set-Cookie: authjs.session-token=…; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax` (Secure applies under https in Auth.js and could not be checked on localhost); a POST without csrfToken → `/login?error=MissingCSRF`. See blocker 1 for the GET credential leak. |","+| NFR-3 | PASS | credentials.ts:24,56 (DUMMY_HASH compare); integration \"same code for unknown email and wrong password\" |","+| NFR-4 | PASS | 6 sign-ins via /api/auth/callback/credentials on the local dev server took 0.31–0.63s (bcrypt 12) |","+| NFR-5 | **FAIL** | aria-live regions are present, but focus does not move: tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx \"blocks an invalid email client-side, focusing the field\" and tests/e2e/auth-qa.spec.ts \"…focuses the first invalid field\" both fail. Root cause: FormField.tsx:39 (see finding 2). |","+| NFR-6 | PASS | All SH-1 UI imports come from @mui/material and @mui/icons-material (typecheck clean); toasts go through useToast. Whether Dev consulted mui-mcp cannot be verified after the fact. |","+| NFR-7 | PASS | tests/unit/eslint-no-restricted-imports.test.ts (16 pass); grep for banned packages in src → 0 |","+| NFR-8 | PASS | tests/integration/auth.test.ts \"no audit metadata carries password or token keys or values\" |","+| NFR-9 | PASS | (app)/layout.tsx + account/security/page.tsx `requirePageUser`; api/account/password `requireUser`; unauthenticated curl → 307 |","+| NFR-10 | PASS | api/account/password/route.ts (parseBody → service → ok); tests/unit/http.test.ts |","+| NFR-11 | PASS | ForgotPasswordForm, SetPasswordForm and ChangePasswordForm use zodResolver with schemas from src/lib/validators/auth.ts, which the API routes also use |","+| NFR-12 | PASS | `grep -rn console.log src` → only inside src/lib/logger.ts |","+| NFR-13 | **FAIL** | Scope guard OK: only the 14 owned files changed, and course-access.ts and student-access.ts are untouched. Typecheck and lint pass. But `npm run test` cannot start (vitest.config.ts imports `vitest/config.js`), and the suite run with the identical config has 3 failing tests and 2 test files that won't load. The ones caused by SH-1 work are the rate-limit timeout and the NFR-5 defect; the rest existed before (finding 3). |","+| NFR-14 | PASS | tests/e2e/auth-qa.spec.ts (/signup, /sign-up, /register → /login); tests/unit/public-routes.test.ts |","+| NFR-15 | PASS | No browser-specific APIs in the SH-1 code. Only Chromium was executed; Firefox, WebKit and Edge were not run. |"," ","-## Tests written by QA","+## How QA ran things"," ","-- `tests/integration/timetable-concurrency.test.ts` has 16 tests running against real Postgres.","-- It skips without `TEST_DATABASE_URL`.","-- Its fixtures are tagged `QA6-` / `@qa-sh6.test` and removed afterwards. The SchoolDay table and the school timezone are snapshotted and restored.","-- It passed 4 runs in a row, and the dev DB was left unchanged.","+- `npm run typecheck` ✔ and `npm run lint` ✔.","+- `npm run test` ✘ (startup error). The suite was run with `TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://schoolhub:schoolhub@localhost:5433/schoolhub?schema=public npx vitest run -c vitest.tmp.config.ts`: **188 passed, 3 failed** (191 tests across 22 files).","+- `npm run build` ✘: MUI X `useFirstRender` export mismatch (existed before SH-1).","+- E2E:","+  - Ran against `next dev -p 3100`. Port 3000 is a stale `next-server` from Oct 27 that returns 500 on every route; QA did not kill it.","+  - Ran with a throwaway Playwright config that set `use.bypassCSP: true`. That config has been deleted.","+  - Playwright chromium build 1134 was installed into the user cache.","+  - Results: `auth.spec.ts` 5/5, `dashboard.spec.ts` 2/2 (render), `auth-qa.spec.ts` 4/5 (NFR-5).","+  - Without the bypass, every interactive e2e test fails because of blocker 1.","+- All QA test users (`@qa-e2e.test`, `@auth-it.test`) were removed. Seed user student2 was restored by `auth.spec.ts` afterAll."," ","-## Recommendation","+## Recommended fixes (in priority order)"," ","-Send SH-6 back to Dev to finish TASK-9 to TASK-16, starting with the TimetableGrid, then the editor, then the seed (FR-41 to FR-44), because the e2e test needs the seed. Dev also needs to write a real SH-6 `dev-log.md` and `task-completion-markers.json`. The backend is ready for the UI and does not need rework.","+1. Make the CSP compatible with Next hydration (nonce via middleware, or `'unsafe-inline'`), and add `method=\"post\"` to the auth forms.","+2. In `FormField.tsx`, pass `inputRef={field.ref}` (fixes NFR-5 everywhere).","+3. In `vitest.config.ts`, change the import from `'vitest/config.js'` to `'vitest/config'`, then delete `vitest.tmp.config.ts`.","+4. Give the rate-limit integration test a 20s timeout.","+5. Align the `@mui/x-*` versions so that `next build` succeeds.","+6. Have the Dev phase write an SH-1 dev-log and task-completion-markers."]}],"originalFile":"# QA Report — SH-6 (PRD-06 Bell Schedule & Timetable)\n\n## QA Summary\n\n- ticketId: SH-6\n- timestamp: 2026-11-05T10:36:00Z\n- overallStatus: FAIL\n- requirementsChecked: 61\n- requirementsPassed: 34\n- requirementsFailed: 27 (1 FAIL + 26 NOT-IMPLEMENTED)\n\n## Headline findings\n\n1. **Dev stopped after TASK-8. The whole UI and the seed are missing.**\n   - Not built: TASK-9 to TASK-16, which cover the grid, the bell schedule page, the timetable editor, the personal, student and course timetable views, navigation, the seed, and the e2e test.\n   - None of the 25 planned CREATE files for those tasks exist.\n   - The planned edits to `student-tabs.ts`, `course-tabs.ts`, `navigation.ts`, `shell.tsx` and `seed.ts` were not made.\n   - `@dnd-kit/core` was added to `package.json` but is never imported.\n2. **The Dev artifacts are stale and do not describe this ticket.**\n   - `artifacts/dev/dev-log.md` and `task-completion-markers.json` are SH-4 (Notifications) files dated 2026-11-04. Their \"TASK-1..21 complete\" claims refer to PRD-04.\n   - No SH-6 dev log exists, but `dev-rerun-count.json` says `firstPassAccepted: true`. The pipeline accepted a Dev phase that never wrote its own outputs.\n3. **The backend that does exist is solid.**\n   - Covers TASK-1 to TASK-8: schema, migration, validators, clash engine, service, and 10 API routes.\n   - Contains real logic, with no stubs, TODO markers or console.log calls.\n   - Typecheck and lint pass.\n   - Passes 21 Dev unit tests and 16 new QA integration tests against real Postgres, including the NFR-1 concurrency guarantee.\n4. **The build is healthy, with no regressions.**\n   - `npm run typecheck` and `npm run lint` are both clean.\n   - `vitest run` shows 3 failing files. They are the same 3 failures recorded before this ticket (`DataTable` MUI X exports, `lockout` next-auth import, `useToast` timer), and none of them touch SH-6 code.\n\n## Requirement Results\n\n| Requirement | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | PASS | prisma/schema.prisma (`enum PeriodKind`, `model Period`); migration 20261105000000_timetable; used by tests/integration/timetable-concurrency.test.ts |\n| FR-2 | PASS | `model SchoolDay` + migration; integration \"FR-7/FR-40\" test upserts and reads it |\n| FR-3 | PASS | `model TimetableSlot` with `@@unique([courseId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` and `@@index([academicYearId, dayOfWeek, periodId])` in migration.sql; course FK `ON DELETE CASCADE` |\n| FR-4 | PASS | One additive migration with no ALTERs to existing tables except new FKs; back-relations on Course, Period and Room (schema lines 219/280/418/459); `prisma migrate status` reports it as up to date |\n| FR-5 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | `src/app/(app)/admin/timetable/periods/page.tsx` and `BellScheduleEditor.tsx` are missing. Only the API exists. |\n| FR-6 | PASS | src/lib/validators/timetable.ts (`hhmm`, `periodSchema`); service `assertNoOverlap`; tests/unit/timetable-time.test.ts (periodsOverlap, periodSchema) |\n| FR-7 | FAIL | The backend works: `updateSchoolDays` cascade-deletes slots and returns the count (integration \"FR-7/FR-40\"). The ToggleButton editor and the confirmation dialog are missing. |\n| FR-8 | PASS | `deletePeriod` throws CONFLICT with `details.slotCount`; integration \"FR-8\" |\n| FR-9 | PASS | clash-rules.ts TEACHER rule; unit (main and co-teacher, both directions); integration \"FR-9/FR-10\" (exact message) and \"co-teacher clash\" |\n| FR-10 | PASS | ROOM rule; unit; integration exact message `Clash: QA6-R1 is used by QA6-MATH-7A on Monday, QA6-P1.` |\n| FR-11 | PASS | SECTION rule; unit; integration \"FR-11\" exact message |\n| FR-12 | PASS | `overlapByCourse` (ACTIVE only); integration \"FR-12\" (a DROPPED enrollment is excluded, count = 1) |\n| FR-13 | PASS | PERIOD_KIND / NON_TEACHING_DAY; unit; integration \"FR-13\" |\n| FR-14 | PASS | `validateSlot` returns every clash (integration gets TEACHER and ROOM together); PATCH excludes the moving slot (integration \"FR-14/FR-18\", unit \"excludes the moving slot\") |\n| FR-15 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | `src/app/(app)/admin/timetable/page.tsx` and `TimetableEditor.tsx` are missing |\n| FR-16 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | `src/components/TimetableGrid/` is missing |\n| FR-17 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | Editor is missing (POST /api/timetable/slots exists) |\n| FR-18 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | The UI drag, Delete key and confirmation are missing. The PATCH/DELETE service is tested in integration. |\n| FR-19 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | The red tint, icon and tooltip are missing. The availability API passes (see FR-36). |\n| FR-20 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | The snap-back and toast are missing |\n| FR-21 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | The room Popover is missing. `getFreeRooms` / GET /api/timetable/free-rooms is tested in integration \"FR-21\". |\n| FR-22 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | The keyboard \"Place course\" dialog is missing |\n| FR-23 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | `@dnd-kit/core` 6.3.1 is installed but imported nowhere in src/ |\n| FR-24 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | `src/app/(app)/timetable/page.tsx` and `PersonalTimetable.tsx` are missing. The data API passes (FR-38). |\n| FR-25 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | The child selector UI is missing. The server-side rule is tested (integration \"FR-38/FR-25\"). |\n| FR-26 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | The Week/Today toggle is missing. The `nowAndNext` helper exists and is unit-tested. |\n| FR-27 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | src/config/student-tabs.ts has no Timetable entry; `students/[id]/timetable/page.tsx` is missing |\n| FR-28 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | src/config/course-tabs.ts has no Schedule entry; `courses/[courseId]/schedule/page.tsx` is missing |\n| FR-29 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | `PrintButton.tsx` and `TimetablePrintStyles.tsx` are missing |\n| FR-30 | PASS | `getScheduleForDate`; integration \"FR-30/FR-31/FR-45\" (ordered entries for teacher and student; Saturday returns []) |\n| FR-31 | PASS | `getCurrentSlot`; same test (inside the period → slot; at the exclusive end → null) |\n| FR-32 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | src/config/navigation.ts has no Timetable, Timetable editor or Bell schedule entries |\n| FR-33 | PASS | src/app/api/periods/{route,[id]/route,reorder/route}.ts: GET uses `requireUser`, writes use `requireRole('ADMIN')`. Handler wiring was checked by reading the code; the service is tested in integration. |\n| FR-34 | PASS | src/app/api/school-days/route.ts (GET `requireUser`, PUT `requireRole('ADMIN')`); service tested in integration \"FR-7/FR-40\" |\n| FR-35 | PASS | `assertCanViewTimetable`; integration \"FR-35\" covers ADMIN any view, TEACHER own view and homeroom section, and 403 for another teacher, another section and a STUDENT. Note: TEACHER can also view sections they teach a course in (design decision D8), which is broader than \"homeroom only\". |\n| FR-36 | PASS | `getAvailability`; integration \"FR-36\" (key `4-<periodId>` holds the exact clash message; free cells are absent) |\n| FR-37 | PASS | slots routes are ADMIN-only; integration \"FR-37/FR-40\" (academicYearId comes from the course) and \"FR-9/FR-10\" (CONFLICT with `details.clashes[]` and 0 rows saved) |\n| FR-38 | PASS | `resolvePersonalTarget`; integration \"FR-38/FR-25\". Minor: a multi-child parent with no `studentId` gets 400 VALIDATION_ERROR rather than 403. That is reasonable, but it differs from the spec wording. |\n| FR-39 | PASS | src/lib/validators/timetable.ts holds every schema and is imported by all 10 handlers; unit \"periodSchema\" tests |\n| FR-40 | PASS | `audit()` calls in every write; integration checks the slot create, update and delete rows and `schoolDay.update` with `deletedSlotCount`. Period create, update, delete and reorder audits were checked by reading the code only. |\n| FR-41 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | prisma/seed.ts seeds no periods; `prisma/seed-timetable-week.ts` is missing |\n| FR-42 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | No SchoolDay seed (the dev DB has 0 SchoolDay rows; the service defaults to Mon–Fri) |\n| FR-43 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | No 7A/7B week seed |\n| FR-44 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | No Tom, Sam or Pat fixtures, sections or courses; the dev DB has 0 users |\n| FR-45 | PASS (server) | `schoolNow` + `schoolTimezone()`; unit tests across UTC, Los Angeles and Kolkata, including the date line; integration runs with SchoolSettings.timezone = Asia/Kolkata. The UI consumers do not exist yet (see FR-24 and FR-26). |\n| NFR-1 | PASS | `createSlot`/`moveSlot` use a SERIALIZABLE transaction and retry on P2034; integration \"NFR-1/NFR-12\" (exactly 1 of 2 concurrent inserts succeeds; the retry path ran) |\n| NFR-2 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | The editor does not exist, so the section-week load cannot be measured |\n| NFR-3 | PASS (indicative) | `getAvailability` runs a fixed number of queries. The whole 16-test integration suite, availability included, ran in about 400 ms on a small dataset. It was not measured at seed scale. |\n| NFR-4 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | There is no UI to check |\n| NFR-5 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | No UI was written, so there is no mui-mcp lookup trail |\n| NFR-6 | PASS | The only new dependency is `@dnd-kit/core` pinned at 6.3.1; `next lint` (no-restricted-imports) is clean |\n| NFR-7 | PASS (API) | All 10 handlers call `requireUser` or `requireRole` before the service runs, and per-entity checks run on the server (`assertCanViewTimetable`, `resolvePersonalTarget`). There are no server pages yet. |\n| NFR-8 | PASS | Handlers follow `withHandler` → `parseBody`/`parseQuery` (Zod) → service → `ok()`; CONFLICT is used for clashes and for period delete-with-slots |\n| NFR-9 | PASS | Reuses `http.ts`, `audit()` and `logger`; service at src/server/timetable/timetable-service.ts; no renames |\n| NFR-10 | PASS | `tsc --noEmit` and `next lint` are clean. `vitest run`: 133 pass, 1 fail, in the same 3 files that failed before SH-6, so nothing regressed. |\n| NFR-11 | PASS | tests/unit/timetable-clash.test.ts and tests/unit/timetable-time.test.ts (21/21) |\n| NFR-12 | PASS | tests/integration/timetable-concurrency.test.ts (written by QA) |\n| NFR-13 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | `tests/e2e/timetable.spec.ts` is missing, and there is no UI to drive |\n| NFR-14 | PASS | grep finds no `console.log` in any SH-6 file; the service uses `logger.warn` |\n| NFR-15 | PASS | No solver, multi-week cycle, substitute or holiday code; there is only a holiday hook comment in `getScheduleForDate` |\n| NFR-16 | NOT-IMPLEMENTED | There is no UI or print output to check |\n\n## Tests written by QA\n\n- `tests/integration/timetable-concurrency.test.ts` has 16 tests running against real Postgres.\n- It skips without `TEST_DATABASE_URL`.\n- Its fixtures are tagged `QA6-` / `@qa-sh6.test` and removed afterwards. The SchoolDay table and the school timezone are snapshotted and restored.\n- It passed 4 runs in a row, and the dev DB was left unchanged.\n\n## Recommendation\n\nSend SH-6 back to Dev to finish TASK-9 to TASK-16, starting with the TimetableGrid, then the editor, then the seed (FR-41 to FR-44), because the e2e test needs the seed. Dev also needs to write a real SH-6 `dev-log.md` and `task-completion-markers.json`. The backend is ready for the UI and does not need rework.\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01TFC9zBBzkQfn3JxS55bLkY","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
