{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkA7aCVqAzPukRUfUqSC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"QA for SH-1 failed. The ticket's own code is solid, but the app's existing Content Security Policy stops every page's JavaScript from running in a real browser, so none of the new auth pages work as shipped.\n\n**Verdict:** 47 of 49 requirements pass and 2 fail (NFR-5 and NFR-13). All 34 functional requirements pass, but the UI passes only with the CSP turned off in Playwright (`bypassCSP`).\n\n**Blockers that existed before SH-1:**\n1. **CSP:** `next.config.js` (from Oct 16) sets `script-src 'self'`, which blocks the inline scripts Next.js needs to start React. The pages render but nothing on them works. Forms then submit the browser's default way, which puts the email and password in the URL (`/login?email=…&password=…`). Fix it with a nonce-based policy in middleware, or by allowing inline scripts. Separately, add `method=\"post\"` to the auth forms so passwords can never end up in a URL.\n2. **`npm run test` won't start:** `vitest.config.ts` imports `vitest/config.js`, which doesn't exist in vitest 2.1.1. I ran the suite with `vitest.tmp.config.ts`, which is identical apart from that import: 188 passed, 3 failed.\n3. **`next build` fails:** the `@mui/x-data-grid` and `@mui/x-internals` versions don't match. The same error also hangs the dev server once any page using that data grid compiles (e.g. `/admin/email-log`).\n\n**Defect found in the app's code:**\n- **NFR-5, focus on the first invalid field:** this doesn't work on any form. The shared `TextFormField` attaches the form library's ref to the wrapper `<div>` instead of the `<input>`. The fix is one line: `inputRef={field.ref}` in `FormField.tsx`. I confirmed it in unit tests and in real Chromium, and left those two tests failing on purpose so the defect stays visible.\n\n**What passes:**\n- Typecheck and lint are clean.\n- Dev's tests: 11/11 integration tests against real Postgres when run on their own, and 5/5 in `auth.spec.ts`.\n- My tests: 27 of 29 pass; the 2 failures are the NFR-5 tests.\n- Sign-in takes 0.31–0.63s.\n- Dev changed exactly the 14 planned files and nothing else.\n\n**Dev phase records:** the Dev records under `artifacts/dev/` (dev log and task-completion markers) are left over from ticket SH-4. Nothing was written for SH-1, so I checked the code directly.\n\n**Tests I added:**\n- `tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx`\n- `tests/unit/public-routes.test.ts`\n- `tests/e2e/auth-qa.spec.ts`\n\nI also changed two locators in Dev's `tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts`. Once the page actually runs, Next adds an empty alert element, and the old locators matched it too.\n\n**Two flaky-test and environment notes:**\n- Dev's integration test \"rate limits after 10 attempts per IP\" times out in the full suite, though it passes on its own (3/3 runs). Its 10 slow password checks exceed the 5-second default timeout, so it needs a longer one.\n- Port 3000 has an old Next server from Oct 27 that returns 500 on every route. I left it running and used port 3100.\n\nI installed Playwright's Chromium into your browser cache. All test users I created have been removed.\n\nFiles are in `artifacts/qa/`:\n- `qa-report.md`\n- `coverage-report.md`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6235,"cache_read_input_tokens":129435,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6235},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"f52d74ab-5795-43ec-9250-cb726f8a81b9","uuid":"dfc40e68-19de-4949-841b-f12738c40dab","timestamp":"2026-11-05T17:15:07.255Z","request_id":"req_011CgkA7Zkhx9fbpxookNrUH"}
