r their own courses, and admins for any date. Future dates are refused on both client and server.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-9 | The register page /attendance/take/[courseId]?date=&periodId= lists ACTIVE enrolled students sorted by last name, with an avatar, the name and an exclusive MUI ToggleButtonGroup (P/A/L/E). Buttons are\nfunctionalRequirements FR-10 | The EXCUSED option is available only to ADMIN in this PRD. It is hidden or disabled for teachers and rejected server-side for non-admins.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-11 | A 'Mark all present' button sets every unselected student to PRESENT without overwriting existing selections.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-12 | Selecting L reveals a minutes-late input (default 5, valid range 1–240, required when LATE). Each row has an optional note (max 500 characters) behind a note icon.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-13 | The header shows live counters (Present · Absent · Late · Unmarked). Save stays disabled while any student is unmarked.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-14 | Save creates or updates the session and all records in one DB transaction. Editing an existing register shows who last changed it and when.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-15 | A daily homeroom register (sectionId + date, no period) can be read and saved by the section's homeroom teacher and by admins. Its roster is the section members.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-16 | The daily register page route and UI. The PRD names only the course register route, so the daily register is assumed to reuse the same register component at a section-scoped route (e.g. /attendance/ta\nfunctionalRequirements FR-17 | Mobile layout: works one-handed at 360 px width, rows at least 48 px tall, toggle buttons at least 44×44 px, and a sticky save bar (MUI Paper, position: sticky) at the bottom.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-18 | Every status change to an existing record writes an audit() entry 'attendance.record.update' with the old status, the new status, the actor and the note.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-19 | Edit window: teachers can edit their own course records until 14 days after the register date. After that only admins can edit, and others see the register read-only with an explanation. This is enfor\nfunctionalRequirements FR-20 | Register notification types 'attendance.absent' (category ATTENDANCE, default email true, mandatoryInApp true, roles PARENT and STUDENT) and 'attendance.late' (default email false) in src/server/notif\nfunctionalRequirements FR-21 | After the save transaction commits, call notifyStudentAndParents once for each student whose status changed to ABSENT or LATE compared with the previously saved value. Use title 'X was marked absent' \nfunctionalRequirements FR-22 | When a status changes from ABSENT to PRESENT on the same day, send 'attendance.corrected' (title 'Attendance corrected: X was present') to the same recipients. At most one absence notification per stu\nfunctionalRequirements FR-23 | Register the 'attendance.corrected' and 'attendance.register_missing' notification type keys. The PRD does not give their category, email default or roles, so these are assumed: corrected = ATTENDANCE\nfunctionalRequirements FR-24 | Register an 'Attendance' tab in src/config/student-tabs.ts at /students/[studentId]/attendance, visible to every role that can view the student.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-25 | The student Attendance tab shows summary cards for the current term and the year (attendance rate %, absent count, late count, excused count).\nfunctionalRequirements FR-26 | The tab shows a read-only month calendar built with MUI X DateCalendar and a custom 'day' slot coloured success (all present), warning (any late), error (any absent) or default (no data), with a Toolt\nfunctionalRequirements FR-27 | The tab has a filterable table of records (date, period, course, status, minutes late, note). Notes are visible only to ADMIN and TEACHER and are stripped from the API response for STUDENT and PARENT.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-28 | Attendance rate = (PRESENT + LATE + EXCUSED) / total marked records × 100, rounded to one decimal place. Records from DROPPED enrollments still count. Per-period records are used when the mode is PER_\nfunctionalRequirements FR-29 | Register an 'Attendance' tab in src/config/course-tabs.ts (TEACHER and ADMIN) showing a DataGrid matrix: students as rows, the last 20 session dates as horizontally scrollable columns, coloured P/A/L/\nfunctionalRequirements FR-30 | /admin/attendance Today overview shows sessions expected vs taken today and the school-wide rate today.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-31 | It lists 'Missing registers' (meetings with no register 15 minutes after period start, in the school timezone), each with a 'Remind teacher' button that POSTs to /api/admin/attendance/remind and sends\nfunctionalRequirements FR-32 | The report builder filters by date range (max 366 days), grade level, section, course and status, and shows a per-student summary (records, present, absent, late, excused, rate). CSV export with the s\nfunctionalRequirements FR-33 | The 'Below threshold' view lists students whose year-to-date rate is below SchoolSettings.attendanceAlertThreshold (default 90), sorted ascending, each linked to the student page.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-34 | Add navigation entries: 'Attendance' for TEACHER (to /attendance/take) and 'Attendance' for ADMIN in the main group (to /admin/attendance). Students and parents use the student-page tab.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-35 | API routes: GET /api/attendance/today; GET and PUT /api/attendance/register (course or section variant); GET /api/students/:id/attendance?from=&to=; GET /api/courses/:id/attendance; GET /api/admin/att\nfunctionalRequirements FR-36 | Zod validators live in src/lib/validators/attendance.ts and are shared by the register form and the API handlers (PUT body, query params, report filters).\nfunctionalRequirements FR-37 | The attendance service lives at src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts, following the PRD-05 feature-subdirectory precedent.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-38 | Seed: attendance sessions for 7A and 7B covering the 15 teaching days before the seed run date. Use a fixed RNG seed and roughly 94% present, 3% late and 3% absent, with two Grade 7 students deliberat\nfunctionalRequirements FR-39 | Unit tests: rate calculation, the edit-window rule, and change detection for notifications (no duplicate on re-save).\nfunctionalRequirements FR-40 | Integration tests: the register save transaction, enrollment validation, and the partial unique indexes.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-41 | Playwright tests: the take-attendance flow on a mobile viewport (375 px), and a parent seeing the notification and the absence on the attendance calendar.\nnonFunctionalRequirements NFR-1 | Saving a 35-student register completes in under 500 ms. A student's yearly attendance tab loads in under 400 ms with 1,200 records.\nnonFunctionalRequirements NFR-2 | If saving fails because of a network error, unsaved marks persist in localStorage keyed by course or section, date and period, and the next open offers 'Restore unsaved attendance'.\nnonFunctionalRequirements NFR-3 | Records may only be saved for students with an ACTIVE enrollment on that date (or section members for daily registers). Others are rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR (400).\nnonFunctionalRequirements NFR-4 | A teacher can take attendance for a 30-student class in under 30 seconds on a phone.\nnonFunctionalRequirements NFR-5 | Parents receive absence notifications within 5 minutes. In-app notifications are immediate, and the email is queued in EmailOutbox.\nnonFunctionalRequirements NFR-6 | UI component rule: build only with MUI (@mui/material, icons and the MUI X packages), looking up every component via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs for 9.5.0) before use. No banned libraries\nnonFunctionalRequirements NFR-7 | Access is enforced server-side in every handler and server page. Parents see only linked students, students see only themselves, teachers see their courses and homeroom sections, and admins see everyt\nnonFunctionalRequirements NFR-8 | Follow the platform conventions: response shapes and error codes, pagination (pageSize max 100), cuid IDs, @db.Date for date-only values, UTC storage with display in SchoolSettings.timezone, the logge\nnonFunctionalRequirements NFR-9 | Accessibility: toggle buttons have screen-reader labels, and touch targets are at least 44×44 px.\nnonFunctionalRequirements NFR-10 | Brownfield safety: reuse existing helpers, components and models, never rename routes or models, keep npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test green, and do not implement scope owned by PRD-1\nclarificationLog None |","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88405567-c8b9-4e5f-8912-47ba3c7edb01","uuid":"284bb70d-6074-4a2f-aa1b-fb3a7de6b61f","timestamp":"2026-11-06T06:06:20.116Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"Ticket SH-7: execute the qa phase (task qa-main). Read prior phase artifacts under artifacts/, follow qa.md, and write this phase's artifacts to artifacts/qa/.\nSH-7 dict_keys(['ticketId', 'timestamp', 'phase', 'version', 'prd', 'runMode', 'brownfieldFindings', 'functionalRequirements', 'nonFunctionalRequirements', 'overallConfidencePct', 'clarificationLog', 'status'])\nfunctionalRequirements FR-1 | Add the AttendanceStatus enum (PRESENT, ABSENT, LATE, EXCUSED) and the AttendanceSession and AttendanceRecord Prisma models exactly as specified, with @@unique([sessionId, studentId]) and @@index([stu\nfunctionalRequirements FR-2 | Exactly one of AttendanceSession.courseId or sectionId must be set. Enforce this in the service layer and with a raw SQL CHECK constraint in the migration.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-3 | Add two partial unique indexes in migration SQL: (courseId, date, periodId) WHERE courseId IS NOT NULL, and (sectionId, date) WHERE sectionId IS NOT NULL.\nfunctionalRequirements FR-4 | Add attendanceMode (PER_PERIOD default | DAILY_