{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BosnkmBYE6DxGSJUp1LJjV","type":"tool_result","content":"# Dev Log — SH-7 (PRD-07 Attendance Tracking)\n\n> The previous content of this file was a stale SH-4 log. Per the dev-planning note\n> (\"Stale SH-1 artifacts under artifacts/dev/ must be regenerated, not reused\") it was\n> replaced. This is SH-7's first dev iteration.\n\n## Iteration 1 (2026-11-06)\n\nAll 19 tasks in `implementation-plan.json` were implemented in dependency order, at the exact paths in `file-ownership-matrix.json`. All 36 owned files exist.\n\n### Checklist\n- TASK-1: Prisma schema + attendance migration (CHECK + 2 partial unique indexes) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-2: Zod validators (src/lib/validators/attendance.ts) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-3: 4 attendance notification types — ✓ complete\n- TASK-4: Settings input + PATCH /api/settings/school — ✓ complete\n- TASK-5: Pure rules module + unit tests — ✓ complete\n- TASK-6: getSchoolScheduleForDate in the timetable service — ✓ complete\n- TASK-7: Attendance service — ✓ complete\n- TASK-8: Integration tests (attendance-service) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-9: Teacher API routes (today, register GET/PUT) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-10: Student/course attendance API routes — ✓ complete\n- TASK-11: Admin API routes (overview, report+CSV, below-threshold, remind) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-12: RegisterForm client component — ✓ complete\n- TASK-13: Take pages + DateNav — ✓ complete\n- TASK-14: Student Attendance tab — ✓ complete\n- TASK-15: Course Attendance tab (matrix) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-16: Admin attendance page (Today / Report / Below threshold / Settings) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-17: Tab + navigation config entries — ✓ complete\n- TASK-18: Seed attendance (mulberry32, idempotent) — ✓ complete\n- TASK-19: Playwright e2e at 375×667 — ✓ complete (file written and run; see verification for which assertions were proven)\n\n### Implementation notes\n- **Migration (TASK-1).** Generated with `prisma migrate diff --from-schema-datasource --to-schema-datamodel`, the equivalent of `--create-only` with no shadow DB. The diff is additive only. The CHECK constraint and the two partial unique indexes were then appended by hand. Applied to the local DB with `migrate deploy`.\n- **Service, outside Next (TASK-7).** The service does not import `services/settings.ts`, because its `react.cache` is undefined outside Next (the same pattern as the timetable service). It reads the settings row directly instead.\n- **Service, saving a register.** `saveRegister` runs one interactive transaction:\n  - It checks the active-on-date roster (`invalidStudentIds`) and requires the full roster (`missingStudentIds`).\n  - It does find-or-create of the session, then the diff writes.\n  - A P2002 error aborts a Postgres transaction, so a re-read inside the same transaction is impossible. The P2002 race (ADR-3) is therefore handled by re-running the transaction once; the retry's `findFirst` sees the winning session.\n  - Audit and notifications run after commit.\n- **Service, enrollment dates.** Enrollment dates for the active-on-date rule are compared at the start of the next day in the school timezone (`fromZonedTime`).\n- **`getToday` date parameter.** `getToday` takes an optional `date` so the landing page's DatePicker works. `/api/attendance/today` still uses today, matching the contract.\n- **Report and below-threshold pagination.** Both group the rows in SQL (`groupBy`), then paginate in memory. This is marked with a `ponytail:` comment; its ceiling is the student count.\n- **Tooltip accessibility.** The calendar day Tooltip uses `describeChild`. Without it, MUI sets the tooltip text as the day button's aria-label, which hides the day number from assistive tech.\n- **NFR-6.** Before the UI work (TASK-12 to TASK-16), mui-mcp was reached:\n  - `useMuiDocs` for `@mui/material@9.5.0` and `@mui/x-date-pickers`.\n  - `fetchDocs` for ToggleButtonGroup, ToggleButton, Tabs and DateCalendar (the custom `day` slot).\n  - The v9 upgrade guide was also read.\n  - The code follows the v9 rules from those docs: no system props, `slotProps.htmlInput`/`inputLabel`, `Tab` only inside `Tabs`, and `PickerDay` (v9) as the day slot.\n- **Seed (TASK-18).** The dev DB and the existing seed have **no sections, courses, periods or timetable slots**. They come from other PRDs' data. So the seed skips attendance with a log line instead of inventing 7A/7B (scope rule 5).\n  - I verified the generation path with a temporary 7A course, slots and enrollments, removed afterwards.\n  - Result: 15 sessions over 15 teaching days. Running it twice gives identical rows, so it is idempotent and deterministic.\n  - The first version left the forced students at 86.7%. Now they are deterministic: absent every 4th day, which gives 73%, always below 85%.\n\n### Verification\n- `tsc --noEmit`: clean. `eslint` on every SH-7 file: clean.\n- `tests/unit/attendance-rules.test.ts`: 13/13 pass. They cover:\n  - 14/15-day edges, future dates and the school-tz `schoolToday`.\n  - Diff and notifications: re-save with no change, ABSENT→PRESENT corrected, minutes-only edits.\n  - Rate, day colour and validators.\n- `tests/integration/attendance-service.test.ts` against the local migrated DB (`TEST_DATABASE_URL`): 7/7 pass. They cover:\n  - NFR-3 roster rejection (enrolled-after and dropped students), incomplete roster, and atomic save (no session row).\n  - EXCUSED refused for a teacher; non-owner teacher refused.\n  - Transition-only notifications (student + parent) and the audit count.\n  - Edit window: 403 at 15 days and 400 for a future date.\n  - Homeroom-only daily register.\n  - The CHECK constraint (both and neither), and P2002 on both partial indexes.\n  - Fixtures are cleaned up: 0 rows left.\n- Full vitest (with `vitest.tmp.config.ts`, see blockers): 209/211 tests pass. 4 files fail, and none of them import SH-7 code:\n  - `DataTable.test.tsx` and `lockout.test.ts` fail to load (module resolution).\n  - One test in each of `auth-forms` and `useToast` fails.\n- E2E `tests/e2e/attendance.spec.ts`, run against `next dev` on :3100:\n  - **Teacher test passes.** It covers mark all present, one absent, one late (default 5 min), E disabled for a teacher, Save, the toast and \"Last changed by\".\n  - **Parent test, partly proven.** The parent's `/notifications` assertion (\"Alex Absent was marked absent\") passed.\n  - **Not proven: the red-day calendar assertion.** `/students/[id]/attendance` 500s because of the pre-existing DataGrid package break (blocker 2).\n\n### Blockers / notes for QA (pre-existing, outside SH-7 file ownership — not changed)\n1. **CSP blocks hydration.** This is QA blocker 1 from the earlier QA report. `next.config.js` sends `script-src 'self'`, which blocks Next's inline scripts, so no client UI hydrates in a real browser. The e2e uses `bypassCSP: true`, with a comment, the same as earlier QA.\n2. **MUI X packages are out of sync.** Installed `@mui/x-internals` is 9.15.0, but `@mui/x-data-grid` 9.5.0 imports `@mui/x-internals/useFirstRender`, which 9.15 no longer exports. As a result, **every page that renders DataGrid/DataTable fails to compile**:\n   - SH-7: the student Attendance tab, the course Attendance matrix and the admin Report tab.\n   - Pre-existing: `/admin/email-log`, `tests/unit/DataTable.test.tsx`.\n   - I tried `x-internals@9.14.0` (`--no-save`). That only moves the error to `@mui/x-virtualizer` 9.0.0-alpha.8, which wants `isFirefox` from `x-internals/platform`.\n   - I restored 9.15.0; `package-lock.json` is unchanged. A proper fix is to align the MUI X versions in package.json/lockfile, which is a dependency change outside this ticket.\n3. **vitest config.** `vitest.config.ts` imports `vitest/config.js`, which doesn't resolve, so `npm test` fails to start. `vitest.tmp.config.ts` (same config, `vitest/config`) works.\n4. **No 7A/7B data.** There is no seed or dev data for sections, courses or the timetable, so the attendance seed is a no-op on this DB until PRD-05/06 data exists. The e2e creates its own fixtures, so it doesn't depend on that data.\n5. **Student tabs are never rendered.** `studentTabs` is not rendered by any page; it is an extension point only. The Attendance entry is registered, but the student pages have no tab bar to show it. Not in this ticket's scope.\n6. **Unrelated server on :3000.** A stale `next dev` from 2026-10-27 is running on :3000. I did not touch it. All runs used :3100.\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-7\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T11:30:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"dev\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"completed\": [\n    \"TASK-1\",\n    \"TASK-2\",\n    \"TASK-3\",\n    \"TASK-4\",\n    \"TASK-5\",\n    \"TASK-6\",\n    \"TASK-7\",\n    \"TASK-8\",\n    \"TASK-9\",\n    \"TASK-10\",\n    \"TASK-11\",\n    \"TASK-12\",\n    \"TASK-13\",\n    \"TASK-14\",\n    \"TASK-15\",\n    \"TASK-16\",\n    \"TASK-17\",\n    \"TASK-18\",\n    \"TASK-19\"\n  ]\n}\n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-7\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-06T06:05:50.649Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"dev\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"count\": 1,\n  \"firstPassAccepted\": true\n}Ticket SH-7: execute the dev phase (task dev-main). Read prior phase artifacts under artifacts/, follow dev.md, and write this phase's artifacts to artifacts/dev/.","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88405567-c8b9-4e5f-8912-47ba3c7edb01","uuid":"4720d0ba-e95d-438d-b1d5-594e595eb5a9","timestamp":"2026-11-06T06:06:23.151Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# Dev Log — SH-7 (PRD-07 Attendance Tracking)\n\n> The previous content of this file was a stale SH-4 log. Per the dev-planning note\n> (\"Stale SH-1 artifacts under artifacts/dev/ must be regenerated, not reused\") it was\n> replaced. This is SH-7's first dev iteration.\n\n## Iteration 1 (2026-11-06)\n\nAll 19 tasks in `implementation-plan.json` were implemented in dependency order, at the exact paths in `file-ownership-matrix.json`. All 36 owned files exist.\n\n### Checklist\n