{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013n1e2xNRLdfPzoH5PHkXiZ","type":"tool_result","content":"FR-1 Add the AttendanceStatus enum (PRESENT, ABSENT, LATE, EXCUSED) and the AttendanceSession and AttendanceRecord Prisma models exactly as specified, with @@unique([sessionId, studentId]) and @@index([studentId, createdAt]) on records. | AC: None \n\nFR-2 Exactly one of AttendanceSession.courseId or sectionId must be set. Enforce this in the service layer and with a raw SQL CHECK constraint in the migration. | AC: None \n\nFR-3 Add two partial unique indexes in migration SQL: (courseId, date, periodId) WHERE courseId IS NOT NULL, and (sectionId, date) WHERE sectionId IS NOT NULL. | AC: None \n\nFR-4 Add attendanceMode (PER_PERIOD default | DAILY_HOMEROOM | BOTH) and attendanceAlertThreshold (default 90) to SchoolSettings. | AC: None \n\nFR-5 Admins can edit attendanceMode (and attendanceAlertThreshold) on the school settings page. No such page or API route exists today, so the Architect must choose the smallest admin UI and API that satisfies this. | AC: None \n\nFR-6 /attendance/take shows the teacher's schedule for today (via getScheduleForDate), with each meeting's status ('Not taken' / 'Taken HH:mm by <name>'), and highlights the current period's meeting with a primary 'Take attendance' button. | AC: None \n\nFR-7 When attendanceMode includes daily registers, homeroom teachers also see a 'Daily register – <section>' entry on the landing page. | AC: None \n\nFR-8 A date picker lets teachers open a register for any date in the past 14 days for their own courses, and admins for any date. Future dates are refused on both client and server. | AC: None \n\nFR-9 The register page /attendance/take/[courseId]?date=&periodId= lists ACTIVE enrolled students sorted by last name, with an avatar, the name and an exclusive MUI ToggleButtonGroup (P/A/L/E). Buttons are coloured via the theme palette and have screen-reader labels. Nothing is selected by default for a new register. | AC: None \n\nFR-10 The EXCUSED option is available only to ADMIN in this PRD. It is hidden or disabled for teachers and rejected server-side for non-admins. | AC: None \n\nFR-11 A 'Mark all present' button sets every unselected student to PRESENT without overwriting existing selections. | AC: None \n\nFR-12 Selecting L reveals a minutes-late input (default 5, valid range 1–240, required when LATE). Each row has an optional note (max 500 characters) behind a note icon. | AC: None \n\nFR-13 The header shows live counters (Present · Absent · Late · Unmarked). Save stays disabled while any student is unmarked. | AC: None \n\nFR-14 Save creates or updates the session and all records in one DB transaction. Editing an existing register shows who last changed it and when. | AC: None \n\nFR-15 A daily homeroom register (sectionId + date, no period) can be read and saved by the section's homeroom teacher and by admins. Its roster is the section members. | AC: None \n\nFR-16 The daily register page route and UI. The PRD names only the course register route, so the daily register is assumed to reuse the same register component at a section-scoped route (e.g. /attendance/take/section/[sectionId]?date=). | AC: None \n\nFR-17 Mobile layout: works one-handed at 360 px width, rows at least 48 px tall, toggle buttons at least 44×44 px, and a sticky save bar (MUI Paper, position: sticky) at the bottom. | AC: None \n\nFR-18 Every status change to an existing record writes an audit() entry 'attendance.record.update' with the old status, the new status, the actor and the note. | AC: None \n\nFR-19 Edit window: teachers can edit their own course records until 14 days after the register date. After that only admins can edit, and others see the register read-only with an explanation. This is enforced server-side. | AC: None \n\nFR-20 Register notification types 'attendance.absent' (category ATTENDANCE, default email true, mandatoryInApp true, roles PARENT and STUDENT) and 'attendance.late' (default email false) in src/server/notifications/types.ts. | AC: None \n\nFR-21 After the save transaction commits, call notifyStudentAndParents once for each student whose status changed to ABSENT or LATE compared with the previously saved value. Use title 'X was marked absent' / 'X was marked late (N min)', body '<Course> – <Section>, <Period>, <Weekday d MMM yyyy>' and link /students/<id>/attendance. | AC: None \n\nFR-22 When a status changes from ABSENT to PRESENT on the same day, send 'attendance.corrected' (title 'Attendance corrected: X was present') to the same recipients. At most one absence notification per student per session, so re-saving never sends a duplicate. | AC: None \n\nFR-23 Register the 'attendance.corrected' and 'attendance.register_missing' notification type keys. The PRD does not give their category, email default or roles, so these are assumed: corrected = ATTENDANCE, PARENT+STUDENT, email false; register_missing = ATTENDANCE, TEACHER, email false. | AC: None \n\nFR-24 Register an 'Attendance' tab in src/config/student-tabs.ts at /students/[studentId]/attendance, visible to every role that can view the student. | AC: None \n\nFR-25 The student Attendance tab shows summary cards for the current term and the year (attendance rate %, absent count, late count, excused count). | AC: None \n\nFR-26 The tab shows a read-only month calendar built with MUI X DateCalendar and a custom 'day' slot coloured success (all present), warning (any late), error (any absent) or default (no data), with a Tooltip summary and month navigation. | AC: None \n\nFR-27 The tab has a filterable table of records (date, period, course, status, minutes late, note). Notes are visible only to ADMIN and TEACHER and are stripped from the API response for STUDENT and PARENT. | AC: None \n\nFR-28 Attendance rate = (PRESENT + LATE + EXCUSED) / total marked records × 100, rounded to one decimal place. Records from DROPPED enrollments still count. Per-period records are used when the mode is PER_PERIOD or BOTH, and daily records when it is DAILY_HOMEROOM. | AC: None \n\nFR-29 Register an 'Attendance' tab in src/config/course-tabs.ts (TEACHER and ADMIN) showing a DataGrid matrix: students as rows, the last 20 session dates as horizontally scrollable columns, coloured P/A/L/E cells and a per-student rate column. Clicking a column header opens that register. | AC: None \n\nFR-30 /admin/attendance Today overview shows sessions expected vs taken today and the school-wide rate today. | AC: None \n\nFR-31 It lists 'Missing registers' (meetings with no register 15 minutes after period start, in the school timezone), each with a 'Remind teacher' button that POSTs to /api/admin/attendance/remind and sends 'attendance.register_missing' to the teacher. | AC: None \n\nFR-32 The report builder filters by date range (max 366 days), grade level, section, course and status, and shows a per-student summary (records, present, absent, late, excused, rate). CSV export with the same columns comes from ?format=csv. | AC: None \n\nFR-33 The 'Below threshold' view lists students whose year-to-date rate is below SchoolSettings.attendanceAlertThreshold (default 90), sorted ascending, each linked to the student page. | AC: None \n\nFR-34 Add navigation entries: 'Attendance' for TEACHER (to /attendance/take) and 'Attendance' for ADMIN in the main group (to /admin/attendance). Students and parents use the student-page tab. | AC: None \n\nFR-35 API routes: GET /api/attendance/today; GET and PUT /api/attendance/register (course or section variant); GET /api/students/:id/attendance?from=&to=; GET /api/courses/:id/attendance; GET /api/admin/attendance/overview?date=; GET /api/admin/attendance/report (?format=csv); GET /api/admin/attendance/below-threshold; POST /api/admin/attendance/remind. Each route uses the role or access check listed in the API table. | AC: None \n\nFR-36 Zod validators live in src/lib/validators/attendance.ts and are shared by the register form and the API handlers (PUT body, query params, report filters). | AC: None \n\nFR-37 The attendance service lives at src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts, following the PRD-05 feature-subdirectory precedent. | AC: None \n\nFR-38 Seed: attendance sessions for 7A and 7B covering the 15 teaching days before the seed run date. Use a fixed RNG seed and roughly 94% present, 3% late and 3% absent, with two Grade 7 students deliberately below 85%. | AC: None \n\nFR-39 Unit tests: rate calculation, the edit-window rule, and change detection for notifications (no duplicate on re-save). | AC: None \n\nFR-40 Integration tests: the register save transaction, enrollment validation, and the partial unique indexes. | AC: None \n\nFR-41 Playwright tests: the take-attendance flow on a mobile viewport (375 px), and a parent seeing the notification and the absence on the attendance calendar. | AC: None \n\nNFR-1 Saving a 35-student register completes in under 500 ms. A student's yearly attendance tab loads in under 400 ms with 1,200 records. | AC: None \n\nNFR-2 If saving fails because of a network error, unsaved marks persist in localStorage keyed by course or section, date and period, and the next open offers 'Restore unsaved attendance'. | AC: None \n\nNFR-3 Records may only be saved for students with an ACTIVE enrollment on that date (or section members for daily registers). Others are rejected with VALIDATION_ERROR (400). | AC: None \n\nNFR-4 A teacher can take attendance for a 30-student class in under 30 seconds on a phone. | AC: None \n\nNFR-5 Parents receive absence notifications within 5 minutes. In-app notifications are immediate, and the email is queued in EmailOutbox. | AC: None \n\nNFR-6 UI component rule: build only with MUI (@mui/material, icons and the MUI X packages), looking up every component via the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs/fetchDocs for 9.5.0) before use. No banned libraries are allowed. An unreachable MCP server is a hard blocker. QA verifies there are no banned imports and that every MUI import is documented. | AC: None \n\nNFR-7 Access is enforced server-side in every handler and server page. Parents see only linked students, students see only themselves, teachers see their courses and homeroom sections, and admins see everything. | AC: None \n\nNFR-8 Follow the platform conventions: response shapes and error codes, pagination (pageSize max 100), cuid IDs, @db.Date for date-only values, UTC storage with display in SchoolSettings.timezone, the logger instead of console.log, and audit() for mutations to records owned by others. | AC: None \n\nNFR-9 Accessibility: toggle buttons have screen-reader labels, and touch targets are at least 44×44 px. | AC: None \n\nNFR-10 Brownfield safety: reuse existing helpers, components and models, never rename routes or models, keep npm run lint && npm run typecheck && npm run test green, and do not implement scope owned by PRD-14 (holidays) or PRD-15 (absence notes and the EXCUSED workflow). | AC: None","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88405567-c8b9-4e5f-8912-47ba3c7edb01","uuid":"b3f7fc6e-2b30-453e-9389-6d4e637988fd","timestamp":"2026-11-06T06:06:44.982Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"FR-1 Add the AttendanceStatus enum (PRESENT, ABSENT, LATE, EXCUSED) and the AttendanceSession and AttendanceRecord Prisma models exactly as specified, with @@unique([sessionId, studentId]) and @@index([studentId, createdAt]) on records. | AC: None \n\nFR-2 Exactly one of AttendanceSession.courseId or sectionId must be set. Enforce this in the service layer and with a raw SQL CHECK constraint in the migration. | AC: None \n\nFR-3 Add two partial unique indexes in migration SQL: (courseId, date, periodId) WHERE courseId IS NOT NULL, and (sectionId, date) WHERE sectionId IS NOT NULL. | AC: None \n\nFR-4 Add attendanceMode (PER_PERIOD default | DAILY_HOMEROOM | BOTH) and attendanceAlertThreshold (default 90) to SchoolSettings. | AC: None \n\nFR-5 Admin