{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VPgzYSsSgU1eP8oBy1hy9q","type":"tool_result","content":"11:SchoolHub is a single-school web platform for administrators, teachers, students and parents. It is built incrementally by a sequence of PRDs (PRD-00 … PRD-18). **When this PRD runs, every lower-numbered PRD is already implemented in the workspace.** Reuse existing models, services, components and helpers — never re-scaffold the project, never duplicate a helper that already exists, never renam\n68:Attendance is a legal record. It must be quick to take (a teacher has under a minute at the start of a class), editable for corrections with an audit trail, and visible to families on the same day. Chronic absence (below 90 % attendance) is an early-warning signal schools must act on.\n137:3. Register page (`/attendance/take/[courseId]?date=&periodId=`): list of ACTIVE enrolled students (sorted by last name) showing avatar and name, with an exclusive MUI `ToggleButtonGroup` per student: P / A / L / E (each `ToggleButton` coloured via the theme palette and labelled for screen readers) (EXCUSED available to ADMIN only in this PRD). Default for a new register: nothing selected.\n151:3. When a status changes from ABSENT to PRESENT within the same day, send `attendance.corrected` (title \"Attendance corrected: Sam Student was present\") to the same recipients. Do not send more than one absence notification per student per session.\n186:2. **Reliability:** if the network drops while saving, the register keeps the unsaved marks in `localStorage` keyed by course/date/period and offers \"Restore unsaved attendance\" on next open.\n193:3. Given Tom changes Sam from ABSENT to PRESENT the same day, then an `attendance.corrected` notification is sent and an audit entry records the old and new status.\n202:- Unit: rate calculation, edit-window rule, change detection for notifications (no duplicate on re-save).","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88405567-c8b9-4e5f-8912-47ba3c7edb01","uuid":"2e849524-8179-4e26-bd03-5ac844df9bc1","timestamp":"2026-11-06T06:06:51.778Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"11:SchoolHub is a single-school web platform for administrators, teachers, students and parents. It is built incrementally by a sequence of PRDs (PRD-00 … PRD-18). **When this PRD runs, every lower-numbered PRD is already implemented in the workspace.** Reuse existing models, services, components and helpers — never re-scaffold the project, never duplicate a helper that already exists, never renam\n68:Attendance is a legal record. It must be quick to take (a teacher has under a minute at the start of a class), editable for corrections with an audit trail, and visible to families on the same day. Chronic absence (below 90 % attendance) is an early-warning signal schools must act on.\n137:3. Register page (`/attendance/take/[courseId]?date=&periodId=`): list of ACTIVE enrolled students (sorted by last name) showing avatar and name, with an exclusive MUI `ToggleButtonGroup` per student: P / A / L / E (each `ToggleButton` coloured via the theme palette and labelled for screen readers) (EXCUSED available to ADMIN only in this PRD). Default for a new register: nothing selected.\n151:3. When a status changes from ABSENT to PRESENT within the same day, send `attendance.corrected` (title \"Attendance corrected: Sam Student was present\") to the same recipients. Do not send more than one absence notification per student per session.\n186:2. **Reliability:** if the network drops while saving, the register keeps the unsaved marks in `localStorage` keyed by course/date/period and offers \"Restore unsaved attendance\" on next open.\n193:3. Given Tom changes Sam from ABSENT to PRESENT the same day, then an `attendance.corrected` notification is sent and an audit entry records the old and new status.\n202:- Unit: rate calculation, edit-window rule, change detection for notifications (no duplicate on re-save).","stde