e (finding 1) |\n| FR-33 | FAIL | `getBelowThreshold` passes (ascending, href, threshold 90); the UI doesn't compile (finding 1) |\n| FR-34 | PASS | src/config/navigation.ts:34-35 |\n| FR-35 | PASS | All 9 routes exist under src/app/api/{attendance,students,courses,admin/attendance}. Role gates: `requireRole('TEACHER','ADMIN')` / `requireRole('ADMIN')`, plus service checks (`assertCanManageCourse`/`assertCanViewStudent`). Handlers are not unit-tested; the e2e covers PUT register. |\n| FR-36 | PASS | src/lib/validators/attendance.ts imported by RegisterForm.tsx:19 and every handler |\n| FR-37 | PASS | src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts |\n| FR-38 | PASS | prisma/seed.ts:165-261 (mulberry32(20261107), 15 teaching days, 94/3/3, two students forced to 73%). Code review only: this DB has no 7A/7B data, so the seed skips. |\n| FR-39 | PASS | tests/unit/attendance-rules.test.ts (13/13) |\n| FR-40 | PASS | tests/integration/attendance-service.test.ts (7/7) |\n| FR-41 | FAIL | tests/e2e/attendance.spec.ts: teacher flow at 375 px ✓, parent notification ✓, parent calendar red-day ✘ (finding 1) |\n| NFR-1 | PASS | attendance-qa.test.ts › NFR-1: save of 35 in 39–101 ms, tab with 1,200 records in 45–50 ms (local DB) |\n| NFR-2 | PASS | attendance-register-form.test.tsx › fetch rejects → localStorage `attendance-draft:c1:<date>:p1` → next open offers 'Restore unsaved attendance?' → marks restored |\n| NFR-3 | PASS | attendance-service.test.ts › enrolled-after and dropped students → VALIDATION_ERROR with `invalidStudentIds`; incomplete roster rejected |\n| NFR-4 | PASS | e2e teacher test: mark all + 2 exceptions + save in ~2 s; one tap per exception |\n| NFR-5 | PASS | attendance-qa.test.ts › in-app notification created synchronously after commit; EmailOutbox row queued for the parent |\n| NFR-6 | PASS | No banned imports (static scan above); tsc clean against @mui 9.5 types; dev-log lists the mui-mcp lookups (useMuiDocs 9.5.0, fetchDocs for ToggleButtonGroup/ToggleButton/Tabs/DateCalendar). Caveat: lookups aren't logged for every component used (Chip, Tooltip, DatePicker, DataGrid…). |\n| NFR-7 | PASS | attendance-qa.test.ts › unlinked parent and other student → NOT_FOUND (platform convention), linked parent OK; attendance-service.test.ts › non-owner/non-homeroom teacher FORBIDDEN |\n| NFR-8 | PASS | `@db.Date` DATE columns, cuid ids, `ok`/`paginated` envelopes, `parsePagination` (max 100), `audit()` on edits and reminders. Minor: prisma/seed.ts:205 uses `console.log` (seed script). |\n| NFR-9 | PASS | attendance-register-form.test.tsx › every toggle has an accessible name and is ≥44×44 px |\n| NFR-10 | FAIL | lint and typecheck are green; `npm run test` does not start (vitest.config.ts, from before SH-7). No PRD-14/15 scope was implemented. |\n\n## Other observations (not failing)\n\n- **NFR-2 restore.** \"Restore\" merges the whole saved draft into the current rows. If the roster changed since the draft was saved, the merge can bring back students who are no longer on the register, and the server then rejects the save with 400. A small fix: filter the draft to the current student ids.\n- **FR-9 avatars.** `avatarUrl` is always `null`, so `UserAvatar` shows initials. That is acceptable unless photos are expected.\n- **Admin page.** The admin page has a single static import chain. Lazy-loading ReportTab (`next/dynamic`) would keep the Today, Below-threshold and Settings tabs working even while DataGrid is broken.\n\n## New QA test files\n\n- `tests/integration/attendance-qa.test.ts`: 10 tests. The 2 that fail are intentional: they document defects FR-22 and FR-19.\n- `tests/unit/attendance-register-form.test.tsx`: 8 tests, all pass.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":129,"newStart":1,"newLines":121,"lines":["-# QA Report — SH-1 (PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC)","+# QA Report — SH-7 (PRD-07 Attendance Tracking)"," "," ## QA Summary"," ","-- ticketId: SH-1","-- timestamp: 2026-11-05T17:16:00Z","+- ticketId: SH-7","+- timestamp: 2026-11-06T12:35:00Z"," - overallStatus: FAIL","-- requirementsChecked: 49","-- requirementsPassed: 47","-- requirementsFailed: 2","+- requirementsChecked: 51","+- requirementsPassed: 38","+- requirementsFailed: 13"," ","+> This file replaces the stale SH-1 QA report.","+"," ## Headline findings"," ","-1. **BLOCKER (existed before SH-1, but every SH-1 page depends on it): the app's CSP stops React from hydrating, so no client UI works in a real browser.**","-   - `next.config.js` (dated Oct 16) sends `Content-Security-Policy: … script-src 'self'`.","-   - That policy blocks Next's inline `self.__next_f` scripts, plus `eval` in dev. In Chromium, `/login` was still not hydrated after 60s.","-   - Consequences:","-     - `/login`, `/forgot-password`, `/invite/[token]`, `/reset-password/[token]` and `/account/security` all render, but none of them work.","-     - Submitting a form falls back to a native **GET**, which puts credentials in the URL. For example: `/login?email=admin%40schoolhub.test&password=SchoolHub123%21` (seed creds).","-   - Every UI verdict below was proven with Playwright `bypassCSP: true`. That proves the SH-1 code is correct; it does **not** prove the shipped app works.","-   - Fix:","-     - Use a nonce-based CSP in middleware, or allow `'unsafe-inline'` for scripts (plus `'unsafe-eval'` in dev only).","-     - Also add `method=\"post\"` to the auth `<form>`s so a hydration failure can never leak passwords into URLs, logs or history.","-2. **FAIL NFR-5: focus does not move to the first invalid field.**","-   - The shared `TextFormField` (`src/components/FormField/FormField.tsx:39`) spreads `{...field}`. That puts RHF's `ref` on the TextField root `<div>` instead of the `<input>`, so neither `shouldFocusError` nor `setError(…, { shouldFocus })` can focus anything.","-   - Reproduced in jsdom (`tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx`) and in real Chromium (`tests/e2e/auth-qa.spec.ts` › NFR-5).","-   - One-line fix: pass `inputRef={field.ref}`, and keep `ref` out of the spread.","-   - This fixes every form in the app, not only the auth forms.","-3. **FAIL NFR-13: `npm run test` cannot start.**","-   - `vitest.config.ts` imports `vitest/config.js`, which doesn't exist in vitest 2.1.1. The file dates from 10:47 today, before SH-1's Dev run.","-   - `vitest.tmp.config.ts` is identical apart from the import, so QA ran the suite with it.","-   - The full suite then has 3 failing tests:","-     - `useToast` auto-hide: existed before SH-1.","-     - The QA NFR-5 test: the real defect in finding 2.","-     - The Dev integration test \"rate limits after 10 attempts per IP\": it times out at the 5s default under parallel load, because 10 × bcrypt-12 dummy compares run too long. It passes on its own (3/3 runs). Give it a `{ timeout: 20_000 }`.","-   - Two test files fail to load for reasons that existed before SH-1: `DataTable` (MUI X `useFirstRender` export) and `lockout` (`next/server` import).","-4. **`next build` fails, for a reason that existed before SH-1.**","-   - Cause: `@mui/x-data-grid` imports `@mui/x-internals/useFirstRender`, which that package doesn't export (a version mismatch).","-   - It also wedges `next dev` once any DataGrid page compiles. That page is `/admin/email-log`, so `notifications.spec.ts` could not run.","-   - SH-1 pages don't import DataGrid.","-5. **The Dev artifacts are stale.**","-   - `artifacts/dev/dev-log.md` and `task-completion-markers.json` are SH-4 files from 2026-11-04.","-   - There is no SH-1 dev log. Even so, `dev-rerun-count.json` says `firstPassAccepted: true`.","-   - QA therefore checked reality directly: all 14 files in `file-ownership-matrix.json` exist, they contain real implementations (no stubs, no TODOs), and no other file was modified.","-6. **The SH-1 code itself is solid.**","-   - Typecheck and lint are clean.","-   - Tests pass:","-     - Dev integration tests: 11/11 against real Postgres.","-     - Dev e2e `auth.spec.ts`: 5/5.","-     - QA tests: 27/29, and the 2 failures are the NFR-5 defect.","-   - Sign-in p95 is under 0.65s.","+1. **BLOCKER (dependency issue from before SH-7): every attendance page that uses DataGrid fails to compile, so 9 FRs don't work in the running app.**","+   - Root cause: `@mui/x-data-grid@9.5.0` imports `@mui/x-internals/useFirstRender`. The lockfile resolves `@mui/x-internals` to `9.15.0` (because x-data-grid allows `^9.1.0`), and 9.15.0 no longer exports that path.","+   - QA reproduced it two ways:","+     - `node -e \"import('@mui/x-data-grid')\"` fails with *\"Package subpath './useFirstRender' is not defined by exports\"*.","+     - `next dev` logs `⨯ ./node_modules/@mui/x-data-grid/DataGrid/useDataGridComponent.mjs`.","+   - Pages that fail:","+     - `/students/[id]/attendance` (StudentAttendanceClient → DataTable).","+     - `/courses/[id]/attendance` (CourseAttendanceMatrix).","+     - **all of** `/admin/attendance`, because AdminAttendanceClient imports ReportTab statically, and ReportTab imports DataGrid. That takes down the Settings, Today and Below-threshold tabs as well.","+   - The **service and API layer behind these pages is proven correct** by the integration tests below. Each FAIL verdict blocked by this issue says so.","+   - Fix (a dependency change, outside SH-7's file ownership): pin `@mui/x-internals` to a version that matches 9.5, or upgrade all `@mui/x-*` packages together.","+2. **FAIL FR-22: an absent → present → absent sequence sends a second absence notification for the same session.**","+   - `notificationsFor` only compares against the previous save. Re-saving with no change is handled correctly, but the PRD says *\"Do not send more than one absence notification per student per session.\"*","+   - Evidence: `tests/integration/attendance-qa.test.ts` › FR-22 (expected 1, got 2).","+   - Fix: inside the transaction, check for an existing `attendance.absent` notification for this student and session (or keep a per-record `absenceNotifiedAt`) before sending.","+3. **FAIL FR-19 (from the FR-10 check): once an admin marks any student EXCUSED, the teacher can no longer save that register.**","+   - `saveRegister` rejects any EXCUSED value in the body for non-admins (`attendance-service.ts:219`), even when the row is unchanged.","+   - The UI always sends the full roster, so a teacher's later correction to *another* student fails with 403. That breaks the teacher's 14-day edit right.","+   - Evidence: `tests/integration/attendance-qa.test.ts` › FR-10/FR-19 (got FORBIDDEN).","+   - Fix: reject only rows whose status is EXCUSED **and** differs from the saved value. Do the check on `diff` inside the transaction.","+4. **FAIL NFR-10: `npm run test` cannot start** (issue from before SH-7). `vitest.config.ts` imports `vitest/config.js`, which doesn't resolve. Every test in this report was run with `vitest.tmp.config.ts`, the same config with the `vitest/config` import.","+5. **Carried over: the CSP still blocks hydration** (`next.config.js` `script-src 'self'`). The e2e only works with `bypassCSP: true`. See SH-1 QA blocker 1."," ","-Also seen, outside SH-1's scope: the sidebar `<ul>` has `<a>` children (`ListItemButton component={Link}`), which is an axe `list` serious violation on signed-in pages. It only shows once the page hydrates. This is pre-existing shell nav code.","+## Test execution"," ","+| Suite | Command | Result |","+|---|---|---|","+| Typecheck | `npx tsc --noEmit` | clean |","+| Lint | `npm run lint` | ✔ no warnings/errors |","+| `npm run test` | — | **does not start** (finding 4) |","+| Full vitest | `TEST_DATABASE_URL=… npx vitest run -c vitest.tmp.config.ts` | 225/229 pass. Failures: 2 QA SH-7 defect tests, plus 2 older failures (`auth-forms`, `useToast`). 2 older files fail to load (`DataTable`, `lockout`). |","+| SH-7 unit | attendance-rules (13) + attendance-register-form (8, new) | 21/21 pass |","+| SH-7 integration | attendance-service (7) + attendance-qa (10, new) | 15/17 pass (FR-22 and FR-19 fail) |","+| E2E | `APP_URL=http://localhost:3100 npx playwright test tests/e2e/attendance.spec.ts` (next dev :3100) | teacher test ✓. Parent test: notification ✓ (2nd, warm run); calendar ✘ (page fails to compile) |","+| NFR-1 timing (local) | attendance-qa › NFR-1 | 35-student save **39–101 ms** (<500). 1,200-record tab **45–50 ms** (<400). |","+","+Static checks:","+- No banned or non-MUI UI libraries are imported in any SH-7 file. The only third-party imports are `@prisma/client`, `date-fns(-tz)`, `next/*`, `react` and `zod`, plus `@mui/*`.","+- No `console.*` calls in SH-7 `src/` files.","+"," ## Requirement Results"," "," | Requirement | Status | Evidence |"," |---|---|---|","-| FR-1 | PASS | prisma/schema.prisma (User/AuthToken/AuditLog, AuthToken.tokenHash @unique, onDelete Cascade); exercised by tests/integration/auth.test.ts |","-| FR-2 | PASS | src/app/(auth)/login/*; tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts \"admin signs in…\" (with CSP bypass; see blocker 1) |","-| FR-3 | PASS | src/server/auth/credentials.ts; tests/integration/auth.test.ts \"rejects DISABLED, archived and locked accounts\", \"rejects unknown email and wrong password with the same code\" |","-| FR-4 | PASS | LoginForm.tsx `loginErrorMessage`; tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts; tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts \"a wrong password shows the generic error\" |","-| FR-5 | PASS | tests/integration/auth.test.ts \"locks on the 5th failure…\" and \"success resets failedLoginCount, sets lastLoginAt…\" |","-| FR-6 | PASS | tests/integration/auth.test.ts \"rate limits after 10 attempts per IP\" (passes in isolation; full-suite timeout under NFR-13); tests/unit/rate-limit.test.ts; 429 copy in tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx |","-| FR-7 | PASS | tests/unit/auth-validators.test.ts `safeCallbackUrl`; tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts callbackUrl redirect |","-| FR-8 | PASS | tests/integration/auth.test.ts (auth.lockout and auth.login.success rows asserted); auth.login.failure in credentials.ts:43 (code-reviewed only, no test asserts the row) |","-| FR-9 | PASS | auth.config.ts:12 (maxAge 8h, updateAge 15m); the user menu shows the session name and role in tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts |","-| FR-10 | PASS | auth.ts:36-47 (authTime vs passwordChangedAt; `reauth` update); tests/integration/auth.test.ts \"success bumps passwordChangedAt\"; tests/e2e/auth-qa.spec.ts (current session survives reload after change). Logout of other devices is not e2e-tested. |","-| FR-11 | PASS | src/middleware.ts; tests/unit/public-routes.test.ts (QA); tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts redirect; curl /account/security → 307 /login?callbackUrl=%2Faccount%2Fsecurity |","-| FR-12 | PASS | src/server/auth/tokens.ts; tests/unit/tokens.test.ts; the invite/reset pages call verifyToken, and the APIs consume the token (integration \"token cannot be reused\") |","-| FR-13 | PASS | src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx; tests/e2e/auth-qa.spec.ts \"bogus invite token…\" and the read-only name/email; tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx |","-| FR-14 | PASS | tests/e2e/auth-qa.spec.ts \"invite accept → signed in on /dashboard; the link cannot be reused\" (DB: status ACTIVE, passwordChangedAt set); tests/integration/auth.test.ts acceptInvite |","-| FR-15 | PASS | src/lib/validators/auth.ts; tests/unit/password-policy.test.ts and auth-validators.test.ts; client rejection in tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx |","-| FR-16 | PASS | PasswordChecklist wired into SetPasswordForm (invite and reset) and ChangePasswordForm.tsx:70; asserted in tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx |","-| FR-17 | PASS | forgot-password/page.tsx + ForgotPasswordForm.tsx; tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx (same copy, 429); tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts; limits in services/auth.ts:42,46 (code-reviewed) |","-| FR-18 | PASS | tests/integration/auth.test.ts \"a known email gets a token and an outbox row; an unknown email gets neither\" |","-| FR-19 | PASS | reset-password/[token]/page.tsx; tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts forgot → reset → /login?reset=1 toast → sign in; tests/integration/auth.test.ts \"resetPassword clears lockout fields…\" |","-| FR-20 | PASS | account/security/*; tests/e2e/auth-qa.spec.ts (wrong current → field error; success → \"Password updated\"); tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx; api/account/password/route.ts re-issues the session through unstable_update |","-| FR-21 | PASS | shell.tsx:167-169; tests/e2e/auth-qa.spec.ts clicks the \"Account security\" menu item and lands on /account/security |","-| FR-22 | PASS | src/server/services/users.ts (createUser:118, setUserStatus:345, unlockUser:374, createInviteToken:383, sendInvite:392); verify-only, unchanged |","-| FR-23 | PASS | src/server/auth/requireRole.ts; used by (app)/layout.tsx and account/security/page.tsx; tests/unit/http.test.ts (error envelope) |","-| FR-24 | PASS | src/server/audit.ts; audit rows asserted in tests/integration/auth.test.ts |","-| FR-25 | PASS | `grep -rn PLACEHOLDER_USER src` → 0 matches; layout.tsx passes the requirePageUser() user to AppShell |","-| FR-26 | PASS | shell.tsx:162-176; tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts (name \"Alice Admin\", \"ADMIN\" chip, Sign out → /login) |","-| FR-27 | PASS | shell.tsx:74 `navigationForRole(user.role)` |","-| FR-28 | PASS | DB: 6 ACTIVE @schoolhub.test users; tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts signs in with `SchoolHub123!` |","-| FR-29 | PASS | DB: invited@schoolhub.test is INVITED; prisma/seed.ts:56 |","-| FR-30 | PASS | prisma/seed.ts:29,56 (createInviteToken + authLink via logger.info) |","-| FR-31 | PASS | tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts reads the reset link from EmailOutbox; tests/integration/auth.test.ts outbox row |","-| FR-32 | PASS | prisma/schema.prisma:176 `ip String?` (not renamed) |","-| FR-33 | PASS | prisma/migrations/20261106000000_user_role_status_index |","-| FR-34 | PASS | tests/integration/auth.test.ts (11 tests); tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts (5 tests); tests/e2e/helpers/auth.ts |","-| NFR-1 | PASS | tokens.ts:17 (sha256), :27 (32 bytes base64url), :56 (timingSafeEqual); tests/unit/tokens.test.ts |","-| NFR-2 | PASS | Observed `Set-Cookie: authjs.session-token=…; HttpOnly; SameSite=Lax` (Secure applies under https in Auth.js and could not be checked on localhost); a POST without csrfToken → `/login?error=MissingCSRF`. See blocker 1 for the GET credential leak. |","-| NFR-3 | PASS | credentials.ts:24,56 (DUMMY_HASH compare); integration \"same code for unknown email and wrong password\" |","-| NFR-4 | PASS | 6 sign-ins via /api/auth/callback/credentials on the local dev server took 0.31–0.63s (bcrypt 12) |","-| NFR-5 | **FAIL** | aria-live regions are present, but focus does not move: tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx \"blocks an invalid email client-side, focusing the field\" and tests/e2e/auth-qa.spec.ts \"…focuses the first invalid field\" both fail. Root cause: FormField.tsx:39 (see finding 2). |","-| NFR-6 | PASS | All SH-1 UI imports come from @mui/material and @mui/icons-material (typecheck clean); toasts go through useToast. Whether Dev consulted mui-mcp cannot be verified after the fact. |","-| NFR-7 | PASS | tests/unit/eslint-no-restricted-imports.test.ts (16 pass); grep for banned packages in src → 0 |","-| NFR-8 | PASS | tests/integration/auth.test.ts \"no audit metadata carries password or token keys or values\" |","-| NFR-9 | PASS | (app)/layout.tsx + account/security/page.tsx `requirePageUser`; api/account/password `requireUser`; unauthenticated curl → 307 |","-| NFR-10 | PASS | api/account/password/route.ts (parseBody → service → ok); tests/unit/http.test.ts |","-| NFR-11 | PASS | ForgotPasswordForm, SetPasswordForm and ChangePasswordForm use zodResolver with schemas from src/lib/validators/auth.ts, which the API routes also use |","-| NFR-12 | PASS | `grep -rn console.log src` → only inside src/lib/logger.ts |","-| NFR-13 | **FAIL** | Scope guard OK: only the 14 owned files changed, and course-access.ts and student-access.ts are untouched. Typecheck and lint pass. But `npm run test` cannot start (vitest.config.ts imports `vitest/config.js`), and the suite run with the identical config has 3 failing tests and 2 test files that won't load. The ones caused by SH-1 work are the rate-limit timeout and the NFR-5 defect; the rest existed before (finding 3). |","-| NFR-14 | PASS | tests/e2e/auth-qa.spec.ts (/signup, /sign-up, /register → /login); tests/unit/public-routes.test.ts |","-| NFR-15 | PASS | No browser-specific APIs in the SH-1 code. Only Chromium was executed; Firefox, WebKit and Edge were not run. |","+| FR-1 | PASS | prisma/schema.prisma; migrations/20261107000000_attendance/migration.sql:2,12-47 (enum, models, `sessionId_studentId` unique, `studentId_createdAt` index) |","+| FR-2 | PASS | migration.sql:73 CHECK; service builds course-xor-section keys (attendance-service.ts:247); attendance-service.test.ts › DB CHECK (both and neither rejected) |","+| FR-3 | PASS | migration.sql:77-78; attendance-service.test.ts › P2002 on both partial indexes |","+| FR-4 | PASS | migration.sql:8-9 (defaults PER_PERIOD / 90); attendance-qa.test.ts › FR-33 reads threshold 90 |","+| FR-5 | FAIL | `PATCH /api/settings/school` (src/app/api/settings/school/route.ts) and the Settings tab exist, but `/admin/attendance` doesn't compile (finding 1). The PATCH route also has no test. |","+| FR-6 | PASS | attendance-qa.test.ts › FR-6 (meeting listed, `taken:null`, `isCurrent`); take/page.tsx 'Taken HH:mm by' label + contained button for the current meeting |","+| FR-7 | PASS | attendance-service.ts:155-162 + take/page.tsx 'Daily register – <section>'. Code review only: no test, because the global mode is PER_PERIOD. |","+| FR-8 | PASS | attendance-rules.test.ts (14/15-day edges, future dates); attendance-service.test.ts › future → VALIDATION_ERROR, 15 days → FORBIDDEN, admin OK; DateNav.tsx disableFuture plus the same `canOpen` |","+| FR-9 | PASS | attendance-register-form.test.tsx › nothing selected by default, SR labels; attendance-service.test.ts › roster sorted by last name; e2e teacher test |","+| FR-10 | PASS | attendance-register-form.test.tsx › E disabled for a teacher, enabled for an admin; attendance-service.test.ts › teacher EXCUSED → FORBIDDEN. (The overly broad server check is reported under FR-19.) |","+| FR-11 | PASS | attendance-register-form.test.tsx › Mark all present keeps existing A |","+| FR-12 | PASS | attendance-register-form.test.tsx › L reveals minutes (default 5), 241 blocked, note behind icon, maxlength 500; validators.ts:40-48 |","+| FR-13 | PASS | attendance-register-form.test.tsx › live counters, Save disabled while unmarked; e2e |","+| FR-14 | PASS | attendance-service.test.ts › atomic save (no session row on failure), single session; register-form test + e2e › 'Last changed by' |","+| FR-15 | PASS | attendance-service.test.ts › homeroom teacher OK, other teacher FORBIDDEN; roster = sectionMember (service:97-99) |","+| FR-16 | PASS | src/app/(app)/attendance/take/section/[sectionId]/page.tsx reuses RegisterForm |","+| FR-17 | PASS | attendance-register-form.test.tsx › 44 px toggles and note button, sticky Paper; RegisterForm.tsx:182 minHeight 48; e2e at 375×667 |","+| FR-18 | PASS | attendance-service.test.ts › audit count; service:284-296 metadata {old,new,note}, actor |","+| FR-19 | FAIL | Window rule passes (attendance-service.test.ts). But attendance-qa.test.ts › FR-10/FR-19 shows a teacher can't save a register an admin has excused anyone on (finding 3). |","+| FR-20 | PASS | src/server/notifications/types.ts:61-76 |","+| FR-21 | PASS | attendance-qa.test.ts › title 'QA Aardvark was marked absent', body '<Course> – <Section>, <Period>, <Weekday d MMM yyyy>', link `/students/<id>/attendance`, parent + student |","+| FR-22 | FAIL | attendance-qa.test.ts › A→P→A sends 2 absence notifications (finding 2). Corrected and plain re-save work (attendance-service.test.ts). Also, \"within the same day\" is not enforced for `attendance.corrected`. |","+| FR-23 | PASS | types.ts:77-92; attendance-qa.test.ts › register_missing delivered to the teacher |","+| FR-24 | PASS | src/config/student-tabs.ts:13 (ALL_ROLES). Note: no page renders `studentTabs` yet (it is an extension point). |","+| FR-25 | FAIL | Service summary is correct (attendance-qa.test.ts › FR-28 summary.year). The tab page doesn't compile (finding 1). |","+| FR-26 | FAIL | `dayColour` is unit-tested; the e2e calendar assertion fails because the page doesn't compile (finding 1). |","+| FR-27 | FAIL | Notes are stripped for PARENT/STUDENT (attendance-qa.test.ts › FR-27), but the table page doesn't compile (finding 1). The table also has no filter controls beyond month navigation. |","+| FR-28 | PASS | attendance-rules.test.ts › rate; attendance-qa.test.ts › DROPPED records count (rate 0, records 1); `kindWhere` (service:52) picks session kind by mode |","+| FR-29 | FAIL | `getCourseMatrix` passes (attendance-qa.test.ts › dropped row, rate, oldest→newest sessions); CourseAttendanceMatrix doesn't compile (finding 1) |","+| FR-30 | FAIL | `getOverview` passes (attendance-qa.test.ts › FR-30/31); `/admin/attendance` doesn't compile (finding 1) |","+| FR-31 | FAIL | Missing-register list + `remindTeacher` pass (attendance-qa.test.ts); the admin UI with the Remind button doesn't compile (finding 1) |","+| FR-32 | FAIL | `getReport` aggregates and status filter pass, CSV via `toCsv` (attendance-qa.test.ts › FR-32); the ReportTab UI doesn't compile (finding 1) |","+| FR-33 | FAIL | `getBelowThreshold` passes (ascending, href, threshold 90); the UI doesn't compile (finding 1) |","+| FR-34 | PASS | src/config/navigation.ts:34-35 |","+| FR-35 | PASS | All 9 routes exist under src/app/api/{attendance,students,courses,admin/attendance}. Role gates: `requireRole('TEACHER','ADMIN')` / `requireRole('ADMIN')`, plus service checks (`assertCanManageCourse`/`assertCanViewStudent`). Handlers are not unit-tested; the e2e covers PUT register. |","+| FR-36 | PASS | src/lib/validators/attendance.ts imported by RegisterForm.tsx:19 and every handler |","+| FR-37 | PASS | src/server/attendance/attendance-service.ts |","+| FR-38 | PASS | prisma/seed.ts:165-261 (mulberry32(20261107), 15 teaching days, 94/3/3, two students forced to 73%). Code review only: this DB has no 7A/7B data, so the seed skips. |","+| FR-39 | PASS | tests/unit/attendance-rules.test.ts (13/13) |","+| FR-40 | PASS | tests/integration/attendance-service.test.ts (7/7) |","+| FR-41 | FAIL | tests/e2e/attendance.spec.ts: teacher flow at 375 px ✓, parent notification ✓, parent calendar red-day ✘ (finding 1) |","+| NFR-1 | PASS | attendance-qa.test.ts › NFR-1: save of 35 in 39–101 ms, tab with 1,200 records in 45–50 ms (local DB) |","+| NFR-2 | PASS | attendance-register-form.test.tsx › fetch rejects → localStorage `attendance-draft:c1:<date>:p1` → next open offers 'Restore unsaved attendance?' → marks restored |","+| NFR-3 | PASS | attendance-service.test.ts › enrolled-after and dropped students → VALIDATION_ERROR with `invalidStudentIds`; incomplete roster rejected |","+| NFR-4 | PASS | e2e teacher test: mark all + 2 exceptions + save in ~2 s; one tap per exception |","+| NFR-5 | PASS | attendance-qa.test.ts › in-app notification created synchronously after commit; EmailOutbox row queued for the parent |","+| NFR-6 | PASS | No banned imports (static scan above); tsc clean against @mui 9.5 types; dev-log lists the mui-mcp lookups (useMuiDocs 9.5.0, fetchDocs for ToggleButtonGroup/ToggleButton/Tabs/DateCalendar). Caveat: lookups aren't logged for every component used (Chip, Tooltip, DatePicker, DataGrid…). |","+| NFR-7 | PASS | attendance-qa.test.ts › unlinked parent and other student → NOT_FOUND (platform convention), linked parent OK; attendance-service.test.ts › non-owner/non-homeroom teacher FORBIDDEN |","+| NFR-8 | PASS | `@db.Date` DATE columns, cuid ids, `ok`/`paginated` envelopes, `parsePagination` (max 100), `audit()` on edits and reminders. Minor: prisma/seed.ts:205 uses `console.log` (seed script). |","+| NFR-9 | PASS | attendance-register-form.test.tsx › every toggle has an accessible name and is ≥44×44 px |","+| NFR-10 | FAIL | lint and typecheck are green; `npm run test` does not start (vitest.config.ts, from before SH-7). No PRD-14/15 scope was implemented. |"," ","-## How QA ran things","+## Other observations (not failing)"," ","-- `npm run typecheck` ✔ and `npm run lint` ✔.","-- `npm run test` ✘ (startup error). The suite was run with `TEST_DATABASE_URL=postgresql://schoolhub:schoolhub@localhost:5433/schoolhub?schema=public npx vitest run -c vitest.tmp.config.ts`: **188 passed, 3 failed** (191 tests across 22 files).","-- `npm run build` ✘: MUI X `useFirstRender` export mismatch (existed before SH-1).","-- E2E:","-  - Ran against `next dev -p 3100`. Port 3000 is a stale `next-server` from Oct 27 that returns 500 on every route; QA did not kill it.","-  - Ran with a throwaway Playwright config that set `use.bypassCSP: true`. That config has been deleted.","-  - Playwright chromium build 1134 was installed into the user cache.","-  - Results: `auth.spec.ts` 5/5, `dashboard.spec.ts` 2/2 (render), `auth-qa.spec.ts` 4/5 (NFR-5).","-  - Without the bypass, every interactive e2e test fails because of blocker 1.","-- All QA test users (`@qa-e2e.test`, `@auth-it.test`) were removed. Seed user student2 was restored by `auth.spec.ts` afterAll.","+- **NFR-2 restore.** \"Restore\" merges the whole saved draft into the current rows. If the roster changed since the draft was saved, the merge can bring back students who are no longer on the register, and the server then rejects the save with 400. A small fix: filter the draft to the current student ids.","+- **FR-9 avatars.** `avatarUrl` is always `null`, so `UserAvatar` shows initials. That is acceptable unless photos are expected.","+- **Admin page.** The admin page has a single static import chain. Lazy-loading ReportTab (`next/dynamic`) would keep the Today, Below-threshold and Settings tabs working even while DataGrid is broken."," ","-## Recommended fixes (in priority order)","+## New QA test files"," ","-1. Make the CSP compatible with Next hydration (nonce via middleware, or `'unsafe-inline'`), and add `method=\"post\"` to the auth forms.","-2. In `FormField.tsx`, pass `inputRef={field.ref}` (fixes NFR-5 everywhere).","-3. In `vitest.config.ts`, change the import from `'vitest/config.js'` to `'vitest/config'`, then delete `vitest.tmp.config.ts`.","-4. Give the rate-limit integration test a 20s timeout.","-5. Align the `@mui/x-*` versions so that `next build` succeeds.","-6. Have the Dev phase write an SH-1 dev-log and task-completion-markers.","+- `tests/integration/attendance-qa.test.ts`: 10 tests. The 2 that fail are intentional: they document defects FR-22 and FR-19.","+- `tests/unit/attendance-register-form.test.tsx`: 8 tests, all pass."]}],"originalFile":"# QA Report — SH-1 (PRD-01 Authentication, Sessions & RBAC)\n\n## QA Summary\n\n- ticketId: SH-1\n- timestamp: 2026-11-05T17:16:00Z\n- overallStatus: FAIL\n- requirementsChecked: 49\n- requirementsPassed: 47\n- requirementsFailed: 2\n\n## Headline findings\n\n1. **BLOCKER (existed before SH-1, but every SH-1 page depends on it): the app's CSP stops React from hydrating, so no client UI works in a real browser.**\n   - `next.config.js` (dated Oct 16) sends `Content-Security-Policy: … script-src 'self'`.\n   - That policy blocks Next's inline `self.__next_f` scripts, plus `eval` in dev. In Chromium, `/login` was still not hydrated after 60s.\n   - Consequences:\n     - `/login`, `/forgot-password`, `/invite/[token]`, `/reset-password/[token]` and `/account/security` all render, but none of them work.\n     - Submitting a form falls back to a native **GET**, which puts credentials in the URL. For example: `/login?email=admin%40schoolhub.test&password=SchoolHub123%21` (seed creds).\n   - Every UI verdict below was proven with Playwright `bypassCSP: true`. That proves the SH-1 code is correct; it does **not** prove the shipped app works.\n   - Fix:\n     - Use a nonce-based CSP in middleware, or allow `'unsafe-inline'` for scripts (plus `'unsafe-eval'` in dev only).\n     - Also add `method=\"post\"` to the auth `<form>`s so a hydration failure can never leak passwords into URLs, logs or history.\n2. **FAIL NFR-5: focus does not move to the first invalid field.**\n   - The shared `TextFormField` (`src/components/FormField/FormField.tsx:39`) spreads `{...field}`. That puts RHF's `ref` on the TextField root `<div>` instead of the `<input>`, so neither `shouldFocusError` nor `setError(…, { shouldFocus })` can focus anything.\n   - Reproduced in jsdom (`tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx`) and in real Chromium (`tests/e2e/auth-qa.spec.ts` › NFR-5).\n   - One-line fix: pass `inputRef={field.ref}`, and keep `ref` out of the spread.\n   - This fixes every form in the app, not only the auth forms.\n3. **FAIL NFR-13: `npm run test` cannot start.**\n   - `vitest.config.ts` imports `vitest/config.js`, which doesn't exist in vitest 2.1.1. The file dates from 10:47 today, before SH-1's Dev run.\n   - `vitest.tmp.config.ts` is identical apart from the import, so QA ran the suite with it.\n   - The full suite then has 3 failing tests:\n     - `useToast` auto-hide: existed before SH-1.\n     - The QA NFR-5 test: the real defect in finding 2.\n     - The Dev integration test \"rate limits after 10 attempts per IP\": it times out at the 5s default under parallel load, because 10 × bcrypt-12 dummy compares run too long. It passes on its own (3/3 runs). Give it a `{ timeout: 20_000 }`.\n   - Two test files fail to load for reasons that existed before SH-1: `DataTable` (MUI X `useFirstRender` export) and `lockout` (`next/server` import).\n4. **`next build` fails, for a reason that existed before SH-1.**\n   - Cause: `@mui/x-data-grid` imports `@mui/x-internals/useFirstRender`, which that package doesn't export (a version mismatch).\n   - It also wedges `next dev` once any DataGrid page compiles. That page is `/admin/email-log`, so `notifications.spec.ts` could not run.\n   - SH-1 pages don't import DataGrid.\n5. **The Dev artifacts are stale.**\n   - `artifacts/dev/dev-log.md` and `task-completion-markers.json` are SH-4 files from 2026-11-04.\n   - There is no SH-1 dev log. Even so, `dev-rerun-count.json` says `firstPassAccepted: true`.\n   - QA therefore checked reality directly: all 14 files in `file-ownership-matrix.json` exist, they contain real implementations (no stubs, no TODOs), and no other file was modified.\n6. **The SH-1 code itself is solid.**\n   - Typecheck and lint are clean.\n   - Tests pass:\n     - Dev integration tests: 11/11 against real Postgres.\n     - Dev e2e `auth.spec.ts`: 5/5.\n     - QA tests: 27/29, and the 2 failures are the NFR-5 defect.\n   - Sign-in p95 is under 0.65s.\n\nAlso seen, outside SH-1's scope: the sidebar `<ul>` has `<a>` children (`ListItemButton component={Link}`), which is an axe `list` serious violation on signed-in pages. It only shows once the page hydrates. This is pre-existing shell nav code.\n\n## Requirement Results\n\n| Requirement | Status | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| FR-1 | PASS | prisma/schema.prisma (User/AuthToken/AuditLog, AuthToken.tokenHash @unique, onDelete Cascade); exercised by tests/integration/auth.test.ts |\n| FR-2 | PASS | src/app/(auth)/login/*; tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts \"admin signs in…\" (with CSP bypass; see blocker 1) |\n| FR-3 | PASS | src/server/auth/credentials.ts; tests/integration/auth.test.ts \"rejects DISABLED, archived and locked accounts\", \"rejects unknown email and wrong password with the same code\" |\n| FR-4 | PASS | LoginForm.tsx `loginErrorMessage`; tests/unit/login-error-message.test.ts; tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts \"a wrong password shows the generic error\" |\n| FR-5 | PASS | tests/integration/auth.test.ts \"locks on the 5th failure…\" and \"success resets failedLoginCount, sets lastLoginAt…\" |\n| FR-6 | PASS | tests/integration/auth.test.ts \"rate limits after 10 attempts per IP\" (passes in isolation; full-suite timeout under NFR-13); tests/unit/rate-limit.test.ts; 429 copy in tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx |\n| FR-7 | PASS | tests/unit/auth-validators.test.ts `safeCallbackUrl`; tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts callbackUrl redirect |\n| FR-8 | PASS | tests/integration/auth.test.ts (auth.lockout and auth.login.success rows asserted); auth.login.failure in credentials.ts:43 (code-reviewed only, no test asserts the row) |\n| FR-9 | PASS | auth.config.ts:12 (maxAge 8h, updateAge 15m); the user menu shows the session name and role in tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts |\n| FR-10 | PASS | auth.ts:36-47 (authTime vs passwordChangedAt; `reauth` update); tests/integration/auth.test.ts \"success bumps passwordChangedAt\"; tests/e2e/auth-qa.spec.ts (current session survives reload after change). Logout of other devices is not e2e-tested. |\n| FR-11 | PASS | src/middleware.ts; tests/unit/public-routes.test.ts (QA); tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts redirect; curl /account/security → 307 /login?callbackUrl=%2Faccount%2Fsecurity |\n| FR-12 | PASS | src/server/auth/tokens.ts; tests/unit/tokens.test.ts; the invite/reset pages call verifyToken, and the APIs consume the token (integration \"token cannot be reused\") |\n| FR-13 | PASS | src/app/(auth)/invite/[token]/page.tsx; tests/e2e/auth-qa.spec.ts \"bogus invite token…\" and the read-only name/email; tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx |\n| FR-14 | PASS | tests/e2e/auth-qa.spec.ts \"invite accept → signed in on /dashboard; the link cannot be reused\" (DB: status ACTIVE, passwordChangedAt set); tests/integration/auth.test.ts acceptInvite |\n| FR-15 | PASS | src/lib/validators/auth.ts; tests/unit/password-policy.test.ts and auth-validators.test.ts; client rejection in tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx |\n| FR-16 | PASS | PasswordChecklist wired into SetPasswordForm (invite and reset) and ChangePasswordForm.tsx:70; asserted in tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx |\n| FR-17 | PASS | forgot-password/page.tsx + ForgotPasswordForm.tsx; tests/unit/auth-forms.test.tsx (same copy, 429); tests/e2e/auth.spec.ts; limits in services/auth.ts:42,46 (code-reviewed) |\n| FR-18 | PASS | tests/integration/auth.test.ts \"a known