{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgmBembaNztayEzVzWEGS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"SH-7 QA is done, and the verdict is **FAIL**: 38 of 51 requirements pass and 13 fail.\n\n**Main blocker.** Every attendance page that uses MUI's DataGrid fails to compile, so 9 requirements fail in the running app even though their server logic tests correctly. The cause is a version mismatch that was already there before SH-7: `@mui/x-data-grid` 9.5.0 needs a file that the installed `@mui/x-internals` 9.15.0 no longer provides. The broken pages are:\n- the student Attendance tab;\n- the course Attendance tab;\n- all of `/admin/attendance`, because it loads the Report tab up front. That also takes down the Today, Below-threshold and Settings tabs.\n\nThe fix is to pin `@mui/x-internals` or upgrade all the `@mui/x-*` packages together. That's a dependency change outside this ticket.\n\n**Two bugs in SH-7's own code**, each shown by a new test that fails:\n- **Duplicate absence notification (FR-22):** marking a student absent, then present, then absent again sends a second absence notification for the same register. The PRD allows only one.\n- **Teachers locked out after an admin excuse (FR-19):** once an admin marks any student Excused, the teacher gets a 403 on every later save of that register, because the server rejects any Excused value from a teacher, even one that hasn't changed. The fix is to reject it only when the status actually changes.\n\n**Other failures:**\n- `npm run test` still won't start because of a bad import in `vitest.config.ts` (pre-existing). I ran everything with `vitest.tmp.config.ts` instead.\n- The parent end-to-end test fails at the calendar step because of the DataGrid break. The teacher flow and the parent's notification both pass.\n\n**What I ran:**\n- Typecheck and lint are clean.\n- The full test suite: 225 of 229 pass. The 4 failures are my 2 bug tests and 2 older tests unrelated to SH-7; 2 older test files also fail to load.\n- The performance targets are met locally: saving a 35-student register took 39–101 ms (target 500), and a student's year tab with 1,200 records loaded in 45–50 ms (target 400).\n\n**New test files:**\n- `tests/integration/attendance-qa.test.ts`: 10 tests against the local database. The 2 failures are the bugs above, left failing on purpose. The tests clean up their data, and I confirmed nothing was left behind.\n- `tests/unit/attendance-register-form.test.tsx`: 8 tests of the register form, all passing.\n\nThere's no coverage tool installed, so `coverage-report.md` maps tests to functions by hand instead of measuring lines. I overwrote both QA reports, which were stale SH-1 copies.\n\nFiles are in `artifacts/qa/`:\n- `qa-report.md`\n- `coverage-report.md`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5916,"cache_read_input_tokens":140510,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5916},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"88405567-c8b9-4e5f-8912-47ba3c7edb01","uuid":"b925c2d9-941c-4372-9fec-752227fc4659","timestamp":"2026-11-06T06:15:53.870Z","request_id":"req_011CgmBemB35DXSYA5hqTW7Z"}
