{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrrpWdGi7LEcMdhVxrYW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The QA phase for SH-9 is finished and the verdict is **FAIL**: 76 of 78 requirements pass. All 61 functional requirements pass. The 2 failures are non-functional, and neither is a feature defect.\n\n**Test results:**\n- **Typecheck and lint:** both clean.\n- **SH-9 tests:** all 57 pass (29 unit, 23 integration against the local Postgres, 5 Playwright end-to-end). I ran the end-to-end tests against a production server on port 3100, then stopped it.\n- **New tests:** I wrote `tests/integration/assignments/qa-sh9.test.ts`, 9 tests for what Dev's tests didn't cover. These include scheduling and visibility, the \"published\" notification being sent only once, delete vs archive, duplicating to other courses, students not seeing each other's work, and access control. All 9 pass.\n- **Dev's report holds up:** every file Dev was supposed to create exists, and none are stubs or TODOs.\n\n**The 2 failures:**\n1. **NFR-12 (no `console.log`):** the new seed code in `prisma/seed.ts` (lines 303, 341, 385) uses `console.log`. It's a 3-line fix: switch to `logger.info`, which is already imported in that file.\n2. **NFR-13 (`npm run test` stays green):** the full suite has 6 failing tests, all outside SH-9 (attendance, auth, the login forms, toasts, lockout). The evidence says they predate SH-9: the attendance code hasn't changed since Nov 6, none of the tests use SH-9 code, and 2 passed on a rerun. I can't prove it, because the whole project is untracked in git (the repo root is your home folder), so there's nothing to compare against. They need a fix in a separate ticket.\n\n**Things a person should check:**\n- **Student tab (FR-41):** the tab is registered, but no page shows it yet, so it's only reachable by typing the URL.\n- **Admin menu (FR-40):** the \"Assignments\" menu entry also appears for admins, which the spec didn't ask for.\n- **Config changes:** Dev changed `next.config.js`. File URLs can now be shown inside the app's own pages (for PDF previews), and there is a build workaround for a MUI library export problem. Both need a sign-off.\n- **Stale server:** an old server from 27 Oct is still running on port 3000 and serving old code. Restart it before testing by hand.\n- **Not run:** I read the seed data code but didn't run it, to avoid changing the shared database. The keyboard shortcuts on the grading screen and the under-300 ms student switching are built, but no test checks them.\n\nThere are no line-coverage percentages: no coverage tool is installed, and the plan forbids adding dependencies. Instead, `coverage-report.md` maps each function to the tests that run it. About 90% of the service functions are covered; `listStudentAssignments` and `listManagedCourses` have no tests.\n\nFiles are in `artifacts/qa/`:\n- `qa-report.md`\n- `coverage-report.md`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":231,"cache_read_input_tokens":129230,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":231,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e675b554-96f9-4967-b795-466c40a9a33c","uuid":"2b101452-5201-44ad-8a00-55df92f84605","timestamp":"2026-11-09T06:12:28.672Z","request_id":"req_011CgrrpWNdHnHL1mLynByf9"}
