{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019kzYqAbJFD69HGg5C2ffGg","type":"tool_result","content":"SH-10 ['ticketId', 'timestamp', 'phase', 'version', 'prdTitle', 'prdTicketRef', 'runMode', 'functionalRequirements', 'nonFunctionalRequirements', 'overallConfidencePct', 'clarificationLog', 'existingCodebaseNotes', 'status']\nFR-1 | Add Prisma enums QuizStatus, QuestionType, ResultsVisibility, AttemptStatus and ScoringPolicy, and add the models Quiz, Question, QuizAttempt, QuizAnswer and QuizAccommodation exactly as listed in FR-1, in a new prisma migrate mig\nFR-2 | Enforce the field limits from FR-1 in Zod validators (src/lib/validators/quiz.ts): availableUntil > availableFrom, timeLimitMinutes 1–300 or null, maxAttempts 1–10, points 0.5–100, extraTimeMinutes 0–300, extraAttempts 0–5, choice\nFR-3 | Add pure auto-grading in src/server/quiz/grading.ts. SINGLE_CHOICE and TRUE_FALSE score all or nothing. MULTIPLE_CHOICE gives partial credit: points × max(0, (correctSelected − incorrectSelected) / totalCorrect). For the FR-2 exam\nFR-4 | SHORT_ANSWER grading trims the text and collapses whitespace, then matches it against any accepted answer. Matching ignores case unless caseSensitive is set. A non-match scores 0, is flagged for review, and a teacher can override \nFR-5 | ESSAY questions are never auto-graded. An optional guidance text is stored in `correct`.\nFR-6 | Quiz builder page /courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/edit. It has a settings panel for every Quiz field, with validation that the time limit is no longer than the availability window.\nFR-7 | The builder question list supports add (type picker), inline edit, duplicate, delete and drag reorder (@dnd-kit with MUI items). Each type has its own editor: option rows with a correct radio or checkbox, an accepted-answers list,\nFR-8 | The builder shows a running points total. 'Preview as student' opens the player in a preview mode that records nothing.\nFR-9 | Publishing requires at least 1 question, a correct answer on every choice question, and points > 0 on every question.\nFR-10 | Once any attempt exists, only question text, explanation and accepted answers can be edited. Adding or removing questions and changing points or type are blocked with an explanation. A Regrade action (POST /api/quizzes/:id/regrade\nFR-11 | Register a 'Quizzes' course tab in src/config/course-tabs.ts. Teachers see a list with status, window, attempt count, average score and 'Needs grading' count. Students see Upcoming, Available now (Start/Resume), Completed (score i\nFR-12 | Quiz player start screen at /quizzes/[quizId]/take. It shows instructions, question count, total points, time limit and attempts used/allowed. 'Start attempt' asks for confirmation because the timer starts immediately.\nFR-13 | Starting an attempt freezes questionOrder (shuffled when enabled) and the option order (deterministic shuffle seeded by attempt id). It sets deadlineAt = min(startedAt + timeLimit + extraTime, availableUntil).\nFR-14 | Player layout uses MUI RadioGroup, FormGroup with Checkboxes or TextField per type, plus a LinearProgress for completion. It shows either all questions on one page or one per page with a navigator grid of MUI Buttons (answered, un\nFR-15 | Autosave sends PUT /api/attempts/:id/answers/:questionId, debounced 800 ms. Failed saves are queued in localStorage and retried every 5 s. A status pill shows 'All answers saved', 'Saving…' or 'Offline — answers saved on this devi\nFR-16 | The timer is display-only. The server rejects answer writes after deadlineAt + 30 s grace with 409 CONFLICT and auto-submits the attempt.\nFR-17 | Submit asks for confirmation and shows the unanswered count. On submit, the attempt is auto-graded. Its status becomes NEEDS_GRADING if it has any ESSAY or any unmatched SHORT_ANSWER flagged for review; otherwise it becomes GRADED\nFR-18 | An IN_PROGRESS attempt past deadlineAt is auto-submitted with autoSubmitted = true. This happens lazily when the student or teacher loads it, and in autoSubmitExpiredAttempts() during the maintenance run.\nFR-19 | Each student can have only one IN_PROGRESS attempt per quiz. Opening the quiz in a second tab, or reopening it, resumes the same attempt with its saved answers.\nFR-20 | Results visibility: IMMEDIATELY shows results after submit, AFTER_CLOSE after availableUntil, and MANUAL after 'Release results' (POST /api/quizzes/:id/release-results sets resultsReleasedAt). Until then, students see 'Submitted —\nFR-21 | The result page shows the score, percentage, per-question correctness, the student's response and teacher feedback. It shows correct answers and explanations only when showCorrectAnswers is set.\nFR-22 | Export getStudentQuizScore(quizId, studentId). It applies the scoring policy (HIGHEST, LATEST or AVERAGE) across GRADED attempts, for use by PRD-11.\nFR-23 | The attempt limit is maxAttempts + extraAttempts. Further starts are refused. Example: with maxAttempts=2, a 3rd attempt is refused, but allowed with 1 extra attempt.\nFR-24 | Manual grading page /courses/[courseId]/quizzes/[quizId]/grade. It has 'By student' and 'By question' modes, with points input (0 to question points, step 0.5) and feedback. Teachers can override auto-graded answers. Saving uses P\nFR-25 | When every answer in an attempt is graded, the attempt becomes GRADED and its score is recomputed.\nFR-26 | The teacher Analytics tab shows attempts, average, median, highest, lowest, average time taken, and a score histogram (10% buckets, MUI X BarChart).\nFR-27 | The analytics per-question table shows % correct and average points. For choice questions it also shows the option distribution, highlighting the most-chosen wrong option. GET /api/quizzes/:id/analytics?format=csv exports all atte\nFR-28 | Teachers grant extra time and extra attempts per student on the quiz settings page (PUT /api/quizzes/:id/accommodations/:studentId). Both values feed the deadlineAt and attempt-limit checks.\nFR-29 | Register notification types quiz.published and quiz.results_released in src/server/notifications/types.ts. quiz.published goes to enrolled students on publish, with email off by default.\nFR-30 | quiz.results_released goes to the student and their parents when results become visible. For AFTER_CLOSE it is sent once by the maintenance run after close; for MANUAL it is sent on release; for IMMEDIATELY nothing is sent.\nFR-31 | Quiz and question CRUD REST endpoints follow the API table: GET/POST /api/courses/:id/quizzes (role-shaped list), GET/PATCH/DELETE /api/quizzes/:id (delete only without attempts), POST /api/quizzes/:id/questions, PATCH/DELETE /api\nFR-32 | Attempt endpoints: POST /api/quizzes/:id/attempts (STUDENT, start or resume), GET /api/attempts/:id (owner or manager), PUT /api/attempts/:id/answers/:questionId (owner), POST /api/attempts/:id/submit (owner).\nFR-33 | Practice quizzes (isPractice=true) are ungraded and never reach the gradebook. getStudentQuizScore callers (PRD-11) must exclude them, so the service exposes the isPractice flag.\nFR-34 | 'manage' and 'view course' roles reuse the existing course-access checks in src/server/auth/course-access.ts: teacher of the course or ADMIN manage; enrolled students view; parents of enrolled students view read-only.\nFR-35 | autoSubmitExpiredAttempts() and the AFTER_CLOSE results_released pass hook into the existing maintenance pass in /api/internal/email/dispatch, next to sendDueReminders(), and must be idempotent.\nFR-36 | Seed data. MATH-7A: 'Fractions Check' (8 objective questions, IMMEDIATELY, closed, all students attempted) and 'Unit 1 Test' (12 questions incl. 2 essays, AFTER_CLOSE, open for the next 3 days, no attempts). ENG-7A: practice quiz \nFR-37 | Add a Quizzes entry (or a quiz-aware link) to navigation if needed. The PRD defines only course-tab and direct routes, so no sidebar entry is assumed.\nFR-38 | Teacher actions on another user's records (grading, overriding, regrade, release results, accommodations) write an AuditLog row through audit().\nFR-39 | Question prompts are Markdown and may include an uploaded image, using the existing MarkdownEditor/MarkdownView and file upload components.\nNFR-1 | Security: correct answers (`correct`, explanation) and scores are never sent to a student's browser before results are visible. A dedicated student serializer enforces this, with a unit test asserting the `correct` key is absent. \nNFR-2 | Reliability/performance: answer autosave handles 300 concurrent students saving every few seconds. Each save is one upsert on QuizAnswer (attemptId, questionId), under 50 ms.\nNFR-3 | Accessibility: the player is fully keyboard operable. Choice options are native radio/checkbox inputs (MUI Radio/Checkbox). Timer warnings use aria-live='assertive' and are announced at 5 and 1 minutes remaining.\nNFR-4 | UI component rule: Material UI only (@mui/material 9.5.0, icons, x-data-grid, x-date-pickers, x-charts). Every component is looked up through the mui-mcp server (useMuiDocs → fetchDocs) before use, and an unreachable MCP is a bloc\nNFR-5 | Server-side access control on every handler and server page via requireUser/requireRole/course access checks. Students can access only their own attempts, parents only their linked children's released results, and teachers only co\nNFR-6 | API conventions: thin Zod-parsed handlers, { data } / list / { error } response shapes, standard error codes (409 after deadline), pagination ?page/?pageSize ≤ 100, cuid ids, UTC storage, and display in SchoolSettings.timezone.\nNFR-7 | Brownfield constraints: new code goes in src/server/quiz/ (feature subdirectory per the PRD-05 precedent). Reuse existing helpers: grading-math Decimal helpers, DataTable, ConfirmDialog, Toast/useToast, MarkdownView, notify(), aud\nNFR-8 | Tests: unit tests for every grading rule (partial credit, short-answer normalisation), deadline computation with accommodations, scoring policies, and the student serializer. Integration tests for autosave rejected after the deadl\nNFR-9 | Usability goal: a teacher can build a 10-question multiple-choice quiz in under 10 minutes.\nNFR-10 | Out of scope: lockdown browser, webcam proctoring, shared or random question banks, LaTeX formula input.\nNone | \n{\n  \"ticketId\": \"SH-10\",\n  \"timestamp\": \"2026-11-09T14:30:00Z\",\n  \"phase\": \"dev\",\n  \"version\": \"1.0\",\n  \"completed\": [\n    \"TASK-1\",\n    \"TASK-2\",\n    \"TASK-3\",\n    \"TASK-4\",\n    \"TASK-5\",\n    \"TASK-6\",\n    \"TASK-7\",\n    \"TASK-8\",\n    \"TASK-9\",\n    \"TASK-10\",\n    \"TASK-11\",\n    \"TASK-12\",\n    \"TASK-13\",\n    \"TASK-14\",\n    \"TASK-15\",\n    \"TASK-16\",\n    \"TASK-17\",\n    \"TASK-18\",\n    \"TASK-19\",\n    \"TASK-20\",\n    \"TASK-21\",\n    \"TASK-22\",\n    \"TASK-23\"\n  ]\n}","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1873d368-49d2-4130-ab97-f8c75b3c27a8","uuid":"fb16c868-5257-4dc5-890c-74ab205fd871","timestamp":"2026-11-09T07:53:09.841Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"SH-10 ['ticketId', 'timestamp', 'phase', 'version', 'prdTitle', 'prdTicketRef', 'runMode', 'functionalRequirements', 'nonFunctionalRequirements', 'overallConfidencePct', 'clarificationLog', 'existingCodebaseNotes', 'status']\nFR-1 | Add Prisma enums QuizStatus, QuestionType, ResultsVisibility, AttemptStatus and ScoringPolicy, and add the models Quiz, Question, QuizAttempt, QuizAnswer and QuizAccommodation exactly as listed in FR-1, in a new prisma migrate mig\nFR-2 | Enforce the field limits from FR-1 in Zod validators (src/lib/validators/quiz.ts): availableUntil > availableFrom, timeLimitMinutes 1–300 or null, maxAttempts 1–10, points 0.5–100, extraTimeMinutes 0–300, extraAttempts 0–5, choice\nFR-3 | Add pure auto-grading in src/server/quiz/grading.ts. SINGLE_CHOICE and TRUE_FALSE score all or nothing. MULTIPLE_CHOICE gives partial credit: points × max(0, (correctSelected − incorrectSelected) / totalCorrect). For the FR-2 exam\nFR-4 | SHORT_