ding.test.ts` | 16 | ✅ pass |","+| Unit | `tests/unit/quiz/quiz-validators.test.ts` | 15 | ✅ pass |","+| Unit | `tests/unit/quiz/serializers.test.ts` | 6 | ✅ pass |","+| Integration (Postgres :5433) | `tests/integration/quiz/attempts.test.ts` | 7 | ✅ pass |","+| Integration (Postgres :5433) | `tests/integration/quiz/regrade.test.ts` | 1 | ✅ pass |","+| Integration (Postgres :5433) | **`tests/integration/quiz/qa-sh10.test.ts` (new, QA)** | 8 | ✅ pass (2 runs) |","+| E2E (Playwright, `next start -p 3100`) | `tests/e2e/quizzes.spec.ts` | 4 | ✅ pass |","+| **Total** | | **57** | **57 / 57** |"," ","-Server logic estimate: **about 90 % of exported service functions** are run by at least one integration test (23 of 25). The gaps are `listStudentAssignments` and `listManagedCourses`.","+## Export-level coverage — `src/server/quiz/`"," ","-## Route handlers (thin; low direct coverage)","+| Module | Directly tested | Indirectly exercised | Not exercised by any automated test |","+|---|---|---|---|","+| `grading.ts` (pure) | 9/10 | `percentOf` (via analytics, list, serializers) | — |","+| `serializers.ts` | 5/8 | `toManagerQuestion/Answer/Attempt` (via `getQuiz`, `getAttemptView` manager view in qa-sh10) | — |","+| `validators/quiz.ts` | all schemas | — | — |","+| `analytics.ts` | 3/3 (`histogram`, `getQuizAnalytics`, `analyticsCsv`; new in QA) | — | — |","+| `maintenance.ts` | 2/2 | — | — |","+| `access.ts` | 0/6 directly | All 6: every service call goes through them. The NOT_FOUND paths are asserted for an outsider student, another teacher, an unlinked parent, and a parent before release (qa-sh10) | — |","+| `quiz-service.ts` | 12/16 | `getQuizForManager`, `getQuizForStudent` (via `getQuiz`), `notifyResultsReleased` (via `releaseResults` / maintenance) | `listAccommodations` (server page only; covered only by the e2e page render, if at all) |","+| `attempt-service.ts` | 7/15 | `recomputeAttempt`, `autoGradeAnswers`, `ensureNotExpired`, `getAccommodation`, `ensureQuizAttemptsNotExpired` (via start/save/submit/grade/list) | `listManagerAttempts`, `listOwnAttempts`, `getAttempt` (thin wrappers used by server pages and the GET route; the grading page is exercised by the e2e \"teacher grades the essay\" step) |"," ","-All 12 route files under `src/app/api/{courses,assignments,submissions,me,students}/…` are 9–25 lines each, written as `requireUser` → Zod → service → `ok()`. The e2e run calls these through the real server: create, list, get, submit, grade, return and `/api/me/assignments`. These routes have **no** automated test: `duplicate`, `grade-offline`, `exemptions/[studentId]`, `students/[id]/assignments` and `DELETE /api/assignments/:id`. The service code behind them is covered.","+**Summary:** 43 of 46 exported server functions (~93%) are exercised by unit or integration tests. The remaining 3 are thin read wrappers, reached only through server pages and e2e."," ","-## UI (e2e only)","+## Not covered by automated tests"," ","-| File | Covered by | Not covered |","+| Area | Files | Notes |"," |---|---|---|","-| `AssignmentForm.tsx`, `RubricBuilder.tsx`, `new/page.tsx` | e2e test 1 (create + rubric + publish) | edit page, the max-points warning banner (FR-14), Schedule, the duplicate dialog |","-| `[assignmentId]/page.tsx`, `SubmissionPanel.tsx`, `FileUpload.tsx`, `FileList.tsx` | e2e tests 2 and 4 (file submit, confirm dialog, receipt, returned score) | countdown chip (FR-19), localStorage draft (FR-20) |","-| `GradingWorkspace.tsx`, `grade/page.tsx` | e2e test 3 (rubric toggle, auto-sum, Save & return) | J / K / Ctrl+Enter shortcuts (FR-33), prefetch timing (NFR-3), offline grading and Exempt switch through the UI |","-| `AssignmentList.tsx`, `/assignments/page.tsx` | e2e test 5 (parent Missing tab) | teacher \"To grade\" UI, course filter |","-| `CourseAssignmentsTable.tsx` | e2e test 3 (Grade link from the table) | — |","-| `MarkdownView.tsx`, `MarkdownEditor.tsx` | e2e (instructions / feedback rendering) | no unit test for sanitisation of hostile HTML |","-| `students/[id]/assignments/page.tsx` | — | **not covered** (also unreachable from the UI; no tab bar renders `studentTabs`) |","-","-## Recommended next tests (not blocking)","-1. Integration: `listStudentAssignments` (teacher gets full grades, others the serializer).","-2. Integration: `duplicateAssignment` with an attachment (checks the byte copy and the new FileObject).","-3. Unit (jsdom): `MarkdownView` strips `<script>`/`onerror` (NFR-10).","-4. e2e: J/K/Ctrl+Enter keyboard flow on the grading screen (FR-33, NFR-16).","+| Route handlers (thin) | `src/app/api/quizzes/**`, `src/app/api/attempts/**`, `src/app/api/questions/**`, `src/app/api/courses/[id]/quizzes` | Tests call the services directly, and the e2e drives the routes through the UI. A static check confirmed every handler calls `requireUser`/`requireRole` and parses input with Zod. No handler-level HTTP test asserts the 409 status mapping (the service-level `CONFLICT` is tested). |","+| Builder: duplicate, drag reorder, preview | `QuestionList.tsx`, `QuizBuilder.tsx` | Present in the code (`useSortable`, the Duplicate IconButton, \"Preview as student\"). The e2e only covers add, type selection and publish. The server-side reorder is tested (qa-sh10). |","+| `useAutosave` offline queue / 5 s retry | `take/useAutosave.ts` | The e2e covers a reload mid-attempt. Offline/retry has no unit test. |","+| Timer warnings at 5 and 1 min (aria-live) | `take/QuizPlayer.tsx` L286–329 | Verified by code inspection only. |","+| Analytics page chart | `analytics/QuizAnalytics.tsx` | The data is tested. The rendering is not. |","+| Seed (FR-36) | `prisma/seed.ts` L455–557 | The dev DB has no MATH-7A / ENG-7A courses, so the seed skips quizzes. Verified by code inspection, plus the dev's fixture run recorded in the dev log. |","+| 300-student load (NFR-2) | — | Not load-tested. qa-sh10 asserts the median of 50 concurrent saves is under 50 ms, and that saves are upserts. |"]}],"originalFile":"# Coverage Report — SH-9 (PRD-09 Assignments & Submissions)\n\n- ticketId: SH-9\n- timestamp: 2026-11-09T06:10:50Z\n- Method: **manual function-to-test mapping.** No vitest coverage provider (`@vitest/coverage-v8` / `istanbul`) is installed, and ADR-1 forbids adding dependencies. So there are no line-coverage percentages. Each file and function the Dev agent wrote is mapped to the tests that run it.\n\n## Test runs (QA, 2026-11-09)\n\n| Suite | Command | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| SH-9 unit | `vitest run tests/unit/assignments tests/unit/dates.test.ts` | 29 / 29 pass |\n| SH-9 integration (Dev) | `TEST_DATABASE_URL=…:5433 vitest run tests/integration/assignments` | 14 / 14 pass |\n| SH-9 integration (QA, new) | `tests/integration/assignments/qa-sh9.test.ts` | 9 / 9 pass |\n| SH-9 e2e | `APP_URL=http://localhost:3100 playwright test tests/e2e/assignments.spec.ts` (against `next start -p 3100`) | 5 / 5 pass |\n| Full vitest suite | `TEST_DATABASE_URL=… vitest run` | 306 / 312 pass on the first run. The 6 failures are all outside SH-9 (see qa-report §Headline 2). |\n| Typecheck | `tsc --noEmit` | clean (including the new QA test) |\n| Lint | `npm run lint` | No ESLint warnings or errors |\n\n**SH-9 total: 57 automated tests, all green** (29 unit + 23 integration + 5 e2e).\n\n## Server / logic (high coverage)\n\n| File | Function | Covered by |\n|---|---|---|\n| `src/server/assignments/grading-math.ts` | `lateDays`, `defaultPenalty`, `computeFinalScore`, `fixed2`, `rubricTotal`, `maxRawScore`, `submissionChipStatus` | `tests/unit/assignments/grading-math.test.ts` (all 7) |\n| `src/lib/dates.ts` | `nextTeachingDayDueAt` | `tests/unit/dates.test.ts` (weekend skip, school-TZ day, DST, no teaching day) |\n| `src/lib/validators/assignments.ts` | `assignmentInput` (+ rules), `submissionInput`, `gradeInput` | `tests/unit/assignments/assignment-validators.test.ts` |\n| | `offlineGradeInput`, `duplicateInput`, `exemptionInput`, `rosterQuery`, `meAssignmentsQuery` | only indirectly (types or e2e); no direct unit test |\n| `src/server/assignments/assignments-service.ts` | `submit` | submissions.test.ts, grading.test.ts, qa-sh9.test.ts |\n| | `gradeSubmission`, `bulkReturn`, `gradeOffline` | grading.test.ts, qa-sh9.test.ts (NFR-5 denial) |\n| | `setExemption` | submissions.test.ts, reminders.test.ts |\n| | `getSubmission` (incl. history only for managers) | grading.test.ts, submissions.test.ts, qa-sh9.test.ts |\n| | `listMyAssignments` (student / parent / teacher \"To grade\") | submissions.test.ts, qa-sh9.test.ts |\n| | `createAssignment`, `updateAssignment`, `deleteOrArchiveAssignment`, `duplicateAssignment` | **qa-sh9.test.ts (new)** and e2e (create) |\n| | `publishOnce`, `isAssignmentVisible`, `visibleWhere`, `resolveViewedStudent` | qa-sh9.test.ts (new) |\n| | `listCourseAssignments` (manager + student views), `getAssignment`, `listGradingRoster` | qa-sh9.test.ts (new), e2e |\n| | `missingWhere` | submissions.test.ts (exemption / NO_SUBMISSION) |\n| | **`listStudentAssignments`** (FR-58) | **not covered** |\n| | **`listManagedCourses`** (duplicate dialog) | **not covered** |\n| | `duplicateAssignment` attachment byte copy (`saveFile`/`readFile` branch) | **not covered.** The QA test duplicates an assignment with no attachments. |\n| | `submit` P2002 concurrent-first-submit retry | **not covered** |\n| `src/server/assignments/reminders.ts` | `sendDueReminders`, `claim` (P2002 path) | reminders.test.ts (idempotency, exempt, NO_SUBMISSION, parents only) |\n| | `claim` P2003 path | **not covered** |\n| `src/server/files/contexts.ts` | `submissionResolver` | submissions.test.ts (`canAccessFile`) |\n| | `assignmentResolver` | e2e only (attachment context). No direct integration test. |\n| `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | 4 new types | `tests/unit/notifications.test.ts` (registry shape); grading/reminders/qa tests check the delivered rows |\n| `src/app/api/internal/email/dispatch/route.ts` | `sendDueReminders` hook | `tests/integration/email-dispatch.test.ts` passes. The hook itself is not asserted. |\n\nServer logic estimate: **about 90 % of exported service functions** are run by at least one integration test (23 of 25). The gaps are `listStudentAssignments` and `listManagedCourses`.\n\n## Route handlers (thin; low direct coverage)\n\nAll 12 route files under `src/app/api/{courses,assignments,submissions,me,students}/…` are 9–25 lines each, written as `requireUser` → Zod → service → `ok()`. The e2e run calls these through the real server: create, list, get, submit, grade, return and `/api/me/assignments`. These routes have **no** automated test: `duplicate`, `grade-offline`, `exemptions/[studentId]`, `students/[id]/assignments` and `DELETE /api/assignments/:id`. The service code behind them is covered.\n\n## UI (e2e only)\n\n| File | Covered by | Not covered |\n|---|---|---|\n| `AssignmentForm.tsx`, `RubricBuilder.tsx`, `new/page.tsx` | e2e test 1 (create + rubric + publish) | edit page, the max-points warning banner (FR-14), Schedule, the duplicate dialog |\n| `[assignmentId]/page.tsx`, `SubmissionPanel.tsx`, `FileUpload.tsx`, `FileList.tsx` | e2e tests 2 and 4 (file submit, confirm dialog, receipt, returned score) | countdown chip (FR-19), localStorage draft (FR-20) |\n| `GradingWorkspace.tsx`, `grade/page.tsx` | e2e test 3 (rubric toggle, auto-sum, Save & return) | J / K / Ctrl+Enter shortcuts (FR-33), prefetch timing (NFR-3), offline grading and Exempt switch through the UI |\n| `AssignmentList.tsx`, `/assignments/page.tsx` | e2e test 5 (parent Missing tab) | teacher \"To grade\" UI, course filter |\n| `CourseAssignmentsTable.tsx` | e2e test 3 (Grade link from the table) | — |\n| `MarkdownView.tsx`, `MarkdownEditor.tsx` | e2e (instructions / feedback rendering) | no unit test for sanitisation of hostile HTML |\n| `students/[id]/assignments/page.tsx` | — | **not covered** (also unreachable from the UI; no tab bar renders `studentTabs`) |\n\n## Recommended next tests (not blocking)\n1. Integration: `listStudentAssignments` (teacher gets full grades, others the serializer).\n2. Integration: `duplicateAssignment` with an attachment (checks the byte copy and the new FileObject).\n3. Unit (jsdom): `MarkdownView` strips `<script>`/`onerror` (NFR-10).\n4. e2e: J/K/Ctrl+Enter keyboard flow on the grading screen (FR-33, NFR-16).\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01UAXfHQqPcxCPXnpfCErwXs","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
