{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgrzsrCzxfTg3W2a2yQGN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've finished the QA pass for SH-10. The verdict is **FAIL**: 47 of 49 requirements pass and 2 fail. All 39 functional requirements pass and the quiz feature works end to end; the two failures are non-functional.\n\n**What I ran:**\n- **Lint, typecheck and database migrations:** all clean.\n- **Quiz unit and integration tests:** 53/53 pass. That includes 8 new tests I wrote in `tests/integration/quiz/qa-sh10.test.ts`.\n- **Quiz end-to-end test:** 4/4 pass on a production build (port 3100). It covers a teacher building a quiz, a student taking it and reloading mid-attempt, grading the essay, and the student seeing results.\n- **Dev's work:** all 51 planned files exist, have real implementations, and contain no TODOs or stubs.\n\n**What the new tests check** (dev's tests didn't cover these):\n- Correct answers and explanations never reach a student's browser before results are released.\n- The course quiz list differs correctly for teachers, students and parents.\n- Quiz analytics and the CSV export.\n- Parents, other students and other teachers can't see records they shouldn't.\n- Grading, regrade, releasing results and student accommodations (extra time or attempts) each write an audit log entry.\n- Reordering questions rejects an incomplete or duplicated list.\n- Saving an answer takes under 50 ms (median of 50 concurrent saves).\n\n**The 2 failures:**\n1. **NFR-7 (no `console.log`):** `prisma/seed.ts` lines 463 and 526 use `console.log`. The fix is to switch both to `logger.info`, which the file already imports.\n2. **NFR-8 (full test run must be green):** `npm run test` has 6 failing tests. They are the same ones listed in the SH-9 report, from before SH-10, and none of them touch quiz code. A seventh test (`email-dispatch`) failed once in the full run but passed 3/3 when run alone, so it's flaky rather than broken by SH-10.\n\nI marked both as FAIL to match how SH-9 handled the same two problems.\n\n**Limits of this run:**\n- No coverage tool is installed and the requirements forbid adding dependencies, so `coverage-report.md` counts which of the quiz module's 46 server functions the tests reach (43, about 93%) instead of line coverage.\n- I couldn't run the seed data step because the dev database has no MATH-7A or ENG-7A courses. I checked that code by reading it.\n\nBoth reports are in `artifacts/qa/` and replace the old SH-9 versions; `qa-report.md` was written last."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6104,"cache_read_input_tokens":108409,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":6104,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":5,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1873d368-49d2-4130-ab97-f8c75b3c27a8","uuid":"a4e9184e-c4c7-4662-9e35-471162caeb28","timestamp":"2026-11-09T07:58:07.367Z","request_id":"req_011Cgrzsqkxj4ymyhfJncBzg"}
