des |\n| UI: `GradebookGrid.tsx` | gradebook e2e | **Medium.** Covers keyboard edit (digits+Enter, E, M, Delete), 78.0% C+ | Column menu (hide/show, mark missing, stats), Export CSV button, synced-cell click-through, Add item / Override dialogs |\n| UI: `ReportCardDocument.tsx`, `PrintButton.tsx`, print pages | report-cards e2e | **Medium.** Covers the parent print view with chrome hidden under `print` media | Bulk \"Print all\" page |\n| UI: `StudentGradesView.tsx`, `/grades`, `/students/[id]/grades`, course Grades | — | **Low.** Only the data layer is tested (qa-sh11) | Rendering, child selector |\n| UI: admin grading-scales, gradebook settings, admin report-cards roster, homeroom list/review, student report-cards tab | report-cards e2e (admin roster only) | **Low** | Scale editor, settings live-sum chip, homeroom review page |\n| `prisma/seed.ts` (PRD-11 block) | Dev manual run on temp 7A fixtures (dev-log) | **Not re-run by QA.** The dev DB has no 7A courses, so the block would only log a skip | — |\n\n## Summary\n\n- **Server logic** (calc, sync, backfill, student grades, report cards): well covered. Every PRD \"Test Requirements\" item (calculation matrix, sync hooks, backfill idempotency, snapshot immutability, the 3 Playwright flows) exists and passes.\n- **Estimated line coverage of new server code: ~75–80%** (hand estimate). The main untested pieces are `scales-service.ts`, `exportGradebookCsv`, `deleteItem`, and the CLI wrapper.\n- **UI components: ~35–40%** (hand estimate). Only the two e2e flows exercise them.\n- **Recommended additions:** an HTTP test for `/api/grading-scales` on an isolated DB; a CSV export assertion; a Playwright check for the column menu and the student Grades tab.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":53,"newStart":1,"newLines":59,"lines":["-# Coverage Report — SH-10 (PRD-10 Quizzes & Online Exams)","+# Coverage Report — SH-11 (PRD-11 Gradebook, Grading Scales & Report Cards)"," ","-> This file replaces the stale SH-9 coverage report.","+- ticketId: SH-11","+- timestamp: 2026-11-09T14:29:37Z"," ","-- ticketId: SH-10","-- timestamp: 2026-11-09T07:58:00Z","+> This file replaces the stale SH-10 coverage report."," ","-## How coverage was measured","+## Method"," ","-No coverage provider (`@vitest/coverage-v8` / `istanbul`) is installed. NFR-7 forbids new dependencies, so line coverage could not be collected.","-Instead, coverage is measured at two levels:","-1. **Export-level:** for each exported function in `src/server/quiz/*`, is it called directly by a test, or reached through a function that is?","-2. **Requirement-level:** see the Requirement Results table in `qa-report.md`.","+No coverage instrumenter is installed (`@vitest/coverage-v8` is not a dependency), and QA did not add one. Coverage is therefore mapped by hand: for each new or changed module, the tests that exercise it **and were run by QA in this phase**."," ","-## Test inventory (SH-10)","+## Tests run by QA"," ","-| Suite | File | Tests | Result (QA run) |","-|---|---|---|---|","-| Unit | `tests/unit/quiz/grading.test.ts` | 16 | ✅ pass |","-| Unit | `tests/unit/quiz/quiz-validators.test.ts` | 15 | ✅ pass |","-| Unit | `tests/unit/quiz/serializers.test.ts` | 6 | ✅ pass |","-| Integration (Postgres :5433) | `tests/integration/quiz/attempts.test.ts` | 7 | ✅ pass |","-| Integration (Postgres :5433) | `tests/integration/quiz/regrade.test.ts` | 1 | ✅ pass |","-| Integration (Postgres :5433) | **`tests/integration/quiz/qa-sh10.test.ts` (new, QA)** | 8 | ✅ pass (2 runs) |","-| E2E (Playwright, `next start -p 3100`) | `tests/e2e/quizzes.spec.ts` | 4 | ✅ pass |","-| **Total** | | **57** | **57 / 57** |","+| Suite | Tests | Result |","+|---|---|---|","+| `tests/unit/gradebook/grade-calc.test.ts` (Dev) | 17 | ✅ pass |","+| `tests/unit/gradebook/term-placement.test.ts` (Dev) | 4 | ✅ pass |","+| `tests/unit/gradebook/validators.test.ts` (**QA, new**) | 4 | ✅ pass |","+| `tests/integration/gradebook/gradebook-sync.test.ts` (Dev) | 8 | ✅ pass (Postgres) |","+| `tests/integration/gradebook/backfill.test.ts` (Dev) | 1 | ✅ pass (Postgres) |","+| `tests/integration/report-cards/report-cards.test.ts` (Dev) | 5 | ✅ pass (Postgres) |","+| `tests/integration/gradebook/qa-sh11.test.ts` (**QA, new**) | 7 | ✅ pass 3/3 runs (Postgres) |","+| `tests/e2e/gradebook.spec.ts` (Dev, Playwright, fresh prod build :3100) | 1 | ✅ pass |","+| `tests/e2e/report-cards.spec.ts` (Dev, Playwright, fresh prod build :3100) | 1 | ✅ pass |","+| **SH-11 total** | **48** | **48/48** |"," ","-## Export-level coverage — `src/server/quiz/`","+Integration tests are skipped without `TEST_DATABASE_URL`. QA ran them with `TEST_DATABASE_URL=$DATABASE_URL`, after confirming with `prisma migrate status` that the schema is up to date."," ","-| Module | Directly tested | Indirectly exercised | Not exercised by any automated test |","+## Per-module coverage","+","+| Module | Covered by | Coverage | Gaps |"," |---|---|---|---|","-| `grading.ts` (pure) | 9/10 | `percentOf` (via analytics, list, serializers) | — |","-| `serializers.ts` | 5/8 | `toManagerQuestion/Answer/Attempt` (via `getQuiz`, `getAttemptView` manager view in qa-sh10) | — |","-| `validators/quiz.ts` | all schemas | — | — |","-| `analytics.ts` | 3/3 (`histogram`, `getQuizAnalytics`, `analyticsCsv`; new in QA) | — | — |","-| `maintenance.ts` | 2/2 | — | — |","-| `access.ts` | 0/6 directly | All 6: every service call goes through them. The NOT_FOUND paths are asserted for an outsider student, another teacher, an unlinked parent, and a parent before release (qa-sh10) | — |","-| `quiz-service.ts` | 12/16 | `getQuizForManager`, `getQuizForStudent` (via `getQuiz`), `notifyResultsReleased` (via `releaseResults` / maintenance) | `listAccommodations` (server page only; covered only by the e2e page render, if at all) |","-| `attempt-service.ts` | 7/15 | `recomputeAttempt`, `autoGradeAnswers`, `ensureNotExpired`, `getAccommodation`, `ensureQuizAttemptsNotExpired` (via start/save/submit/grade/list) | `listManagerAttempts`, `listOwnAttempts`, `getAttempt` (thin wrappers used by server pages and the GET route; the grading page is exercised by the e2e \"teacher grades the essay\" step) |","+| `src/server/gradebook/grade-calc.ts` | grade-calc unit (17), qa-sh11, e2e | **High.** Every exported function is tested: no categories, empty categories, drop lowest, never-drop-all, missing vs ungraded vs excused, hidden, strict due boundary, rounding at band edges (89.95→90.0 A−, 76.95→77.0 C+), letter-only / percent-only / both overrides, colour bands | `applyDropLowest` tie-breaks (equal ratios → dueAt → id) are not asserted |","+| `src/server/gradebook/term-placement.ts` | term-placement unit (4) | **High** | — |","+| `src/lib/validators/gradebook.ts` | validators unit (QA), qa-sh11 (via `.parse`) | **Medium-high.** Covers band rules, weight sum, unique category names, the 1,000-character comment cap | `reportCardPatchSchema`, `unpublishSchema` are only covered indirectly by report-cards integration |","+| `src/server/gradebook/gradebook-sync.ts` | gradebook-sync (8), backfill, qa-sh11 | **High.** Covers assignment publish/draft/archive/delete, return vs save, exemption on/off, A7 hide-survives-resave, quiz IMMEDIATELY / MANUAL / AFTER_CLOSE, practice | `assertCategoryInCourse` rejection (foreign category) is not asserted; the no-term skip path (A6) is only unit-covered via `termFor` |","+| `src/server/gradebook/backfill.ts` + `scripts/gradebook-backfill.ts` | backfill (1) | **Medium.** Idempotency is proven | The CLI wrapper (18 lines) is untested |","+| `src/server/gradebook/load.ts` | qa-sh11, report-cards, e2e | **High** (indirect) | — |","+| `src/server/gradebook/gradebook-service.ts` | qa-sh11 (7), e2e | **Medium-high.** Covers getGradebook (sort, result, 35×80 perf), createManualItem, putGrade (manual, synced-comment-only, out-of-course teacher, student refused, audit, grade.posted once), updateItem (synced reject / hide), markAllMissing (before / after due), putTermOverride (letter-only, unknown letter, audit) | `exportGradebookCsv` (FR-25), `deleteItem`, `updateItem` maxPoints-below-existing-score guard |","+| `src/server/gradebook/categories-service.ts` | qa-sh11 | **Medium.** Covers the weights≠100 reject and a valid replace | Foreign-id reject, gradingScaleId change |","+| `src/server/gradebook/scales-service.ts` | — (validators only) | **Low.** The service is untested. QA did not exercise create/update/delete, because those would flip the school default in the shared dev DB | Admin-only guard, default swap, A11 delete conflicts. The DB invariant is enforced by the partial unique index `grading_scale_one_default` (present in the DB) |","+| `src/server/gradebook/student-grades-service.ts` | qa-sh11, e2e (parent) | **High.** Covers student and parent views, hidden item excluded, unreturned score null, other student / unlinked parent refused | — |","+| `src/server/report-cards/report-card-service.ts`, `snapshot.ts`, `access.ts` | report-cards integration (5), report-cards e2e | **High.** Covers generate, roster warnings, draft hidden from family, comment field rules, publish + notifications, 7B NOT_FOUND, snapshot immutability, regenerate skips PUBLISHED, unpublish with reason | NFR-3 (600×8 < 30 s) is not load-tested |","+| `src/server/assignments/assignments-service.ts` (hooks) | gradebook-sync, existing assignment suites | **High** | See qa-report Headline 1: `publishOnce` change made `qa-sh9` flaky |","+| `src/server/quiz/*` (hooks) | gradebook-sync (3 quiz tests), existing quiz suites | **High** | — |","+| `src/server/notifications/types.ts` | qa-sh11 (grade.posted), report-cards (report_card.published) | **High** | — |","+| API route handlers (`src/app/api/**`, 17 files, 9–19 lines each) | e2e (gradebook PUT grades, report-card generate/publish/GET) | **Low-medium.** Handlers are thin (validator → service) | No HTTP-level tests for grading-scales, grade-categories, term-overrides, mark-missing, students/:id/grades |","+| UI: `GradebookGrid.tsx` | gradebook e2e | **Medium.** Covers keyboard edit (digits+Enter, E, M, Delete), 78.0% C+ | Column menu (hide/show, mark missing, stats), Export CSV button, synced-cell click-through, Add item / Override dialogs |","+| UI: `ReportCardDocument.tsx`, `PrintButton.tsx`, print pages | report-cards e2e | **Medium.** Covers the parent print view with chrome hidden under `print` media | Bulk \"Print all\" page |","+| UI: `StudentGradesView.tsx`, `/grades`, `/students/[id]/grades`, course Grades | — | **Low.** Only the data layer is tested (qa-sh11) | Rendering, child selector |","+| UI: admin grading-scales, gradebook settings, admin report-cards roster, homeroom list/review, student report-cards tab | report-cards e2e (admin roster only) | **Low** | Scale editor, settings live-sum chip, homeroom review page |","+| `prisma/seed.ts` (PRD-11 block) | Dev manual run on temp 7A fixtures (dev-log) | **Not re-run by QA.** The dev DB has no 7A courses, so the block would only log a skip | — |"," ","-**Summary:** 43 of 46 exported server functions (~93%) are exercised by unit or integration tests. The remaining 3 are thin read wrappers, reached only through server pages and e2e.","+## Summary"," ","-## Not covered by automated tests","-","-| Area | Files | Notes |","-|---|---|---|","-| Route handlers (thin) | `src/app/api/quizzes/**`, `src/app/api/attempts/**`, `src/app/api/questions/**`, `src/app/api/courses/[id]/quizzes` | Tests call the services directly, and the e2e drives the routes through the UI. A static check confirmed every handler calls `requireUser`/`requireRole` and parses input with Zod. No handler-level HTTP test asserts the 409 status mapping (the service-level `CONFLICT` is tested). |","-| Builder: duplicate, drag reorder, preview | `QuestionList.tsx`, `QuizBuilder.tsx` | Present in the code (`useSortable`, the Duplicate IconButton, \"Preview as student\"). The e2e only covers add, type selection and publish. The server-side reorder is tested (qa-sh10). |","-| `useAutosave` offline queue / 5 s retry | `take/useAutosave.ts` | The e2e covers a reload mid-attempt. Offline/retry has no unit test. |","-| Timer warnings at 5 and 1 min (aria-live) | `take/QuizPlayer.tsx` L286–329 | Verified by code inspection only. |","-| Analytics page chart | `analytics/QuizAnalytics.tsx` | The data is tested. The rendering is not. |","-| Seed (FR-36) | `prisma/seed.ts` L455–557 | The dev DB has no MATH-7A / ENG-7A courses, so the seed skips quizzes. Verified by code inspection, plus the dev's fixture run recorded in the dev log. |","-| 300-student load (NFR-2) | — | Not load-tested. qa-sh10 asserts the median of 50 concurrent saves is under 50 ms, and that saves are upserts. |","+- **Server logic** (calc, sync, backfill, student grades, report cards): well covered. Every PRD \"Test Requirements\" item (calculation matrix, sync hooks, backfill idempotency, snapshot immutability, the 3 Playwright flows) exists and passes.","+- **Estimated line coverage of new server code: ~75–80%** (hand estimate). The main untested pieces are `scales-service.ts`, `exportGradebookCsv`, `deleteItem`, and the CLI wrapper.","+- **UI components: ~35–40%** (hand estimate). Only the two e2e flows exercise them.","+- **Recommended additions:** an HTTP test for `/api/grading-scales` on an isolated DB; a CSV export assertion; a Playwright check for the column menu and the student Grades tab."]}],"originalFile":"# Coverage Report — SH-10 (PRD-10 Quizzes & Online Exams)\n\n> This file replaces the stale SH-9 coverage report.\n\n- ticketId: SH-10\n- timestamp: 2026-11-09T07:58:00Z\n\n## How coverage was measured\n\nNo coverage provider (`@vitest/coverage-v8` / `istanbul`) is installed. NFR-7 forbids new dependencies, so line coverage could not be collected.\nInstead, coverage is measured at two levels:\n1. **Export-level:** for each exported function in `src/server/quiz/*`, is it called directly by a test, or reached through a function that is?\n2. **Requirement-level:** see the Requirement Results table in `qa-report.md`.\n\n## Test inventory (SH-10)\n\n| Suite | File | Tests | Result (QA run) |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Unit | `tests/unit/quiz/grading.test.ts` | 16 | ✅ pass |\n| Unit | `tests/unit/quiz/quiz-validators.test.ts` | 15 | ✅ pass |\n| Unit | `tests/unit/quiz/serializers.test.ts` | 6 | ✅ pass |\n| Integration (Postgres :5433) | `tests/integration/quiz/attempts.test.ts` | 7 | ✅ pass |\n| Integration (Postgres :5433) | `tests/integration/quiz/regrade.test.ts` | 1 | ✅ pass |\n| Integration (Postgres :5433) | **`tests/integration/quiz/qa-sh10.test.ts` (new, QA)** | 8 | ✅ pass (2 runs) |\n| E2E (Playwright, `next start -p 3100`) | `tests/e2e/quizzes.spec.ts` | 4 | ✅ pass |\n| **Total** | | **57** | **57 / 57** |\n\n## Export-level coverage — `src/server/quiz/`\n\n| Module | Directly tested | Indirectly exercised | Not exercised by any automated test |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `grading.ts` (pure) | 9/10 | `percentOf` (via analytics, list, serializers) | — |\n| `serializers.ts` | 5/8 | `toManagerQuestion/Answer/Attempt` (via `getQuiz`, `getAttemptView` manager view in qa-sh10) | — |\n| `validators/quiz.ts` | all schemas | — | — |\n| `analytics.ts` | 3/3 (`histogram`, `getQuizAnalytics`, `analyticsCsv`; new in QA) | — | — |\n| `maintenance.ts` | 2/2 | — | — |\n| `access.ts` | 0/6 directly | All 6: every service call goes through them. The NOT_FOUND paths are asserted for an outsider student, another teacher, an unlinked parent, and a parent before release (qa-sh10) | — |\n| `quiz-service.ts` | 12/16 | `getQuizForManager`, `getQuizForStudent` (via `getQuiz`), `notifyResultsReleased` (via `releaseResults` / maintenance) | `listAccommodations` (server page only; covered only by the e2e page render, if at all) |\n| `attempt-service.ts` | 7/15 | `recomputeAttempt`, `autoGradeAnswers`, `ensureNotExpired`, `getAccommodation`, `ensureQuizAttemptsNotExpired` (via start/save/submit/grade/list) | `listManagerAttempts`, `listOwnAttempts`, `getAttempt` (thin wrappers used by server pages and the GET route; the grading page is exercised by the e2e \"teacher grades the essay\" step) |\n\n**Summary:** 43 of 46 exported server functions (~93%) are exercised by unit or integration tests. The remaining 3 are thin read wrappers, reached only through server pages and e2e.\n\n## Not covered by automated tests\n\n| Area | Files | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| Route handlers (thin) | `src/app/api/quizzes/**`, `src/app/api/attempts/**`, `src/app/api/questions/**`, `src/app/api/courses/[id]/quizzes` | Tests call the services directly, and the e2e drives the routes through the UI. A static check confirmed every handler calls `requireUser`/`requireRole` and parses input with Zod. No handler-level HTTP test asserts the 409 status mapping (the service-level `CONFLICT` is tested). |\n| Builder: duplicate, drag reorder, preview | `QuestionList.tsx`, `QuizBuilder.tsx` | Present in the code (`useSortable`, the Duplicate IconButton, \"Preview as student\"). The e2e only covers add, type selection and publish. The server-side reorder is tested (qa-sh10). |\n| `useAutosave` offline queue / 5 s retry | `take/useAutosave.ts` | The e2e covers a reload mid-attempt. Offline/retry has no unit test. |\n| Timer warnings at 5 and 1 min (aria-live) | `take/QuizPlayer.tsx` L286–329 | Verified by code inspection only. |\n| Analytics page chart | `analytics/QuizAnalytics.tsx` | The data is tested. The rendering is not. |\n| Seed (FR-36) | `prisma/seed.ts` L455–557 | The dev DB has no MATH-7A / ENG-7A courses, so the seed skips quizzes. Verified by code inspection, plus the dev's fixture run recorded in the dev log. |\n| 300-student load (NFR-2) | — | Not load-tested. qa-sh10 asserts the median of 50 concurrent saves is under 50 ms, and that saves are upserts. |\n","userModified":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01KGhskPL4qBEdNbcXJEUvsy","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"rule"}}]}
