by a specific test or file.\n- Every SH-11 test passes: the 21 unit and 14 integration tests Dev wrote (run against Postgres), my 11 new tests, and the 2 Playwright specs on a fresh production build.\n- Lint, typecheck and the production build are clean.\n- No banned UI libraries, no paid-tier grid features, and no `console.*` calls in the new code.\n\n**What fails**\n- The full suite is 399/409. One failure is new and caused by SH-11: `qa-sh9.test.ts` (the \"notified once\" test) now fails intermittently. It failed in the full run and in 1 of 3 runs on its own.\n- **Cause:** `publishOnce` in `assignments-service.ts` now marks the assignment as notified, then does the new gradebook update, and only then sends the notification. That extra step widens a timing gap the test trips over.\n- **Product risk:** if the gradebook update throws at that point, the notification is never sent, because the assignment is already marked as notified.\n- **Fix:** move the gradebook update to after the notification is sent, or catch and log its errors. It's a one-line move; I didn't change any product code.\n- The other 9 failures are in auth, attendance and toast tests, which SH-11 didn't touch. Most were already failing before SH-11; the rest pass when their files run alone, so they only fail under the parallel full run.\n\n**Tests I added**\n- `tests/integration/gradebook/qa-sh11.test.ts` (7 tests) checks that:\n  - the worked example gives 78.0% C+ in both the gradebook and the student view;\n  - synced grades only accept a comment;\n  - students and parents never see hidden items or unreturned scores;\n  - other teachers, students and parents are refused;\n  - grade changes and overrides write audit rows with old and new values;\n  - the grade-posted notification goes out once;\n  - category weights must total 100;\n  - items can only be marked missing after the due date;\n  - a gradebook of 35 students × 80 items loads in under 800 ms. Dev skipped this performance test.\n\n  It passed 3/3 runs and cleans up after itself.\n- `tests/unit/gradebook/validators.test.ts` (4 tests) covers the grading-scale band rules, weight sums, unique category names and the 1,000-character comment limit.\n\n**Things to know**\n- The current academic year in the dev database has no terms, so both Playwright specs crash during setup. I added a temporary term, ran them (both passed), and deleted it. Someone should add a real term or have the specs create their own.\n- Not verified by me:\n  - Report-card generation finishing in under 30 s for 600 students × 8 courses. I only confirmed the queries are batched; there's no timing test.\n  - The 7A part of the seed. There are no 7A courses in the dev database; Dev verified it on temporary data.\n  - Grading-scale create/edit/delete. I didn't run them because they would change the school's default scale in the shared database.\n\n`coverage-report.md` was written first and `qa-report.md` last; both are in `artifacts/qa/`. There's no coverage tool installed and I didn't add one, so the coverage figures are hand estimates: about 75–80% of the new server code and 35–40% of the UI code.","ttft_ms":1343,"type":"result","duration_ms":917021,"uuid":"c71ed9f9-01e6-4aa5-bb04-f2a6fdc2d17d","ttft_stream_ms":873,"time_to_request_ms":131,"first_content_frame_ms":873,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"model_usage_since_last_result":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":114,"outputTokens":41628,"cacheReadInputTokens":5382130,"cacheCreationInputTokens":138371,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":2.649695999999999,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":7801,"cacheCreationEphemeral5mInputTokens":122238,"cacheCreationEphemeral1hInputTokens":16133,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}}}
