{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgso8XiHuGNUkuKULBShK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"SH-13 QA is finished. The verdict is **PARTIAL**: 42 of 43 requirements pass and 1 fails, but the failure is not caused by SH-13.\n\n- **Functional requirements:** all 32 pass. Each one cites a file or test as evidence.\n- **Non-functional requirements:** 10 of 11 pass. NFR-10 fails because it requires the existing test suite to stay green, and it isn't: the full run is 505/510 and one file (`lockout.test.ts`) won't load. All six of those were already failing in the SH-11 report, and none of those test files import messaging code.\n- **SH-13 tests:** all 92 pass. That's Dev's 71 (which I re-ran) plus 21 new ones I wrote. The 92 includes the 2 Playwright tests, which I re-ran on a fresh dev server. Typecheck and lint are clean.\n- **Dev's work:** all 67 planned files exist and contain real code, with no stubs or `TODO`s. Without a signed-in session, every messaging API returns 401 and `/admin/safeguarding` redirects to login.\n\n**New test files:**\n- `tests/integration/messaging/qa-sh13.test.ts` (12 tests): recipient contact lists, co-teacher access, conversation list sorting and search, read/mute/archive/leave rules, unread count, `lastMessageAt`, loading older messages 30 at a time, quiet-hours settings, attachment access, and an empty poll returning in under 100 ms.\n- `tests/unit/messaging/composer-qa.test.tsx` (9 tests): Enter sends and Shift+Enter doesn't, the character counter, the \"can no longer send\" state, and the input validators.\n\n**Things worth a look (not blocking):**\n1. If a user record were ever hard-deleted, their messages would be deleted with it, which conflicts with the retention rule. Nothing in the app hard-deletes users today; they're archived.\n2. The sidebar unread badge counts muted conversations. The PRD doesn't say either way, so product should confirm.\n3. `canMessage()` is exported but never called.\n4. The student-page message buttons, roster \"Message selected students\", narrow-screen layout, safeguarding screens and quiet-hours section have no automated UI tests. I checked them by reading the code.\n5. I could only partly confirm the demo seed data: the dev database has no courses, so the three course-dependent threads were skipped by design. The \"Staff room\" thread and Alice as safeguarding lead are present.\n\nNo coverage tool is installed and I didn't add one, so the coverage report maps functions to tests by hand. It covers about 91% of the server functions (42 of 46). I changed no product code.\n\nFiles are in `artifacts/qa/`:\n- `qa-report.md`\n- `coverage-report.md`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":528,"cache_read_input_tokens":139074,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":528,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b2a19e14-003d-496b-9902-59b2c0434c99","uuid":"b413dea7-72cb-42e3-9f3c-c5876cceb82b","timestamp":"2026-11-09T18:04:40.264Z","request_id":"req_011Cgso8XTeqUpYUJGVyuYZm"}
