{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtNkjCChQMuFLFUP4fdX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The QA verdict for SH-14 is **FAIL**. Only 7 of the 27 planned tasks were built (TASK-1 to TASK-7). The calendar can't be used by anyone yet.\n\n**What's missing:** TASK-8 to TASK-27 have no code at all. That means:\n- no calendar service and no API routes\n- no `/calendar` or `/account/calendar` pages\n- no holiday handling in the timetable or attendance screens\n- no seed events\n- none of the planned integration or browser (Playwright) tests\n\n31 files that should have been created don't exist, and 14 existing files that should have been changed were left alone. None of the 8 acceptance criteria are met.\n\n**What was built works:** the new packages, database tables and migration, date helpers, input validation, repeating-event expansion, the calendar-file (iCal) generator, the audience lookup and the four `event.*` notification types. None of it is stub or placeholder code, and all of it passes its tests.\n\n| Check | Result |\n|---|---|\n| SH-14 tests | 64/64 pass (47 from Dev, 17 added by QA) |\n| Typecheck and lint | Clean |\n| Database migration | Applied |\n| Full test suite | Not fully green. The failures were already there before SH-14: three are on the SH-13 report's list, and two more pass when run on their own. None touch calendar code. |\n\n**Requirement results (49 total):**\n\n| Verdict | Count | Requirements |\n|---|---|---|\n| Pass | 5 | FR-1, FR-2, FR-3, NFR-6, NFR-11 |\n| Partly built (marked FAIL) | 12 | FR-4, FR-7, FR-15, FR-23, FR-26, FR-28, FR-29, NFR-3, NFR-5, NFR-8, NFR-9, NFR-10 |\n| Not implemented | 32 | everything else |\n\n**What I changed:**\n- **Fixed one of Dev's tests.** `tests/unit/calendar/ical.test.ts` expected the old, wrong escaping of `;`. The code is right; only the test's expected value changed. I changed no product code.\n- **Added `tests/integration/calendar/qa-sh14.test.ts`** (7 tests on the real database). It checks every audience type and the database constraints and cascades. It also checks that looking up \"who is in this audience\" and \"which audiences include me\" give the same answer.\n- **Added `tests/unit/calendar/qa-sh14.test.ts`** (10 edge-case tests). One of them confirms that holidays and term breaks don't default to \"no school\" yet (FR-5).\n\n**Next step:** re-run the Dev phase for TASK-8 to TASK-27, then run QA again. The finished foundation can be built on as it is.\n\nFiles are in `artifacts/qa/`:\n- `qa-report.md`\n- `coverage-report.md`"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5888,"cache_read_input_tokens":103912,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5888},"output_tokens":10,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d4f9b1f7-a7a6-4988-a1be-042973bf331a","uuid":"82c8b077-787f-4a8a-bdd7-a46769065cec","timestamp":"2026-11-10T01:25:37.349Z","request_id":"req_011CgtNkiyo5979NBWoeCtS1"}
